{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla","id":1486212,"title":"Do you think the Tremere will ever have competition in the Camarilla?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-11T04:56:48-07:00","id":1486212,"title":"Do you think the Tremere will ever have competition in the Camarilla?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\">IMHO the Tremere are unlikely to ever have true competitors when it comes to Blood Magic. Now sure there's Hacktivist Thaumaturgy if the Digital Draculas decide to rejoin the Camarilla, but even then their biggest advantage is going to be that they possess knowledge of the Path of Technomancy, something that the Tremere also have. Now don't get me wrong, Hacktivist Thaumaturgy has amazing rituals, but there's very few of them and are practically useless without some sort of wifi connected device. Now compared to the many extremely useful rituals of Thaumaturgy, and the fact that most of them don't require a wifi connection, you begin to understand why the Tremere are a pillar of the Camarilla.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It's the same issue with all the other Blood Magic Traditions; many of the rituals are good for what they were made for, but very few are going to be seen as useful to the Camarilla. And although the Tremere are seen as untrustworthy, do you really think the Camarilla is going to trust a vampire who comes from the Followers of Set, Tzimisce, or Assamites? </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The FoS are definitely going to try corrupting you</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, the Tzimisce have a clan culture of torture, and t</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">here was a reason the Assamites were cursed by the Tremere in the first place.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So what do you think?</span><br /> <br /> Edit: Referring to V20","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-11-2022, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T06:18:43-07:00","id":1486218,"title":"","content":"It's worth remembering that in V5, the Tremere's Pyramid was shattered, with Vienna bombed and many of their ruling elders slaughtered. Whereas before the Tremere were one organization, now there's a lot more rivalry and jockying for position. So suddenly the Tremere are finding themselves in competition with other Tremere in a way that wasn't the case a couple of decades ago.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Banu Haqim have joined the Camarilla, and they have a long history of blood sorcerers including an entire caste of blood sorcerers. Also, many Lasombra have also joined the Camarilla and would have likely brought their knowledge of Abyss Mysticism with them. Abyss Mysticism is pretty niche, but it still offers new magical options that the Tremere don't necessarily have immediate answers too.<br /> <br /> And then on top of all of that, the Hecata have swelled up into being their own major faction by bringing in members from a half-dozen different bloodlines (though you're definitely going to see the Hecata fracture at some point). While they're an independent clan, you'll likely find members of the Hecata in most Camarilla cities and they bring powerful blood magic of their own.<br /> <br /> So the Tremere are still the primary blood sorcerers of the Camarilla, but they suddenly have a lot of competitors and their Pyramid was cracked and nearly collapsed. Two decades ago, if a vampire in the Camarilla found herself needing to hire the services of a blood mage, her only choice would really be a Tremere. Assamites, Lasombra Antitribu and Giovanni/Samedi were all fairly rare. Now suddenly that same vampire has options. The Tremere don't have a monopoly on the Camarilla's blood magic like they used to, and they've been fractured anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-11-2022, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T06:28:10-07:00","id":1486219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486218#post1486218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth remembering that in V5, the Tremere's Pyramid was shattered, with Vienna bombed and many of their ruling elders slaughtered. Whereas before the Tremere were one organization, now there's a lot more rivalry and jockying for position. So suddenly the Tremere are finding themselves in competition with other Tremere in a way that wasn't the case a couple of decades ago.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the Banu Haqim have joined the Camarilla, and they have a long history of blood sorcerers including an entire caste of blood sorcerers. Also, many Lasombra have also joined the Camarilla and would have likely brought their knowledge of Abyss Mysticism with them. Abyss Mysticism is pretty niche, but it still offers new magical options that the Tremere don't necessarily have immediate answers too. And then on top of all of that, the Hecata have swelled up into being their own major faction by bringing in members from a half-dozen different bloodlines. While they're an independent clan, you're likely going to be able to find members of the Hecata in most Camarilla cities and they bring powerful blood magic of their own.<br /> <br /> So the Tremere are still the primary blood sorcerers of the Camarilla, but they suddenly have a lot of competitors and their Pyramid was cracked and nearly collapsed. Two decades ago, if a vampire in the Camarilla found herself needing to hire the services of a blood mage, her only choice would really be a Tremere. Assamites, Lasombra Antitribu and Giovanni/Samedi were all fairly rare. Now suddenly that same vampire has options. The Tremere don't have a monopoly on the Camarilla's blood magic like they used to, and they've been fractured anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>You beat me to it. In V5, there's loads of competition for the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T08:45:00-07:00","id":1486230,"title":"","content":"Even without V5 it is worth mentioning that the Tremere monopoly of Blood Magic in the Camarilla has nothing to do with trust and even less with the power and variety of their magic, even because most people in the Cam can't really tap into their clan-wide variety, only in the few Paths practiced in their city.<br /> <br /> The Tremere had a monopoly because they bargained it and that's that. Most practitioners of Blood Magic never had any interest in selling their services, or would only do so in very particular cases. The Tremere put a price table on the door. They look for clients and actively offer their services. While for others magic is a secondary aspect of clan culture and a tool for the clan's goals, for the Tremere the goal is to develop magic and the means is to get patronage by selling it.<br /> <br /> And finally, they keep others outside of the trade just by bullying and business malpractice. They actively go after the competition while they're weak and the Tremere are necessary. If a Follower or Koldun starts to sell magic to the Prince of a city, the Tremere from a dozen cities will fall on them to find any way whatsoever to destroy the newcomer's reputation, mark them as a criminal and kill with prejudice or capture for interrogation and then as research subject.<br /> <br /> You can bet the Camarilla will grab any opportunity to be rid of this monopoly that is good to the Pyramid, not to the sect. But they're very adamant about staying the only game in town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T14:16:29-07:00","id":1486238,"title":"","content":"When the game was first published, the Tremere were supposed to have a complete monopoly on any kind of blood magic. Too bad for you, other six clans, you'll never have blood magic and need to go to the Tremere! Of course, the game starting add all these other vampires who also knew some form of blood magic. The Sabbat had the Tremere anti-tribu, and some of the Sabbat Paths seem to implied that non-Tremere AT knew them. Then we had more Paths known to the Tal'mahe'ra. Infernalists had Dark Thaumaturgy. And soon more Paths started appearing for this clan or that clan. Within five years, the idea that the Tremere had a monopoly was simply idiotic, and this got worse in Revised. Every faction or clan seemed to have some version of it EXCEPT for the other six Camarilla clans.<br /> <br /> I find that silly. The other six clans not having blood magic was an artifact of a time when it was intended for only the Tremere to know it, and that go thrown out the window. IMHO, keeping that while saying everyone else can have access to blood magic is silly.<br /> <br /> This is how I handle it in my chronicles.<br /> <br /> First, some ancient paths of blood magic pre-date the Tremere and are out there. These Paths are known. People can learn them provided they find the resources or mentors who can do so. I prefer to keep these Paths as those that people popularly assume vampires can do anyway. So these open Paths are Movement of Mind, Weather Control, Lure of Flames, Spirit , and Elemental Mastery. Are these common? No, not at all, though Movement of Mind is the best known of all of these. Finding mentors is difficult. And while these aren't Tremere secrets that the Tremere actively suppress, they do what they can to discourage this knowledge from spreading. The Kindred who know any of them are usually elders who know one or two Paths, and they might teachit to someone else in exchange for very useful boons. Movement of Mind though is known well enough that even some Anarchs might know it (I think vampires flying in the night sky is a popular enough trope it has to be simulated somehow). When the Tremere choose to teach non-Tremere some Thaumaturgy in return for services, it is one of these Paths they teach (like how Nicolai is teaching Gordon Keaton in 1e CbN) as these aren't Tremere secrets and already known. Rituals aren't openly known though.<br /> <br /> Second, there are secret societies within the Camarilla of individuals who know blood magic and actively develop it and recruit new members. There aren't many of them, and they don't have many members. If you combined all of them, their numbers fall for short of the Tremere. But their members include the other six Camarilla clans. The Kindred here often know many or all of the Paths listed above as well as a few more Paths I consider fairly typical like Neptune's Might or Conjuration. These vampires also know various Rituals as well. These aren't dabblers, but actual &quot;magicians&quot; like the Tremere. The Tremere views these as rivals and do what they can to undermine them. They can't replace the Tremere as a source of magic for the sect, and they are absent in most domains. But there's enough of them so that the sect is not entirely dependent on the Tremere.<br /> <br /> However, I also make sure that there are plenty of Tremere-only Paths (Path of Blood obviously), and sometimes even make certain Paths proprietary only to certain chantries or factions within the Tremere. I want to make being part of the Tremere special for those players who want to play them and like that they have some toys not available to others, and to make internal Tremere politics important if they want to learn a lot of Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T15:45:58-07:00","id":1486241,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think the Banu Haqim will be their rivals.<br /> <br /> But the greatest rivals the Tremere will have will always be other Tremere.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T17:27:18-07:00","id":1486245,"title":"","content":"Genrally I tend to just consider the tremere are the best at blood magic. I think this this still holds in v5 were the assamites and lasombra are more about the Marshall applications and the hecata are independent plus oblivion drives you nuts anyway. The koldun's and setites sorcerors are out for smokes this ed so that leaves the tremere still sitting top dog culturally.<br /> <br /> If anything their appeal is up now because you're only dealing with one guy and his local friends and not the might of the pyramid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-11-2022, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T19:21:44-07:00","id":1486249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla#post1486212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Edit: Referring to V20</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, a fellow connoisseur. <br /> <br /> As of V20, Al Ashrad and the Schismatics, of which a large population are Sorcerers, are in the process of joining the Camarilla. I do not believe they would present the united front that the Tremere does, if for no other reason than the structure of magic they both practice (Hermetic magic tends towards formulas and thus towards group academic study, while Persian and Babylonian magic is far less structured and intuitive, and thus lends itself towards a master and apprentice relationship). Still, having two Sorcerers who keep to themselves in the same city as, say, seven or eight Tremere (they've always been a Clan with a lower representation), they'd fare quite well. Certainly, the Tremere would think twice about blacklisting non Tremere rivals, for fear of driving them into the arms of the Assamites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:10:14-07:00","id":1486253,"title":"","content":"-OP is obviously talking about v20 to the deliberate exclusion obvious of v5 elements<br /> - &quot;But V5!&quot;<br /> <br /> To answer the OP<br /> I don't consider the Assamite sorcerers to be numerous enough to be a real threat, and with the precarious position of assamites they will almost certainly make local deals with Tremere. <br /> I don't think Tremere can keep their monopoly in the information age, but I don't think other vampires can really compete with them as service providers. Others might devaulue low level rituals but the high level stuff will likely remain the domain of Tremere. <br /> <br /> There might be some inovation that forces Tremere to diseminate some degree of thaumaturgy, like common heat seeking cameras forcing everyone to learn Domino of life or that level 2 power that causes tech to fail. But practice won't bring you from level 2 to level 3, only knowledge will, so I consider that a safe step for the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:39:08-07:00","id":1486258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486253#post1486253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Tremere can keep their monopoly in the information age, but I don't think other vampires can really compete with them as service providers. Others might devaulue low level rituals but the high level stuff will likely remain the domain of Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically that.<br /> <br /> The Tremere build their entire system, culture and niche to be service providers for the Camarilla. Even if beating them at magic was possible, beating them at business is another thing entirely. I don't even know if someone would want to, but even if they did, would be an uphill battle to even be considered serious competition.<br /> <br /> Now, be it by V5 lore or just V20 in the Information Age (and <i>Rites of the Blood</i> makes it pretty clear that there's no complete monopoly anymore, in a way that makes sense), minor competition is still enough to drive prices down for some services. Even high level rituals, I would say, because you don't have to compete with the whole catalog to present something.<br /> <br /> In the end, though, for those willing to spend good money on it, nothing beats the Tremere ability and disposition to contact the right magician for any task.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T22:52:36-07:00","id":1486259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486253#post1486253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-OP is obviously talking about v20 to the deliberate exclusion obvious of v5 elements<br /> - &quot;But V5!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A reminder the Banu Haqim joined the Camarilla in Revised.<br /> <br /> 4th Edition was metaplotess until BJD, though, so they acted like the Banu Haqim didn't.<br /> <br /> But they've been members of the Camarilla for 20 years.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T23:35:45-07:00","id":1486261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486259#post1486259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A reminder the Banu Haqim joined the Camarilla in Revised.<br /> <br /> 4th Edition was metaplotess until BJD, though, so they acted like the Banu Haqim didn't.<br /> <br /> But they've been members of the Camarilla for 20 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot that!<br /> <br /> Usually I play with the idea that they mostly stayed with the Ashirra, which wouldn't join with the Camarilla until V5, but indeed they've been officially a part of the Camarilla since the Schism, and that has already more than 20 years.<br /> <br /> Not only that, the newcomers included mainly Viziers and Sorcerers, and those are considered in lore to be in high demand in the Cam as an alternative to dealing with the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-11T23:39:49-07:00","id":1486262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486259#post1486259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blah</div> </div> </div> </div>First: On what scale? Vampires are slow moving things that take time. Nobody would've gone &quot;Oh look, the Assamites are in the Camarilla, time for Wroclaw to open up and get it's mandatory schismatics&quot; IE even after 100 years it's still pretty reasonable to not have Assamites in your city. <br /> <br /> Second: Using V20 and ignoring revised metaplot is perfectly legit. That's the Beauty of V20 in that it's more metaplot agnostic than not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T09:12:30-07:00","id":1486284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486262#post1486262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: On what scale? Vampires are slow moving things that take time. Nobody would've gone &quot;Oh look, the Assamites are in the Camarilla, time for Wroclaw to open up and get it's mandatory schismatics&quot; IE even after 100 years it's still pretty reasonable to not have Assamites in your city.<br /> <br /> Second: Using V20 and ignoring revised metaplot is perfectly legit. That's the Beauty of V20 in that it's more metaplot agnostic than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 - The scale of desperation. The Banu Haqim fled the Alamut and a lot of them pledged themselves to the Camarilla. They came in numbers and that's it. Regardless of any particular city, they're a Camarilla presence.<br /> <br /> 2 - It's pretty reasonable to not have any particular clan in your city for any reason whatsoever, so what? The population of <b>a</b> city does not define what is a Camarilla clan or not, or sect wide policies or options.<br /> <br /> 3 - Camarilla law demanded acceptance of every vampire regardless even before the schism. They didn't got a Justicar or Inner Council member, just presence, which has always been fair play for any clan or bloodline, no rule or policy changed in broad terms.<br /> <br /> 4 - Again, the lore specifies that the arrival of the Sorcerers was welcomed by many because it breaks Tremere monopoly.<br /> <br /> 5 - Wasn't the OP question about the Tremere having competition or not? When people brought V5 up you were quick to point out that the OP wasn't talking V5 (and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27313_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27313\" data-vbnamecard=\"27313\">Hello</a> was also quick to edit and write it), now you're moving goal posts to use V20 as a defense to not have to use the schism?<br /> <br /> Stop it you two. We can all see this is veiled edition warring, but it's starting to become too obvious to let pass. You're both free to use whatever you want of the metaplot and to express your opinion on it, but that was not the question and V5 has nothing to do with it. The official lore does not need to stop anyone from thinking it is silly, but as far as the setting goes it is still the official lore. It is valid to post what the setting itself has to say regardless of edition.<br /> <br /> You don't even think it is silly to have competition on the matter, you said so yourself, MWIS. Why the fuck are you so adamant about attacking this plot instead of just say you don't use it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T09:33:16-07:00","id":1486286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486284#post1486284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop it you two. We can all see this is veiled edition warring, but it's starting to become too obvious to let pass. You're both free to use whatever you want of the metaplot and to express your opinion on it, but that was not the question and V5 has nothing to do with it. The official lore does not need to stop anyone from thinking it is silly, but as far as the setting goes it is still the official lore. It is valid to post what the setting itself has to say regardless of edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont know if you referring to me, but just to make it clear I was expecting people to know I was referring to V20 since the tzimisce and FoS no longer have access to blood magic in V5.<br /> <br /> Edit: ill make sure to specify the edition next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-12-2022, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T10:50:23-07:00","id":1486291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486286#post1486286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont know if you referring to me, but just to make it clear I was expecting people to know I was referring to V20 since the tzimisce and FoS no longer have access to blood magic in V5.<br /> <br /> Edit: ill make sure to specify the edition next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifying the edition when you're looking into a very specific context is generally a good idea.<br /> <br /> But at the same time, the question in this thread does not depend on edition. Even if you particularly don't see it applying to V5, you would just be alienating players of that edition for no reason.<br /> <br /> Give context, but do not ground the thread too much on an edition, do not alienate people just to try to lock a thread in a single edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T10:58:38-07:00","id":1486292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486262#post1486262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First: On what scale? Vampires are slow moving things that take time. Nobody would've gone &quot;Oh look, the Assamites are in the Camarilla, time for Wroclaw to open up and get it's mandatory schismatics&quot; IE even after 100 years it's still pretty reasonable to not have Assamites in your city.<br /> <br /> Second: Using V20 and ignoring revised metaplot is perfectly legit. That's the Beauty of V20 in that it's more metaplot agnostic than not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Third: V20 ALSO had the Assamites join the Camarilla in Beckett's Jyhad Diary and was part of OPP's plan for THEIR 5th Edition--but it still happened in V20.<br /> <br /> So the Assamites as part of the Camarilla is not a V5 thing.<br /> <br /> It is a thing that is of classic and OPP V:TM.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486286#post1486286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dont know if you referring to me, but just to make it clear I was expecting people to know I was referring to V20 since the tzimisce and FoS no longer have access to blood magic in V5.<br /> <br /> Edit: ill make sure to specify the edition next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't? I thought both Clans did. After all, The Blood Cults book shows that Blood Cults have access to huge amounts of Blood Sorcery like the Cults of Mithras and Church of Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-12-2022, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:03:18-07:00","id":1486293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486292#post1486292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Third: V20 ALSO had the Assamites join the Camarilla in Beckett's Jyhad Diary and was part of OPP's plan for THEIR 5th Edition--but it still happened in V20.<br /> <br /> So the Assamites as part of the Camarilla is not a V5 thing.<br /> <br /> It is a thing that is of classic and OPP V:TM.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They don't? I thought both Clans did. After all, The Blood Cults book shows that Blood Cults have access to huge amounts of Blood Sorcery like the Cults of Mithras and Church of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thi Tzimisce still have koldunic sorcery and FoS still have akhu?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:07:50-07:00","id":1486295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486293#post1486293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tzimisce still have koldunic sorcery and FoS still have akhu?</div> </div> </div> </div>They haven't been written up but they haven't been stated to have lost them either.<br /> <br /> The Lure of Flames was basically revised in The Blood Cults as rituals standing in for Paths and one-use per memorization.<br /> <br /> OPP basically did the lion's share of the work of adapting Classic WOD magic to Blood Sorcery as best they can.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, &quot;No, there's no rules for them but no one said they don't have Koldunic sorcery or Path of Corruption anymore.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T11:36:15-07:00","id":1486300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486293#post1486293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thi Tzimisce still have koldunic sorcery and FoS still have akhu?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't need to exist as distinct Disciplines in the rules to exist in the lore, hadn't been retconned and have always been OoC either way. As far as anyone can tell, until further notice they're still going as in previous canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T22:01:12-07:00","id":1486322,"title":"","content":"Alright, let me explain this again, slower maybe. <br /> <br /> 1 Ur-Shulgi waking up is a revised event but it is an OPTION in V20<br /> 2 Even if Assamites get in on the inner circle, MOST cities aren't going to welcome a load of assamites because:<br /> a- They already consider themselves overpopulated and there's few things unclaimed for the Assamites to take. <br /> b- fears of secret loyalists and religious zealots among schismatics still cause quite a lot of trouble. <br /> c- prejudice against a clan of diablerists. It should be said that the caste system is pretty strong and inviting a bunch of &quot;warriors&quot; into your peaceful city is a recipe for destabilization. <br /> d- lobbying from powerful tremere. You think you're going to beat the Tremere monopoly by inviting an Assamite Sorcerer in? Too simple! Too Naive! That monopoly has plenty of favours to call in and they can often change who's prince. Why piss off the entrenched, mighty devil you know for small unknown ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-12T23:23:42-07:00","id":1486325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486322#post1486322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, let me explain this again, slower maybe.<br /> <br /> 1 Ur-Shulgi waking up is a revised event but it is an OPTION in V20<br /> 2 Even if Assamites get in on the inner circle, MOST cities aren't going to welcome a load of assamites because:<br /> a- They already consider themselves overpopulated and there's few things unclaimed for the Assamites to take.<br /> b- fears of secret loyalists and religious zealots among schismatics still cause quite a lot of trouble.<br /> c- prejudice against a clan of diablerists. It should be said that the caste system is pretty strong and inviting a bunch of &quot;warriors&quot; into your peaceful city is a recipe for destabilization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except V20's Assamite Defection isn't about Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> If you pay attention to the events of BJD, the Assamites join the Camarilla not because of Ur-Shulgi, though he's certainly probably there but because of the Web of Knives being a hideous fundamentalist cult that is tearing through the ranks of the moderate and liberal (if such a thing exists) in the Banu Haqim's Vizier as well as Sorcerer castes. There's a lot of opposition, particularly from the Camarilla's Tremere, but the fact is that the Camarilla still accepts them and any Prince who doesn't accept them is going to have to be made an example of. The Camarilla needs the Banu Haqim because while the Brujah and Gangrel are still present in V20, they are still people find themselves under attack from a wide variety of threats.<br /> <br /> If it's truly going to be a global power source, they need a global Clan.<br /> <br /> And yes, if you're one of those ignorant Cainites who thinks the Banu Haqim is a bunch of murderous Warrior Caste, well, there's uses for those guys too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> d- lobbying from powerful tremere. You think you're going to beat the Tremere monopoly by inviting an Assamite Sorcerer in? Too simple! Too Naive! That monopoly has plenty of favours to call in and they can often change who's prince. Why piss off the entrenched, mighty devil you know for small unknown ? </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'd hope the Tremere would be smarter than this. It is, after all, the best chance to learn their own new branches of sorcery as well as turn longstanding enemies into allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T03:04:43-07:00","id":1486330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486325#post1486325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but the fact is that the Camarilla still accepts them and any Prince who doesn't accept them is going to have to be made an example of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Source required. Really. This is an aggravating statement. The Camarilla can't and doesn't function like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, if you're one of those ignorant Cainites who thinks the Banu Haqim is a bunch of murderous Warrior Caste, well, there's uses for those guys too. </div> </div> </div>Destabilizing a good city? Introducing diablerie and &quot;second city&quot; nonsense to corrupt the youth? Weakening the clans already in place by giving them competition or forcing territorial concessions from them? Pacifying elders and Anarchs with thoughts of the prince launching overzealous cannibal psychopaths at them?<br /> <br /> Bestowing the title of sherriff onto a member of the dreaded assamite clan is possibly the fastest way to ensure a revolt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I'd hope the Tremere would be smarter than this. It is, after all, the best chance to learn their own new branches of sorcery as well as turn longstanding enemies into allies. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://youtu.be/WO23WBji_Z0?t=14\" target=\"_blank\">I'm sure they can have a civil and productive discussion that will be mutually beneficial</a>.<br /> <br /> It'd be smarter for the Tremere to wheel any sorcerer into the nearest chantry and blood bond them into submission. Quick, direct, efficient, maximum gain, minimal loses. Convert any paths and rituals the Sorcerer has to superior thaumaturgy, get a load of credit, then kill the source when it's outlived it's purpose. The Tremere aren't going to benefit from learning ancient, backwards ways of doing things. The Assamites aren't going to forgive the Tremere for a thousand year curse overnight, and the Schismatics aren't going to be happy with the lousy job done that caused the loyalists to go hog-wild. The notoriously proud assamite sorcerers aren't going to be happy to play second-fiddle to Tremere. Everyone's already suspicious of the Assamites, it's easy enough to frame them.<br /> <br /> This is the World of Darkness not the world of Sunshine and Thornless roses. I'm sure engineers from Lockheed-Martin and AVIC could have great discourses on the finer points of creating military aviation craft but that doesn't mean they're going to start having open and fair dialogues now, is it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T05:43:48-07:00","id":1486334,"title":"","content":"In case it's not clear to you:<br /> In V20, the Camarilla have won, the Tremere have <i>won</i>. The Assamites have imploded, split down the middle, with one half a monstrous parody of the clan destined to unite everyone against it and the other half a desperate, disunited diaspora with a considerable amount of well-earned prejudice directed towards them. Politically speaking, The Assamites are a toxic dumpster fire spewing radioactive waste. Why should the Tremere of V20, well established in their localities, deign to treat newcomer Assamite Sorcerers as equals? Vampires are politically minded creatures, and the only individuals who would choose to patron the in-trouble sorcerers rather than the centuries-established warlocks are those who've already burned their bridges with the clan. In most Domains the Warlocks have accumulated significant prestation and clout, no other clan is quite so good as creating debt as the Tremere, and for all their faults, their position is predictably stable in most domains (barring the cruel whims of omnipotent writers) Meanwhile the Assamites might end up dead tomorrow when a loyalist comes around and cleans them up or when they run afoul of the law. If you like to take risks from an investment standpoint, you might benefit greatly from getting into debt with an assamite and then loosing that debt when the Assamite dies, as such has a considerable likelyhood given the situation, but from a &quot;long term strategy because you're a vampire- standpoint the Tremere are just a better deal and it's not worth humouring a sorcerer if it'll piss off the warlocks. The Assamites are risk incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-13-2022, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T17:06:25-07:00","id":1486377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486334#post1486334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In case it's not clear to you:</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love our disagreements, I should mention that this is settled as the Camarilla accepted the Assamites in classic WOD. They did NOT react like you claim in either V20 or VR.<br /> <br /> But there's nothing wrong with complaining about plotlines you don't like.<br /> <br /> Moving on, my thoughts on how things will change with the Assamites as rivals of the Tremere:<br /> <br /> <b>How the Assamites and Tremere will get along</b><br /> <br /> 1. I feel the Assamite Sorcerer caste will not attempt to overtly engage the Tremere because they're not people are automatically looking for a fight. They will, however, do their best to make alliances if the Tremere move against THEM, though.<br /> <br /> 2. I see the Tremere Council of Seven initially planning to undermine the Assamite defectors before doing a 180 because I see Ur-Shulgi likely ordering an attack on Vienna or sending a massive curse their way. I doubt it will end up 5th Editioning them but it should at least remind the Tremere that the Schismatic Assamites are their ALLIES against Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> 3. I don't see a Renassiance of Blood Magic with the Banu Haqim joining the Camarilla because the Banu Haqim are going to be every bit as secretly and picky about their Blood Magic as the Tremere.<br /> <br /> 4. Blood Magic will become much more available as a tool, though, because the Banu Haqim will be dedicated to doing their best to making as many friends as well as doing as many favors as possible to get people in their pocket.<br /> <br /> 5. REVISED will be an easier time for the Banu Haqim because the Thin Bloods, Gehenna Fears, Week of Nightmares, Gangrel leaving, and Sabbat invasion of the East Coast will all weaken the Camarilla enough to make the Banu Haqim an easier sell.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-13-2022, 09:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T22:14:25-07:00","id":1486387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486377#post1486377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I love our disagreements, I should mention that this is settled as the Camarilla accepted the Assamites in classic WOD. They did NOT react like you claim in either V20 or VR.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and I'm sure when the United States government finally got rid of slavery and declared all men equal the people took to it with ease and race relationships were repaired within a few years so that blacks and whites lived side by side in harmony and no... hold on that didn't fucking happen did it? Alright, when the United Nations had an arbitration and told China that the islands it really wants don't belong to it the Chinese respected the ruling and.... no, that didn't happen either. When Adam Smith wrote his ground breaking book on Capitalism all the aristocracy of the time took it to heart and agreed that landlords are parasites and taxes should be on land rather than income... oh, nobody did that and even to this day the number of ruling bodies that prefer land to income tax is basically limited to a city state or two... Hmm. Next up: the Holy Roman emperor had control over Germany and the other leaders didn't cause internal problems... oh.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is an agreement, not a master. There are more terrifying elders and methuselah outside the inner circle than within. The Inner circle does not have the ability, nor the will, to try and police 4000+ cities and however many towns there might be on petty issues like assamite acceptance. The Camarilla doesn't need the Assamites in V20, the Schismatics need the Camarilla.<br /> (also find that source, will you?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-14-2022, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T00:54:15-07:00","id":1486393,"title":"","content":"To summarize so far: I agree with Black Fox's observation that the Tremere's near-monopoly on blood sorcery within the Camarilla was an idea that developed over the years, with ancients from across the spectrum of clans having some utility with it in early editions and the Tremere just having a focus and a method that made them the best at it in the modern nights.<br /> <br /> With that, Revised takes Thaumaturgy's status as the go-to method for a Kindred out to create new powers and shunts that downstream to the Thinbloods in order to make them interesting. <br /> <br /> The Assamite wizard diaspora makes overtures to join the Camarilla because they're fleeing Ur-Shulgi in Revised. They do the same in V20 with the Web of Knives swapped in as a replacement for Ur-Shulgi in the name of metaplot agnosticism, but there's plenty of wiggle room for the Web of Knives to just be Ur-Shulgi's enforcers if the story you're making with V20's toolkit uses him.<br /> <br /> The net result of the Banu Haqim sorcerors joining the Camarilla is definitely to create competition for the Tremere, in either edition. And yes, the Tremere would predictably have an opinion about competition for their niche and trash talk the newcomers from a variety of predictable angles.<br /> <br /> Personally, I find it hard to picture the Prince of a city being excited about the number of blood sorcerers growing in their domain, regardless of clan background. They're a necessary evil to have on one's side because otherwise they'll be on someone else's side, but the ocean of blood that goes into research and rituals makes any chantry or wizard cult a gigantic Masquerade breach waiting to happen - but then I'm not a big fan of blood sorcery for a number of reasons, and realize that I bring my own bias to the topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-14-2022, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T01:39:04-07:00","id":1486395,"title":"","content":"Its probably worth noting the carmarilla assamites are majority vizier, sorcerors are minority as I recall. Even if their are assamites in a city theirs no guarantee they have a sorceror much less one of competitive level.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of introducing Heceta cappadicians into the carmarilla in my setting, I suspect that would have a simular effect to the assamite presence with the mortis arts. Effectively tremere are still the best by a mile but dont have monopoly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-14-2022, 04:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T08:12:42-07:00","id":1486419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486387#post1486387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla is an agreement, not a master. There are more terrifying elders and methuselah outside the inner circle than within. The Inner circle does not have the ability, nor the will, to try and police 4000+ cities and however many towns there might be on petty issues like assamite acceptance. The Camarilla doesn't need the Assamites in V20, the Schismatics need the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla is an agreement, but part of the agreement is that Princes generally go along with what the Camarilla says and in exchange the Camarilla supports the Prince. If the Prince decides to flatly go against the Camarilla, then the Camarilla will withdraw its support for the Prince. <br /> <br /> So if the Camarilla declares that Assamites are now equal members of the Camarilla and need to be given the same respect that other Camarilla clans have, any Prince who refuses and engages in the persecution of Assamites is going to lose the Camarilla's support. The Camarilla will will throw its weight behind a new Prince. They won't offer any support the Prince in the event of attacks from the Sabbat. They might even clandestinely help the local Anarchs out in an effort to overthrow the Prince (&quot;Go along with this and we'll make sure one of you guys becomes the new Prince.&quot;) Sure, super strong Princes like Mithras can tell the Camarilla to go fuck itself, but most Princes aren't going to have that much power. And you'll have a few Princes who end up being overthrown and killed, and they'll serve as an example so most of the rest who don't want Assamites in their territory will go along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T08:15:51-07:00","id":1486420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486395#post1486395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm thinking of introducing Heceta cappadicians into the carmarilla in my setting, I suspect that would have a simular effect to the assamite presence with the mortis arts. Effectively tremere are still the best by a mile but dont have monopoly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata are already poised for a pretty massive split once the truth about Lazarus' goals start getting out to the rest of the faction, so it wouldn't be hard to have refugees end up fleeing en masse to the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T09:52:55-07:00","id":1486435,"title":"","content":"My view is that Justicars don't exist for dealing with &quot;citizens&quot; of the Camarilla. The Sheriffs and even Archons exist to deal with the vast majority of trouble makers, Anarchs, and even die-hard revolutionaries. No, Justicars exist to dispose of renegade Princes, Redlisters, and ancient powerful things.<br /> <br /> A Camarilla Prince refuses to let Assamites in? He may or may not need to be made an example of. Which probably would include simply walking into the Primogen and saying, &quot;He's no longer Prince.&quot; Maybe with his ashes in a sack.<br /> <br /> The PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES game is actually really good because an Archon attempts this with a 1000 or so year old vampire and it becomes an actual war as she doesn't have the juice of a Justicar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:46:35-07:00","id":1486445,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don\u2019t like the Banu Haqim / Assamites joining the Camarilla. Of course, when someone asks a question on an RPG forum, they are typically interested in canonical answers, not personal opinions or house rules. In Revised and V5, Assamites join the Camarilla. Which means that the Tremere monopoly on magic has already been broken, especially in V5 where Blood Sorcery is a Clan Discipline for them. If I were doing V5, like MWIS, I wouldn\u2019t have the Assamites as a Camarilla Clan, but that is a tangent.<br /> <br /> Actually, the monopoly really started to be broken in Revised when there was a huge proliferation in blood magic. Every non-Camarilla Clan got its own form of blood magic, which always struck me as silly. Now, those were non-Camarilla Clans, but making blood magic so common certainly undermined the idea that the Tremere had strict control over blood magic. <br /> <br /> Now that thin blooded vampires have a form of blood magic and the Tremere are no longer unified, and so be more likely to sell or trade away their secrets, there is even less of a Tremere grip over magic. Also, blood sorcery does a lot less than it used to, so monopolizing it isn\u2019t quite as special as it used to be anyway. <br /> <br /> So, I\u2019d say for all practical purposes, the Tremere\u2019s Camarilla monopoly on blood magic is largely gone, even if they are still the resident experts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:01:52-07:00","id":1486446,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=AnubisXy;n1486419]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So if the Camarilla declares that Assamites are now equal members of the Camarilla and need to be given the same respect that other Camarilla clans have, any Prince who refuses and engages in the persecution of Assamites is going to lose the Camarilla's support. </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla doesn't support princes. The princes support the Camarilla. The overwhelming majority of regions would function fine without the Camarilla label.<br /> <br /> Also like, do you actually believe the Inner circle would be wholly supportive of the move? It's not one King Vampire, it's a whole little friendship group who hate eachother's guts; It's politics. Also, I don't really know why this seems to elude people but there's plenty of ways you can create racist policies without actually calling out a specific race.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla will will throw its weight behind a new Prince. </div> </div> </div>Weight is localized. If I control Berlin, you're not going to be able to do much to me in Berlin and you're going not going to do much from Frankfurt either. Hell, the prince of Frankfurt would probably prefer to side with me for &quot;prince rights&quot; rather than help some petty Camarilla stooge.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They won't offer any support the Prince in the event of attacks from the Sabbat. They might even clandestinely help the local Anarchs out in an effort to overthrow the Prince (&quot;Go along with this and we'll make sure one of you guys becomes the new Prince.&quot;) Sure, super strong Princes like Mithras can tell the Camarilla to go fuck itself, but most Princes aren't going to have that much </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat, pre-5, are pretty rare outside the Americas, and Anarch movements have always been a fringe novelty in the better-run cities of the old-world. Even if we do discuss the Americas, and all the nonsensical metaplot it's been plagued with, the Camarilla really doesn't do much to help local Princes fight Sabbat/Anarchs. When the local police department looks like the military, you don't need the actual military (unless you're dealing with a school shooter, police can't help with that).<br /> <br /> That, and realistically speaking, if you're a prince who's predictably going up against Sabbat and anarchs on a regular basis, you're probably actually keen on getting Assamites on your side. But if you're not in such a situation, you don't need Assamites, you don't want Assamites, and the Cam really doesn't have you in a possition where they can do much about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you'll have a few Princes who end up being overthrown and killed, and they'll serve as an example so most of the rest who don't want Assamites in their territory will go along with it. </div> </div> </div> So, after hundreds of years of surviving nasty plots, the inner circle are stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-14-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:35:59-07:00","id":1486453,"title":"","content":"I don't think letting the Assamites in has to be an all or nothing situation where either the Tremere have to suck it up, or the Assamites aren't going to be part of the sect<br /> <br /> I don't think a Tremere Prince has to give much explanation of why the Assamites were rejected, Princes have the right of granting or denying Domain, after all. But the camarilla is big, there are cities where there's no Tremere, or Tremere are very weak, or have strong frenemies that would love to see them lose power. I think precisely because the sect isn't a monolith, it mkes sense for the Assamites to be accepted in. Sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T16:24:59-07:00","id":1486473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486435#post1486435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is that Justicars don't exist for dealing with &amp;quot;citizens&amp;quot; of the Camarilla. The Sheriffs and even Archons exist to deal with the vast majority of trouble makers, Anarchs, and even die-hard revolutionaries. No, Justicars exist to dispose of renegade Princes, Redlisters, and ancient powerful things.<br /> <br /> A Camarilla Prince refuses to let Assamites in? He may or may not need to be made an example of. Which probably would include simply walking into the Primogen and saying, &amp;quot;He's no longer Prince.&amp;quot; Maybe with his ashes in a sack.<br /> <br /> The PARLIAMENT OF KNIVES game is actually really good because an Archon attempts this with a 1000 or so year old vampire and it becomes an actual war as she doesn't have the juice of a Justicar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahaha no, it doesnt work like that. If the Inner Circle decided to simply kill princes to force them to accept something IN THEIR DOMAINS, you can be sure that the princes of the world would unite EN MASSE and declare a Blood Hunt on the Inner Circle.<br /> <br /> No, it doesnt work like that. Some Princes will be taking in assamite refugees, and they'll have their reasons for doing it - in particular:<br /> - Princes hard pressed by a Tremere Primogen<br /> - Princes ruling over cities with no or few weak Tremere, and that sees benefits on integrating a bunch of sorcerors and assassins<br /> - and Princes wishing to accumulate favors with a group of desperate cainites that would therefore be loyal to their benefactor.<br /> <br /> In cities where the prince is a Tremere it's a big no no, but also in cities where the prince is on good stand with the Tremere primogen or that the prince regularly uses the Tremere services, that's also gonna be a big no no.<br /> <br /> And one more thing, the Princes are WITHIN THEIR RIGHTS to refuse anyone in their domains - that's one of the most basic of the Camarilla laws.<br /> <br /> If the Inner Circle tries to disregard that, they'll face a mass revolt and the Camarilla ends. And remember, revolts by the aristocracy are always worse than revolts of the peasants.<br /> <br /> This is simply not how the Camarilla works.<br /> <br /> So again, some cities will have Assamites - and those will probably be quickly turned into &quot;praetorian guards&quot; of the princes that accept them, but just as many cities will have nor accept none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T16:37:02-07:00","id":1486474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486446#post1486446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Camarilla doesn't support princes. The princes support the Camarilla. The overwhelming majority of regions would function fine without the Camarilla label.<br /> <br /> Also like, do you actually believe the Inner circle would be wholly supportive of the move? It's not one King Vampire, it's a whole little friendship group who hate eachother's guts; It's politics. Also, I don't really know why this seems to elude people but there's plenty of ways you can create racist policies without actually calling out a specific race.<br /> <br /> <br /> Weight is localized. If I control Berlin, you're not going to be able to do much to me in Berlin and you're going not going to do much from Frankfurt either. Hell, the prince of Frankfurt would probably prefer to side with me for &quot;prince rights&quot; rather than help some petty Camarilla stooge.<br /> <br /> The Sabbat, pre-5, are pretty rare outside the Americas, and Anarch movements have always been a fringe novelty in the better-run cities of the old-world. Even if we do discuss the Americas, and all the nonsensical metaplot it's been plagued with, the Camarilla really doesn't do much to help local Princes fight Sabbat/Anarchs. When the local police department looks like the military, you don't need the actual military (unless you're dealing with a school shooter, police can't help with that).<br /> <br /> That, and realistically speaking, if you're a prince who's predictably going up against Sabbat and anarchs on a regular basis, you're probably actually keen on getting Assamites on your side. But if you're not in such a situation, you don't need Assamites, you don't want Assamites, and the Cam really doesn't have you in a possition where they can do much about it.<br /> <br /> So, after hundreds of years of surviving nasty plots, the inner circle are stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Im fully behind on you on that one.<br /> <br /> I dont know why people believe that the Inner Circle can just casually send a Justicar to whatever, burn a Prince at the stake for whatever reason and it's all cool... Particularly doing that in order to impose BREAKING THE LAW OF DOMAIN, one of the 6 basic laws of the sect.<br /> <br /> And yes, I agree with you, for cities having massive problems with Sabbath and Anarchists, the &quot;entreperneurial&quot; prince would be smart to enlist several Assamites, who in turn will have to be fiercely loyal to their &quot;benefactor&quot; (for no other reason that no one else will have them). This means that those Assamites will be seen more and more at the frontlines of the war - which may actually, in time, earn them the prestige they require to be gradually accepted in the sect.<br /> <br /> But hey, no prince is forced to accept ANYONE within their domains. If a Prince decrees &quot;Brujahs go out&quot;, than out they go... The consequences are an entirely other thing.<br /> <br /> For the Justicars to actively hunt down a Prince it has to be something truly massive, and said Prince will have practically incurred the wrath of all his neighbors already before a move is finally agreed upon. The Inner Circle dont just go willy nilly stacking Princes left and right just because they want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T17:01:10-07:00","id":1486477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486473#post1486473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hahaha no, it doesnt work like that. If the Inner Circle decided to simply kill princes to force them to accept something IN THEIR DOMAINS, you can be sure that the princes of the world would unite EN MASSE and declare a Blood Hunt on the Inner Circle.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, after every Prince in the world is dead, which should take about a week, what happens next? I assume the Justicars appoint new Princes. It's not like a Prince will have ANY support in a suicidal charge against the organization that guarantees all of their fortunes and won't be devoured by their own childer at the opportunity to replace their bosses.<br /> <br /> The power of the Camarilla does not rest with the Princes. It rests with the Inner Council and the mutual consent of most Cainites who know they need SOMEONE to internationally protect the Masquerade.The Princes are a convenience that are SO UNIMPORTANT that virtually every city can determine their own Prince with the Camarilla not caring about their murders or assassinations as long as the next Prince proceeds to keep the money flowing up. Their authority derives from the Camarilla's stamp of approval and Justicars can and easily remove them at will.<br /> <br /> A Prince's power is limited by the approval of:<br /> <br /> * The Primogen<br /> * The Elders<br /> * The Inner Circle<br /> * The Justicars<br /> * The Archons<br /> <br /> When a Justicar says jump, the only thing a Prince can say in response is &quot;How high?&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm also confused at this idea of Prince solidarity. There IS an organization that all of the Princes rely upon to dictate to them and smack down anyone who has a problem and that's the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> But if you think I'm making stuff up, I point to Gustav Breidenstein as the go-to example of a completely incompetant and defiant Prince who got smacked down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know why people believe that the Inner Circle can just casually send a Justicar to whatever, burn a Prince at the stake for whatever reason and it's all cool... Particularly doing that in order to impose BREAKING THE LAW OF DOMAIN, one of the 6 basic laws of the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're invoking the Tradition that presentation is accepted. The Camarilla says all vampires are members of the Camarilla and subject to its laws. The Assamite Schismatics by accepting the authority of the Camarilla are no longer outlaws of independents. The Traditions include that you are supposed to accept vampires who agree to your laws into your domain, barring they are outlaws.<br /> <br /> But pulling back a moment, I note I'm curious why people think this, &quot;All or nothing&quot; thing would happen in the first place. Why do people think the Inner Council would accept Assamites but every Prince everywhere will have absolutely no desire to please the Inner Council, curry favor with them, gain new allies, or simply NOT CARE about a new Clan joining that people mostly know only rumors about?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm sure there's Princes who would reject them but would they be anything close to a majority and something they would draw a line in the sand over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-14-2022, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T18:52:43-07:00","id":1486482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486446#post1486446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla doesn't support princes. The princes support the Camarilla. The overwhelming majority of regions would function fine without the Camarilla label.<br /> <br /> Also like, do you actually believe the Inner circle would be wholly supportive of the move? It's not one King Vampire, it's a whole little friendship group who hate eachother's guts; It's politics. Also, I don't really know why this seems to elude people but there's plenty of ways you can create racist policies without actually calling out a specific race.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean V20 and Revised said that a significant chunk of the Assamites were joining the Camarilla. We can argue about whether it's a wise move or not, but it occurred. In Revised/V20, with the loss of the Gangrel, the awakening of Ravnos, the rise of the Sabbat and the invasion of the Wan Kuei, it made sense that the Inner Circle would be willing to accept Assamite refugees. The Camarilla is not in a great position and there's a whole host of problems on the very near horizon and they're going to need as many allies as possible. <br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the relationship between the Princes and the Camarilla is something of a two-way street. Obviously the Camarilla provides quite a bit of support to local Princes. Any city that flagrantly disregards the Camarilla and begins issuing bloodhunts against members of the Camarilla or refusing to allow members of the Camarilla into their cities, simply because those Camarilla members are part of the Clan the Prince doesn't like, is going to find itself in a very, very bad situation.<br /> <br /> I don't know that the Camarilla would straight up send assassins to kill the Prince, but the Camarilla would very likely support a new Prince, one that is willing to accept all members of the Camarilla, and you'd see the domain pushed into a civil war between the old Prince and the Camarilla's new Prince. Vampires who choose to stand against the Camarilla may run into problems with their accumulated prestation going away, with Camarilla backed hackers locking up their money, etc. For the regular vampires in the Domain of a Prince that has decided to stand against the Camarilla, they're probably going to find their nightly existence heavily impacted by that decision and are more likely to support a new Prince who agrees to play ball with the Camarilla.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T19:10:45-07:00","id":1486484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486477#post1486477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, after every Prince in the world is dead, which should take about a week, what happens next? I assume the Justicars appoint new Princes. It's not like a Prince will have ANY support in a suicidal charge against the organization that guarantees all of their fortunes and won't be devoured by their own childer at the opportunity to replace their bosses.<br /> <br /> The power of the Camarilla does not rest with the Princes. It rests with the Inner Council and the mutual consent of most Cainites who know they need SOMEONE to internationally protect the Masquerade.The Princes are a convenience that are SO UNIMPORTANT that virtually every city can determine their own Prince with the Camarilla not caring about their murders or assassinations as long as the next Prince proceeds to keep the money flowing up. Their authority derives from the Camarilla's stamp of approval and Justicars can and easily remove them at will.<br /> <br /> A Prince's power is limited by the approval of:<br /> <br /> * The Primogen<br /> * The Elders<br /> * The Inner Circle<br /> * The Justicars<br /> * The Archons<br /> <br /> When a Justicar says jump, the only thing a Prince can say in response is &amp;quot;How high?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I'm also confused at this idea of Prince solidarity. There IS an organization that all of the Princes rely upon to dictate to them and smack down anyone who has a problem and that's the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> But if you think I'm making stuff up, I point to Gustav Breidenstein as the go-to example of a completely incompetant and defiant Prince who got smacked down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because they're invoking the Tradition that presentation is accepted. The Camarilla says all vampires are members of the Camarilla and subject to its laws. The Assamite Schismatics by accepting the authority of the Camarilla are no longer outlaws of independents. The Traditions include that you are supposed to accept vampires who agree to your laws into your domain, barring they are outlaws.<br /> <br /> But pulling back a moment, I note I'm curious why people think this, &amp;quot;All or nothing&amp;quot; thing would happen in the first place. Why do people think the Inner Council would accept Assamites but every Prince everywhere will have absolutely no desire to please the Inner Council, curry favor with them, gain new allies, or simply NOT CARE about a new Clan joining that people mostly know only rumors about?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm sure there's Princes who would reject them but would they be anything close to a majority and something they would draw a line in the sand over?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gustav is ironically the same example that I was about to use - but at the very other opposite end of the argument. He actually sent the Tremere Justicar back humiliated with a stake, and didnt kill him simply because he wanted to send a message - dont mess with my domain. Because he was fully within his power to actually kill the Tremere Justicar. And what did the Camarilla do face to that provocation? Nothing. They let it go in the hopes that time would &quot;solve the issue&quot;.<br /> <br /> And that's what happened actually, his fall was NOT due to the Camarilla's higher ups intervention, but actually due to his own insane megalomania that led to countless revolts and eventually his own court turning into him.<br /> <br /> The reason why the Camarilla &quot;lets&quot; each city &quot;choose&quot; their own Princes is exactly because the Inner Circle dont have the power to impose its will. What, you dont think the Camarilla cares enough about who will be the one giving the most important jobs on the most important cities of the world? &quot;Let the cainites of Paris, Berlin, London and NY choose who will organize the Camarilla's local affairs; those cities are unimportant and those are matters of little significance&quot;. Please.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle CAN NOT choose who will be the Prince of Paris or London, that's why they &quot;allow&quot; the locals &quot;self governance&quot; - which means they got no way of interfering. It's not because they dont care, it's because they CANT.<br /> <br /> On one thing I do agree with you thou, no man - or vampire - rules alone. So, I do agree that they need the approval of the Primogen. That's a fact.<br /> <br /> Oh, and just guess who would succed a Prince that has been &quot;retired&quot; under your assumption of the &quot;seven vampire kings&quot; of the Inner Circle?<br /> <br /> Oh yes, that's right, a member of the Primogen. You know, one of the elders that just saw the law of Domain being smashed by some pretentious Justicar. Just how long do you calculate those successors would start plotting the downfall of the Inner Circle and the murder of the Justicars and Archons? Specially since that they now know that either they kill the Camarilla's higher ups or are killed by them?<br /> <br /> Also, about the Tradition of Presentation, that has NOTHING to do with FORCING Kindred into other's Kindred territory. Quite the opposite actually, this tradition serves to reinforce the tradition of the domain - when a vampire enters another domain, he/she is expected to present himself, EXACTLY because a cainite's domain is sacred.<br /> <br /> The host however is under NO obligation to receive the guest, and can dismiss the visitor - giving them time to live his domains unharmed, in case the vampires in question managed to successfully present themselves.<br /> <br /> In fact, many Princes order their Sheriffs to forcefully drag any unkown vampire to the Prince, and some even have green light to outright murder anyone unkown within the city!<br /> <br /> Again, the Camarilla as a Sect can accept whoemver they will, but that doesnt mean individual Princes need to give lodging space to all Camarilla vampires that wishes to set in their cities.<br /> <br /> And no, the Inner Circle aint all powerful and dominant within the Camarilla. The Inner Circle coordinate things, but the truth is that they oversee a lose alliance of what is essentially a bunch of &quot;independant city-states&quot;. What the Inner Circle and Justicars do is play high politics; if there's a Prince they dont like, they'll work to undermine him inside of his domains - because if he's strong within his &quot;feud&quot;, there's actually nothing the Camarilla can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T19:33:25-07:00","id":1486485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486477#post1486477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But pulling back a moment, I note I'm curious why people think this, &amp;quot;All or nothing&amp;quot; thing would happen in the first place. Why do people think the Inner Council would accept Assamites but every Prince everywhere will have absolutely no desire to please the Inner Council, curry favor with them, gain new allies, or simply NOT CARE about a new Clan joining that people mostly know only rumors about?<br /> <br /> Yeah, I'm sure there's Princes who would reject them but would they be anything close to a majority and something they would draw a line in the sand over?</div> </div> </div> </div>On that point, I said it already, this wouldnt be an all or nothing proposition. Yes, there would be princes that would just simply outright deny passage to any of the Assamites - and that would've been fine, because they are both within their rights to do so and because there's nothing really that the Inner Circle can do about it (even if did wanted to intervene in that matter, which I dont think they would), and their reasons to do so are their own - ties with Tremere, stable cities that would have nothing to gain from it but possibly a lot to lose, etc.<br /> <br /> Besides, that would be a non-issue to the inner circle because just as many prince that there would be wanting to halt any assamite presence, there would be many welcoming them with open arms. For example, Princes that dont have a very strong grip over their Primogen would love to accept a bunch of powerful and skilled sorcerous or assassins and warriors to serve as his praetorian guard, and being that those newcomers would be completely at such Prince's mercy, they would have to fully throw their lots with their ruler. This could be a MASSIVE boon for such princes - and in fact, it could actually become a major stabilization factor in cities with weaker Princes or with strong Primogens.<br /> <br /> And, the Assamites would also be welcomed and be a boon for cities at the &quot;frontlines&quot; of the conflicts with the Sabbath and Anarchists; in those they would also be welcomed.<br /> <br /> So no, the Inner Circle wouldnt care that some - even MANY princes would exercize their rights over their domains, because just as many others would be welcoming them with open arms. In fact, the Inner Circle would probably even PREFER it to be so, since they know that for some cities, the addition of a bunch of Assamites would bring destabilization and problems, so I fully expect the Inner Circle to expect many Princes to reject them - and that would be absolutely according to plan.<br /> <br /> This would also mean that the Assamites would be diverted to where they will be both needed and where they'll have a positive impact rather than causing problems and disturbances - war zones and unstable zones, meaning that with a single stroke, cities that are more unstable and unsafe will become safer and more orderly (since stronger princes do bring more stability) and cities that are already stable and safe will remain so.<br /> <br /> So no, there will be no Justicars &quot;turning Princes into ashes&quot; over such a non issue. In fact, the Inner Circle will incentivize the Princes to decide on their own (as if they had the power to do otherwise to begin with), because just shoveling Assamites anywhere and everywhere without any considerations of context would be incredibly stupid and counterproductive.<br /> <br /> So again, the &quot;problem&quot; will solve itself up, and will even be done in the most efficient way possible. I just pitty the Assamites because they'll be shoveled into praetorian guards and cannon folder duties, having to become really exposed, at least initially until they manage to settle down within the sect. But hey, that's the price they'll have to pay for being under the Camarilla's umbrella.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T19:56:52-07:00","id":1486488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486482#post1486482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean V20 and Revised said that a significant chunk of the Assamites were joining the Camarilla. We can argue about whether it's a wise move or not, but it occurred. In Revised/V20, with the loss of the Gangrel, the awakening of Ravnos, the rise of the Sabbat and the invasion of the Wan Kuei, it made sense that the Inner Circle would be willing to accept Assamite refugees. The Camarilla is not in a great position and there's a whole host of problems on the very near horizon and they're going to need as many allies as possible. <br /> <br /> Also, I believe that the relationship between the Princes and the Camarilla is something of a two-way street. Obviously the Camarilla provides quite a bit of support to local Princes. Any city that flagrantly disregards the Camarilla and begins issuing bloodhunts against members of the Camarilla or refusing to allow members of the Camarilla into their cities, simply because those Camarilla members are part of the Clan the Prince doesn't like, is going to find itself in a very, very bad situation.<br /> <br /> I don't know that the Camarilla would straight up send assassins to kill the Prince, but the Camarilla would very likely support a new Prince, one that is willing to accept all members of the Camarilla, and you'd see the domain pushed into a civil war between the old Prince and the Camarilla's new Prince. Vampires who choose to stand against the Camarilla may run into problems with their accumulated prestation going away, with Camarilla backed hackers locking up their money, etc. For the regular vampires in the Domain of a Prince that has decided to stand against the Camarilla, they're probably going to find their nightly existence heavily impacted by that decision and are more likely to support a new Prince who agrees to play ball with the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said above, this is a non issue. A prince that refuses Assamites in his city will probably be doing the Camarilla a favor, rather than &quot;defying&quot; it.<br /> <br /> First of all, a Prince that refuses someone or even worse, some entire clan, just out of prejudice, is a total idiot, and I would very much like to know what kind of mystery surrounds such an imbecile to become a prince in the first place.<br /> <br /> Secondly, for a Prince to want to deny the Assamites passage, he would have to be considering the opinion of his subjects, particularly his court. If such a prince KNOWS that this would be nothing but problem to his city, because he knows his primogen, he knows his ancillae harpies and he knows his neonates, why would he invite trouble to a domain that up to that point was stable?<br /> <br /> Also, why would the Camarilla and the Inner Circle want to cause generalized chaos upon cities that up to that point were relatively stable?<br /> <br /> First of all, that would be stupid for the Inner Circle to do, since it would cause massive problems on many cities;<br /> <br /> And Secondly it's completely unnecessary, since the Assamites would actually bring a good deal of safety and stability to many other cities that lacked those and that would welcome them with open (more or less) arms.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Princes / Inner Circle relation cuts both ways.<br /> <br /> But that means exactly that: it cuts both ways.<br /> <br /> It's not a good idea for any Prince to simply break the mask and declare blood hunts on the Justicars; but such insanely extreme case would be just that, an improbable extreme case. And such an idiotic prince would surely fall, but because of his own stupidity, not because the Inner Circle didnt like his funny face.<br /> <br /> On the other hand thou, if the Justicars started to go insane and willy nilly turn Princes into ashes just because, the Camarilla would be over because every Prince would effectively change their title to &quot;Barons&quot; and the Justicars wouldnt be long for this Earth.<br /> <br /> So, to sum it up: the powers of Princes, Justicars and Inner Circle is a fragile balance of political power. And the members of the Inner Circle arent stupid to just simply blow it all up just to behave as spoiled children wanting to have it their way. It's all a big massive political game that they play; they are not vampiric kings of their clans.<br /> <br /> Just think about the apex of feudalism. Yes, there was even a king, but should such a king overplay his authority and overstep his boundaries, the lords would dethrone him in no time.<br /> <br /> And the Camarilla also doesnt need to play like that. There are several levels of cooperation and &quot;tolerable backstabbing&quot; that allows it to be functional. And in fact, being largely descentralized is actually one of the reasons why the Camarilla has been so successful; if there was a bunch of &quot;olygarch kings&quot; trying to micromanage everything, the sect would've fallen to the Sabbath a long time ago","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T20:51:38-07:00","id":1486489,"title":"","content":"That Camarilla isn't going to condone Princes tossing out or denying access to members of a Camarilla clan, simply because they're part of a clan the Prince doesn't like.<br /> <br /> Look no further than the Malkavians. I imagine most Princes would love to toss those guys out of their cities, but they can't. Any attempt to do so results in a massive number of Malkavians taking matters into their own hands, showing up en mass in a domain where they're denied to press the issue. And the Camarilla <i>really</i> doesn't want that to happen because having so many Lunatics running around is just begging for multiple Masquerade breaches. So the Camarilla would prefer to simply not see an issue get to that point in the first place.<br /> <br /> Plus there's the understanding that if the Camarilla condones or supports Princes denying access to Clans like that, then you'll inevitably see Ventrue Princes denying access to Brujah in their domains, Brujah Princes denying access to Venture, Princes denying access to Tremere, or Nosferatu or whoever because of their own personal issues. And then those Clans will take matters into their own hands to get access to the cities, the same way Malkavians do. That's going to end up causing chaos and so it's not in the best interest of the Camarilla to condone or support or allow that sort of behavior.<br /> <br /> So it only makes sense that when Princes begin rejecting the ability for clans to get access to their domains, then the Camarilla will begin taking action to push the Prince into playing ball. Again though, the reality is that some Princes are simply too powerful for the Camarilla to do much about. All they can do is register a complaint and then leave it to individual Clans to solve the issue (though if a given Prince is powerful enough, even that won't happen). On the other hand, weaker Princes can be forced into accepting it via various threats and whatnot.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla won't simply send in a Justicar to kill the Prince, but there are a lot of other ways that the Camarilla can force a reluctant, weaker Prince into compliance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T23:11:07-07:00","id":1486498,"title":"","content":"Even if the Assamites are fully accepted into the Camarilla, the prince still has the right to refuse entry to Assamites. The most sacred laws of the Camarilla are the Traditions and the 5th Tradition is Hospitality. This gives the prince total control over who enters his city, a vampire must have the prince\u2019s permission to enter. If the Inner Circle forces a prince to accept Assamites, then they have essentially declared the 5th Tradition null and void, which is one of the primary laws which grants a prince power. It would seriously destabilize the Camarilla and cause resentment from not only the princes, but numerous movers and shakers in the Camarilla who value the Traditions or the dynamics they create. <br /> <br /> it would be far wiser and more in keeping with the nature of the Camarilla to use political pressure or intrigues against a prince who doesn\u2019t want to play ball with the Inner Circle\u2019s agenda. Also keeping in mind that the Inner Circle doesn\u2019t necessarily want all the Princes to gladly welcome the Assamites and that it might play into the hands of any number of powerful vampires (including Inner Circle members or their allies) to have an anti-assamite prince and pro-assamite factions at odds which each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T01:16:28-07:00","id":1486503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486445#post1486445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the monopoly really started to be broken in Revised when there was a huge proliferation in blood magic. Every non-Camarilla Clan got its own form of blood magic, which always struck me as silly. Now, those were non-Camarilla Clans, but making blood magic so common certainly undermined the idea that the Tremere had strict control over blood magic.<br /> <br /> Now that thin blooded vampires have a form of blood magic and the Tremere are no longer unified, and so be more likely to sell or trade away their secrets, there is even less of a Tremere grip over magic. Also, blood sorcery does a lot less than it used to, so monopolizing it isn\u2019t quite as special as it used to be anyway.<br /> <br /> So, I\u2019d say for all practical purposes, the Tremere\u2019s Camarilla monopoly on blood magic is largely gone, even if they are still the resident experts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't personally think it silly because it is weird to think that vampire had been around for thousands of years working behind the scenes, and magic only came with a self-made clan with barely 1 thousand years. If it were unique to their blood, that could fly, but as long as it can be practiced by any vampire with the knowledge, this is really strange.<br /> <br /> There was also a certain movement to introduce some access to Blood Magic to the other Cam clans without making new Disciplines out of it. <i>Revised</i> already had a number of NPCs with Thaumaturgy without their magic being of Tremere origin, including Creteus being a Ventrue Blood Magician at least a thousand years before the Tremere.<br /> <br /> V20 retconned Cret to have him practicing Dur-An-Ki, but it also added the notion that lesser Blood Magic traditions using Thau rules are a thing and had existed since always, with every clan having scattered practitioners, no exceptions, sealing any pretense to the clan Tremere having a complete monopoly.<br /> <br /> And I do think there <b>is</b> a reason to invest in Blood Magic. It has never been about intensity, but about variety. A Magician add access to options you didn't had before and your opponents aren't likely to expect, they add novel tools to the arsenal of a ruler more than to the personal abilities of the Magician (who's just trading other things for magical development).<br /> <br /> What the Tremere really bring to the table, though, is how effectively they explore Magic as Service and Magic as Clan Identity. There may well be dozens of Elder magicians and a sorcerer group on every clan, it simply isn't the same. A Magician with no greater support has personal power, but can only offer their personal knowledge to vampire society, if they even want to, which they probably don't. And a group within a clan has the clan to serve first, even if they're a big part of it (the Banu Haqim going Cam are mostly Viziers, but the number of Sorcerers <b>is</b> high, the less represented caste is the Warriors). The Tremere has the entire clan geared towards being a provider of magical services, with any Chantry being prepared to put the local ruler in contact with the wider organization if the Chantry can't provide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486446#post1486446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Qualquer coisa</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you already made you <b><i>personal opinion on this unrelated tangent</i></b> very clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486453#post1486453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think letting the Assamites in has to be an all or nothing situation where either the Tremere have to suck it up, or the Assamites aren't going to be part of the sect<br /> <br /> I don't think a Tremere Prince has to give much explanation of why the Assamites were rejected, Princes have the right of granting or denying Domain, after all. But the camarilla is big, there are cities where there's no Tremere, or Tremere are very weak, or have strong frenemies that would love to see them lose power. I think precisely because the sect isn't a monolith, it mkes sense for the Assamites to be accepted in. Sometimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Tremere Prince could even accept them and still make sure that they simply can't be a threat to Tremere power.<br /> <br /> I think that's more likely because the Tremere still want to learn the secrets of Dur-An-Ki, while being the power in town would basically let them steel the Domain against a significant change in who's able to provide magical services to non-Tremere. They're more likely to want to bar Banu Haqim entrance the lower their own power and presence is, because then they really face a threat to whatever power they hold.<br /> <br /> Probably the most likely reason for a Domain to hinder or forbid Banu Haqim settling in would be just racism. Which no one denied to be a thing that many Domains would have, just that it is very different from sect-wide policy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486473#post1486473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is simply not how the Camarilla works.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla can and has ousted Princes in the past several times, openly or not.<br /> <br /> When someone says this would happen, it doesn't mean the Camarilla will issue a sect-wide statement of policy and send Justicars and Archons as thugs to enforce policy, no one is proposing this nonsense (well, ok, sometimes CTPhipps proposes something close, but not exactly that).<br /> <br /> Instead, it is the idea that if this is considered in the best interest of the sect, all things considered (which means <b>all</b> things considered and not only the things you're thinking I'm thinking considered), then the Inner Circle would pull their strings to convince as many Princes as possible, and wayward Princes would be dealt with as befits the problem they're causing. Some would be left alone because they weight nothing on the larger issue, or the cost would be too high, indeed. Others would disappear. Some would be ousted for whatever other reason got out to the wind, by the hand of a Justicar, a rival or just popular uprising (popular uprising with many generous benefactors). Only one or two would be openly ousted by the sect as extreme hardliners whom obviously no one else on good standing agrees with.<br /> <br /> And the fact that it was deemed to be in the best interest of the sect is proven simply by the fact that it happened. This is fiction. A lot of nuance and details can realistically weight in the question, but the complexity of it simply means the author is free to give any answer, since the author ultimately decides those details as they come up. It is worth noting that being open to all Kindred <b>is</b> official Camarilla policy, and one of the few that is heavily implied in the books to be followed almost always to the letter.<br /> <br /> See how the Camarilla deals with the Ravnos. When they come to a city and present themselves, they get <i>at least</i> the standard time of hospitality given to traveling vampires. And if they're not given residency, most Princes will <b>not</b> be blatant about the reason even if everyone knows the reason. Most Princes will do their best to watch and wait for the Ravnos to give them a reason to be expelled or destroyed, many will look for any reasonable excuse to shorten the Ravnos staying as much as possible, and/or pressure the Ravnos through direct or indirect means into making a blunder.<br /> <br /> But the books are very clear that just blatantly denying Ravnos because they're Ravnos isn't usually an option, and they're the apex of clan racism in the setting. Nor is being of a Sabbat clan considered grounds for overt denial unless you're proven Sabbat yourself. Why would things go different with the Banu Haqim when people actually doesn't expect them to screw you for no reason like they expect from the Ravnos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T04:56:02-07:00","id":1486509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486482#post1486482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean V20 and Revised said that a significant chunk of the Assamites were joining the Camarilla. We can argue about whether it's a wise move or not, but it occurred. In Revised/V20, with the loss of the Gangrel, the awakening of Ravnos, the rise of the Sabbat and the invasion of the Wan Kuei, it made sense that the Inner Circle would be willing to accept Assamite refugees.</div> </div> </div> </div>On an individual city by city basis? It makes sense. But on a sect wide level? it makes sense to a degree but that's based on a few assumptions:<br /> - there are few Assamites because the schismatics have largely been purged. Also, the Assamites weren't really a big clan in the first place.<br /> -The Wan Kuei are serious about their invasion and will invade more and invade larger areas (unlikely)<br /> -The Gangrel are never coming back (It's rediculous they left, as I've argued in other threads) (also note that the Gangrel were never really a big presence in the Camarilla)<br /> <br /> <b>If the Cam really wants more members, it hurts them less to just embrace a few more neonates rather than have foreigners join them</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I believe that the relationship between the Princes and the Camarilla is something of a two-way street. Obviously the Camarilla provides quite a bit of support to local Princes. Any city that flagrantly disregards the Camarilla and begins issuing bloodhunts against members of the Camarilla or refusing to allow members of the Camarilla into their cities, simply because those Camarilla members are part of the Clan the Prince doesn't like, is going to find itself in a very, very bad situation. </div> </div> </div>How does the Camarilla support princes? Because IMO the leadership of the city is doing 90% of the work and all outsiders like the cam can do is throw in a few titles to make people sound more legitimate+ catch heinous intercity criminals+ support purges of tricky Gehenna cults (which a prince can usually do himself, it's just a little harder<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know that the Camarilla would straight up send assassins to kill the Prince, but the Camarilla would very likely support a new Prince, one that is willing to accept all members of the Camarilla, and you'd see the domain pushed into a civil war between the old Prince and the Camarilla's new Prince. . </div> </div> </div>How? If the costs of war outweigh the benefits of going to war, don't go to war. <b>A civil war caused by the sect shows the failure of the sect</b>. And again, for all the power of the Camarilla, it's not logistically feasible to use that power to target domains that dissent on policies that you don't really care about all that much. You don't need 5+ in your Intelligence + Politics pool to really see how fucking absurd and stupid it is for the Camarilla to war with itself as it pushes for inclusivity towards one of the most feared clans there is now that the assamite political situation has taken a fucking nosedive. Take advantage of the sitation? Sure, but eliminate prejudice and force princes to allow assamites no matter the thoughts of the prince or his residents? Do you think vampires vote for the fucking Greens or something?<br /> <br /> as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> pointed out, The Traditions are sacred. The prince interprets the traditions as sees fit. The Camarilla is an organization that wholeheartedly supports the traditions. Other than dealing with dangerous destabilizing Gehenna cults, it's really not in their interest to directly go against a tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-15-2022, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T06:38:31-07:00","id":1486513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486509#post1486509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How? If the costs of war outweigh the benefits of going to war, don't go to war. <b>A civil war caused by the sect shows the failure of the sect</b>. And again, for all the power of the Camarilla, it's not logistically feasible to use that power to target domains that dissent on policies that you don't really care about all that much. You don't need 5+ in your Intelligence + Politics pool to really see how fucking absurd and stupid it is for the Camarilla to war with itself as it pushes for inclusivity towards one of the most feared clans there is now that the assamite political situation has taken a fucking nosedive. Take advantage of the sitation? Sure, but eliminate prejudice and force princes to allow assamites no matter the thoughts of the prince or his residents? Do you think vampires vote for the fucking Greens or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Prince decides to ban all Malkavians from his domain, that's going to piss the Malkavians off. And it's very likely that they're going to show up in that Prince's domain and start taking matters into their own hands to force the Prince into accept them. This is very likely going to cause all sorts of Masquerade breaches and other issues all of which are bad for the Camarilla. So the Camarilla has one of two choices - either they stand with the Prince and tell the Malkavians to go fuck themselves, or they side with the Malkavians and tell the Prince he needs to allow the Malkavians into his city.<br /> <br /> Trying to wash their hands of the matter and saying &quot;You guys deal with it&quot; isn't going to work because the Camarilla will be left holding the back and dealing with the fallout and Masquerade breaches that will inevitably result from that sort of conflict. And note that this is true for pretty much any Prince who bans any clan (a Ventrue banning Brujah from his city or a Tremere Prince banning Nosferatu).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is ultimately an organization created by the clans for the clans. This is the benefit to your clan having official recognition and sanction from the Camarilla. There are individual vampires, such as Tzimsci, or Ravnos, or Samedi who are part of the Camarilla and travel between Camarilla cities, but they don't have the backing or sanction, as a clan, from the organization. If a Prince tells one to leave his city, there's not much they can do about it and no one they can complain to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486509#post1486509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1129_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1129\" data-vbnamecard=\"1129\">Sergeant Brother</a> pointed out, The Traditions are sacred. The prince interprets the traditions as sees fit. The Camarilla is an organization that wholeheartedly supports the traditions. Other than dealing with dangerous destabilizing Gehenna cults, it's really not in their interest to directly go against a tradition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, it <i>is</i> in the Camarilla's interest to prevent vampire clans from coming to blows with asshole Princes just because the Prince wants to be an asshole to other respected members of the Camarilla, whether by negotiating or figuring out some sort of deal. And in the event that a Prince proves to be so absolutely recalcitrant that he refuses to listen to any sort of reason or negotiate or budge from his position and the Camarilla has to deal with the fallout for an extended period of time, then eventually the Camarilla is going to start considering what steps could be taken to replace that Prince with someone more reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T08:17:33-07:00","id":1486523,"title":"","content":"This thread has taken some... diversions, shall we say?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I always assume everyone in VTM is scheming against everyone else. If a Justicar comes for the city's Prince, some people will be outraged, but the rest will be figuring out how to either avoid the same fate or how to twist this to their own advantage. The Primogen are the most likely to benefit from this, since one of them is most likely to wind up being Prince.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if the Prince of a neighbouring domain is ousted, it might be time to expand your own rule or send in your puppet. Rebellion is for Anarchs, and those guys are suckers. The Camarilla is the Camarilla because they're the vamps who rejected freedom for safety and comfort (and lots of hiding in shadows).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is run by elders who pretend the even older elders don't exist. Even if they knew the Ancients personally, or are their childer. They're quite happy to bury their heads in the sand to keep the power they have. <br /> <br /> They also have no qualms breaking rules, so long as they aren't found out. The Inner Circle aren't best mates; they're just enemies who get more benefit from working together occasionally, and secretly doing their own thing the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim joining will cause jealousy, hatred and suspicion, but that's Kindred society in a nutshell. We have to remember that the Tremere experimented on Nosferatu and Gangrel right up until the formation of the Camarilla, and the Camarilla didn't immediately implode when they were all forced to play nice.<br /> <br /> It took the Gangrel nearly 500 years to leave this toxic relationship. And even then, many of them stayed out of habit and convenience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T08:54:17-07:00","id":1486524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486503#post1486503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla can and has ousted Princes in the past several times, openly or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, on a case by case situation. Those princes are usually trouble makers who are bringing instability to their domains to begin with. Some would end up ousted no matter what by their own courts, subjects or neighbors.<br /> <br /> The Inner Circle dont just go nilly willy burning Princes left and right just for a silly look; this is a cartoonish depiction of the Camarilla<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486503#post1486503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When someone says this would happen, it doesn't mean the Camarilla will issue a sect-wide statement of policy and send Justicars and Archons as thugs to enforce policy, no one is proposing this nonsense (well, ok, sometimes CTPhipps proposes something close, but not exactly that).</div> </div> </div> </div>If no one was proposing this, I wouldnt be talking. CTPhipps, Ramses and a few others were suggesting EXACTLY that, even stating that Princes who simply decided to uphold one of the most sacred traditions of the Camarilla would be turned to ashes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486503#post1486503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, it is the idea that if this is considered in the best interest of the sect, all things considered (which means all things considered and not only the things you're thinking I'm thinking considered), then the Inner Circle would pull their strings to convince as many Princes as possible, and wayward Princes would be dealt with as befits the problem they're causing. Some would be left alone because they weight nothing on the larger issue, or the cost would be too high, indeed. Others would disappear. Some would be ousted for whatever other reason got out to the wind, by the hand of a Justicar, a rival or just popular uprising (popular uprising with many generous benefactors). Only one or two would be openly ousted by the sect as extreme hardliners whom obviously no one else on good standing agrees with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is called politics. That's how the Camarilla works. Concessions and compromises and acomodations. It would work with Princes asking favors in exchange for the deal, and those favors would be crucial to deliver favors to those bellow the Prince to accept those deals. That's how the Camarilla works. Favors exchange, that's how it works, not just simply Justicars and Archons playing Angels of the Night.<br /> <br /> A Prince being ousted by the Camarilla is an extreme event, not a common day to day businesses, and something that most be dealt with extreme care. The Camarilla is an organization of elders that exist for mutual protection of it's members; if those same elders are dealt as if they were just were cannon fodder of the Inner Circle, there would be no Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486503#post1486503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the fact that it was deemed to be in the best interest of the sect is proven simply by the fact that it happened. This is fiction. A lot of nuance and details can realistically weight in the question, but the complexity of it simply means the author is free to give any answer, since the author ultimately decides those details as they come up. It is worth noting that being open to all Kindred is official Camarilla policy, and one of the few that is heavily implied in the books to be followed almost always to the letter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Writters can write whatever they want, but what matters is if there's consistency to the story. If the writers write that all the Camarilla kindred turned into unicorns, it would be &quot;official&quot;, but it would be ridiculous, thus inconsistent with the story.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Camarilla official policy is that &quot;all vamps be welcome&quot;. And yes, this is followed.<br /> <br /> But so are the 6 traditions, who are the most sacred of their laws. If the Inner Circle decides to simply bulldozer one of their most sacred traditions, the Camarilla is history.<br /> <br /> Yes, any vampire can VISIT any Camarilla city - that's one of their traditions allright. As long as you present yourself, you have a &quot;right&quot; to be &quot;welcomed&quot;.<br /> <br /> That does NOT however mean you have the right to STAY. A vampire's territory is sacred. Nobody can FORCE other vampires to accept residents on their cities.<br /> <br /> So, in the case of the Assamites, any individual Assamite can travel to any Camarilla city unmolested - that's one of their most sacred traditions; it doesnt mean they can take RESIDENCE in whatever city they'd please.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486503#post1486503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See how the Camarilla deals with the Ravnos. When they come to a city and present themselves, they get at least the standard time of hospitality given to traveling vampires. And if they're not given residency, most Princes will not be blatant about the reason even if everyone knows the reason. Most Princes will do their best to watch and wait for the Ravnos to give them a reason to be expelled or destroyed, many will look for any reasonable excuse to shorten the Ravnos staying as much as possible, and/or pressure the Ravnos through direct or indirect means into making a blunder.<br /> <br /> But the books are very clear that just blatantly denying Ravnos because they're Ravnos isn't usually an option, and they're the apex of clan racism in the setting. Nor is being of a Sabbat clan considered grounds for overt denial unless you're proven Sabbat yourself. Why would things go different with the Banu Haqim when people actually doesn't expect them to screw you for no reason like they expect from the Ravnos?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a great example. A Ravnos will have his due time for hospitality, after which he must leave, EVEN IF he declares membership under the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> In fact, not even a Ventrue changing cities is supposed to automatically expect permanent residency in another city. Even a Ventrue Prince can outright deny residency for a foreigner Ventrue.<br /> <br /> And I would say the Assamites were far more hated than the Ravnos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T09:31:26-07:00","id":1486528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486513#post1486513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If a Prince decides to ban all Malkavians from his domain, that's going to piss the Malkavians off. And it's very likely that they're going to show up in that Prince's domain and start taking matters into their own hands to force the Prince into accept them. This is very likely going to cause all sorts of Masquerade breaches and other issues all of which are bad for the Camarilla. So the Camarilla has one of two choices - either they stand with the Prince and tell the Malkavians to go fuck themselves, or they side with the Malkavians and tell the Prince he needs to allow the Malkavians into his city.<br /> <br /> Trying to wash their hands of the matter and saying &amp;quot;You guys deal with it&amp;quot; isn't going to work because the Camarilla will be left holding the back and dealing with the fallout and Masquerade breaches that will inevitably result from that sort of conflict. And note that this is true for pretty much any Prince who bans any clan (a Ventrue banning Brujah from his city or a Tremere Prince banning Nosferatu).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is ultimately an organization created by the clans for the clans. This is the benefit to your clan having official recognition and sanction from the Camarilla. There are individual vampires, such as Tzimsci, or Ravnos, or Samedi who are part of the Camarilla and travel between Camarilla cities, but they don't have the backing or sanction, as a clan, from the organization. If a Prince tells one to leave his city, there's not much they can do about it and no one they can complain to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again though, it <i>is</i> in the Camarilla's interest to prevent vampire clans from coming to blows with asshole Princes just because the Prince wants to be an asshole to other respected members of the Camarilla, whether by negotiating or figuring out some sort of deal. And in the event that a Prince proves to be so absolutely recalcitrant that he refuses to listen to any sort of reason or negotiate or budge from his position and the Camarilla has to deal with the fallout for an extended period of time, then eventually the Camarilla is going to start considering what steps could be taken to replace that Prince with someone more reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Prince that is so short sighted and so dumb is a mystery as to just exactly how such an imbecile became a Prince in the first place.<br /> <br /> That being said, a Prince IS in theory within his rights to ban an entire clan - even a Camarilla clan.<br /> <br /> Such an imbecile will soon find out that the entirety of said clan will turn against him and his court; his court will immediatly realize they are working for a dumb fool and that they'll most likely face problems, and such a dumb Prince wont stay long in office.<br /> <br /> That being said, not every clan is present in every city, so there ARE cities upon which you'll have an &quot;official non-official&quot; policy of not accepting X clan. Like I said, hospitability decrees that all vamps should be received TEMPORARILY. So for example, if city X has no Tremere residents, or no Nosfs or whatever, any Tremere could VISIT the city. That doesnt mean an automatic right for PERMANENT RESIDENCE. If the Tremere visiting the city with no Tremeres asks the local Prince to make residence, the Prince is fully within his rights to just outright say &quot;sorry, we dont take outsiders&quot;. He obviously wont say &quot;I would rather see my sire and my children burning at a stake than having a Tremere filthy in my city!&quot;, but refusal of acceptance of individuals is a day to day affair for kindred society. And in fact, MANY cities do not accept any foreigners in their cities past their visitation periods, and changes in that usually come only under heavy negotiations.<br /> <br /> So again, there's no such a thing as automatically forcing domains to accept A, B or C cainites.<br /> <br /> Now, for every kind of policy a city may have there may be consequences. A city that has zero Malkav residents and that just simply takes no foreigners, may end up having to yield and make concessions given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> One other thing: no man rules alone. And no vampire either. A Prince is not a pupeteer pulling all kindreds in their cities by their strings. A Prince has to consider the predispositions of his court and subjects, from the Primogen elders, ancilla harpies and even neonates. It's not just &quot;oh, the Prince thinks that Tremere are ugly and boring, so he doesnt allow them in their city&quot;. That's not how it works. The Prince has to ponder, would letting a few Tremere in my city be benefitial, or cause a revolt from either the neonates or the Primogen? If the answer is the latter, his response to any Tremere visitor would be &quot;sorry, we are full&quot;. On the other hand, if the kindred in his city desperatly want a Tremere Chantry in the town, even if the Prince personally believes them to be scum, he better convince a Chantry to set up residence, otherwise he wont rule for much longer.<br /> <br /> And, if insisting on your non-Brujah unofficial policy risks facing anarchists at your doorsteps, you may want to reconsider.<br /> <br /> Now, the Inner Circle MAY interfere in pontual cases - if there's good reason to. For instance, if a bunch of Primogen and their Prince elders insistance of refusing Brujahs in is risking a revolt, the Inner Circle may first try to ask nicely, and if that fails, may impose (always as a last resource only).<br /> <br /> However, a city upon which EVERYBODY for whatever reason hates Brujahs and is perfectly stable with that arrangement, why would anyone interfere with? And why would foreigner Brujahs would want to migrate to such a hostile place to begin with?<br /> <br /> Every action has consequences, but let us clear a few things:<br /> 1. A Prince is not an Emperor; therefore, he is the manifestation of the political landscape of a city. The Prince's voice and authority therefore is that of the Primogen and Harpies combined in a single body.<br /> 2. The Prince - which ultimately express the collective will of the elders of a region - is completely within his rights to deny anyone he or his primogen wishes into his domains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T10:17:22-07:00","id":1486534,"title":"","content":"The Tremere are a corperation, but the other Clans are, in a way, unions. The Brujah fight eachother all the time, but they'll come together to smash the prince if they feel he's targeting a Brujah for their clan weakness. After all, if Prince can target Brujah A for frenzying, it sets a precedent for the the prince or anyone else targetting Brujahs B and C. If the prince is obviously targetting Brujah A because he did something wrong... well, that's nothing to do with being a Brujah, so it's probably not a clan concern.<br /> <br /> Not that you'd do it like this, but a prince openly deciding to &quot;Ban all Malkavians&quot; is in no way the same thing as banning Assamites.<br /> Firstly, Malkavians are significantly more widespread and powerful than the Assamites, especially since we're really only talking about the survivors of one side of the schism.<br /> Secondly, Malkavians are everymen. There's no great Malkavian sect/house/club, there's no historical baggage behind the malkavian clan. Malks are prevalent in every major sect, at the extremes and in the middle. Assamites aren't that. They have their own sect and it's difficult to disassociate them with it. They have their own path. They have a caste system so that they can function well independently. They have historically believed themselves to be a superior breed among vampires. It's easier to seperate them in an &quot;Us VS Them&quot; kind of way.<br /> <br /> Going against the independents, the Tremere, the Lasombra or the Tzmisce is difficult, but you can do it given not unreasonable conditions.<br /> Going against the other six clans is insane","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-15-2022, 01:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T10:43:32-07:00","id":1486535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486523#post1486523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This thread has taken some... diversions, shall we say?<br /> <br /> Anyway, I always assume everyone in VTM is scheming against everyone else. If a Justicar comes for the city's Prince, some people will be outraged, but the rest will be figuring out how to either avoid the same fate or how to twist this to their own advantage. The Primogen are the most likely to benefit from this, since one of them is most likely to wind up being Prince.<br /> <br /> Similarly, if the Prince of a neighbouring domain is ousted, it might be time to expand your own rule or send in your puppet. Rebellion is for Anarchs, and those guys are suckers. The Camarilla is the Camarilla because they're the vamps who rejected freedom for safety and comfort (and lots of hiding in shadows).<br /> <br /> The Camarilla is run by elders who pretend the even older elders don't exist. Even if they knew the Ancients personally, or are their childer. They're quite happy to bury their heads in the sand to keep the power they have. <br /> <br /> They also have no qualms breaking rules, so long as they aren't found out. The Inner Circle aren't best mates; they're just enemies who get more benefit from working together occasionally, and secretly doing their own thing the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim joining will cause jealousy, hatred and suspicion, but that's Kindred society in a nutshell. We have to remember that the Tremere experimented on Nosferatu and Gangrel right up until the formation of the Camarilla, and the Camarilla didn't immediately implode when they were all forced to play nice.<br /> <br /> It took the Gangrel nearly 500 years to leave this toxic relationship. And even then, many of them stayed out of habit and convenience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. That's how it works on ponctual case by case. <br /> <br /> But you dont make such a fragile alliance work by basically saying that every elder is useless and that they better obey the &quot;kings&quot; to the letter - or else.<br /> <br /> If you have any doubts, you need not to think on terms of the games fiction. Just think on real life feudalism in Europe and its Byzantine cutthroat politics. Just think how many kings ended up losing their thrones (and their heads) at the hands of treacherous lords. Think on the Holy German Empire, for instance. In theory, the &quot;Emperor&quot; was the boss; in reality thou, an Emperor incapable of being able to balance the needs and wants and the endless rivalries of the many princeses wouldnt last long in the throne.<br /> <br /> In fact, kindred society ressambles very much the HRE or the Byzantine politics. So by that standard you can realize that there's no absolute power that controls everything from top down, and that holds true for all levels of the organization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T10:56:16-07:00","id":1486536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486513#post1486513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again though, it <i>is</i> in the Camarilla's interest to prevent vampire clans from coming to blows with asshole Princes just because the Prince wants to be an asshole to other respected members of the Camarilla, whether by negotiating or figuring out some sort of deal. And in the event that a Prince proves to be so absolutely recalcitrant that he refuses to listen to any sort of reason or negotiate or budge from his position and the Camarilla has to deal with the fallout for an extended period of time, then eventually the Camarilla is going to start considering what steps could be taken to replace that Prince with someone more reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very different scenario from having the Justicars going around the globe and turning hundreds of Princes into cinders city by city just to show how awesomely powerful and tyrannical the Camarilla higher ups are. What you are talking about here is some true trouble maker that is actively causing problems for no good reason whatsoever.<br /> <br /> This scenario however is EXTREMELY unrealistic.<br /> <br /> A Prince that completely disregards his entire court wont be Prince for long. And that cut both ways.<br /> <br /> A Prince that lets the Assamites in despite his entire court saying &quot;dont let them in&quot;, will end up being retired.<br /> <br /> A Prince that dont let them in despite the entire court begging for them, just the same.<br /> <br /> When a Prince says &quot;I dont want X in my city&quot;, it's because X individual/group would cause problems, and that would be no good for the Camarilla at all.<br /> <br /> And, why would the Camarilla want to shove Assamites into cities where they'll only cause problems? Where everybody will be hostile to them?<br /> <br /> The Assamites were accepted, they are in the Camarilla. That being said, there are cities where they didnt go, and others where they did. Simple","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T13:18:25-07:00","id":1486549,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>MyWifeIsScary, a suggestion to tone it down. You seem to be taking this a lot more seriously than it really warrants.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T14:18:44-07:00","id":1486553,"title":"","content":"You're probably right. Should really stop projecting my inner Tremere. IDK why but I get triggered by people wanting Vampire politicians to play nice and fair or to have characters accept good/evil rolls rather than do what's best for them. Because art is about truth for me.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> Playing Tremere and lording it over everyone's fun*<br /> and also<br /> playing -not Tremere thaumaturge- and bitterly struggling against prejudice, a system rigged against you, and your own paranoia (they really are out to get you) is even more fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> VTM, ultimately, is about power dynamics. Making everything fair and equal goes against the fundamentals that drive the game, and from an art/literary point of view it doesn't work to have everything easy. From a Doylist point of view - Monopolistic Big Boss Faction- vs -dangerous underdogs- just works. You can Mirror it with Giovanni VS other necromancers, or you could reverse it: Tremere weren't doing so well a thousand years ago, or you could use -Your own coven of witches who have long dominated thaumaturgy in this region with the support of local powers- vs the Tremere who've pissed someone off and have now been sent to set up a chantry in some forsaken corner they haven't made inroads into yet.<br /> <br /> Lastly, how much assamite lore have you lot actually read?<br /> They're theocratic fascists who believe they're physically and morally a superior race.<br /> Even if we just talk schismatics, we're still mostly in the territory of &quot;superior race&quot; with a lot of schismatics also being zealots for maladapted human religions. IE &quot;I'm not a Nazi, I'm a conservative&quot;<br /> I don't think people should be looking too kindly on that. The Sabbat at least know they're full of shit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T15:09:28-07:00","id":1486555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486553#post1486553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're probably right. Should really stop projecting my inner Tremere. IDK why but I get triggered by people wanting Vampire politicians to play nice and fair or to have characters accept good/evil rolls rather than do what's best for them. Because art is about truth for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Red Text indicates I'm using my mod voice, friend. Which is to say, don't sarcastically reply please. Take a warning now. Next will be asking you to leave the thread.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T16:57:13-07:00","id":1486561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486534#post1486534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that you'd do it like this, but a prince openly deciding to &quot;Ban all Malkavians&quot; is in no way the same thing as banning Assamites.<br /> Firstly, Malkavians are significantly more widespread and powerful than the Assamites, especially since we're really only talking about the survivors of one side of the schism.<br /> Secondly, Malkavians are everymen. There's no great Malkavian sect/house/club, there's no historical baggage behind the malkavian clan. Malks are prevalent in every major sect, at the extremes and in the middle. Assamites aren't that. They have their own sect and it's difficult to disassociate them with it. They have their own path. They have a caste system so that they can function well independently. They have historically believed themselves to be a superior breed among vampires. It's easier to seperate them in an &quot;Us VS Them&quot; kind of way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is though, the Camarilla is not going to officially support a policy that allows for a very broad policy of banning of vampires from cities simply because of their clan, wven if the clan targeted is the Assamites or the Lasombra Antitribu or one of the other non-major clans. If the Camarilla allows Princes to ban vampires from some clans, then it's only a matter of time before Princes start trying to ban vampires from other clans and that's just going to cause headaches for the Camarilla. So the Camarilla will always have the official policy of supporting access of clans to cities.<br /> <br /> Now the reality on the ground might be a bit different. Maybe the Prince of a given city is too strong for the Camarilla to want to oppose. Maybe the Prince has ties to the Inner Circle. There could be tons of other reasons. So it's possible for a Prince to broadly ban vampires from a given clan from settling in his city and the Camarilla might not actually do much about it. But, at least officially, the Camarilla will say that what the Prince is doing is unfair or unjust and officially they'll take a position that the Prince should allow vampires from that clan into his city.<br /> <br /> So you could see some Princes trying to refuse to allow Assamites from entering or settling in their cities. And the Camarilla would exert various forms of pressure on those Princes to accept the Assamites, and in some cases the Princes would accede but in others they wouldn't. That would not likely include outright assassination of the Prince (though that might be result of standing against a clan of well known assassins and you could have vampires who don't like the Assamites, or more traditional Assamites, assassinate the Prince in order to make the Banu Haqim who joined the Camarilla look bad).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T18:28:09-07:00","id":1486569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486553#post1486553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, how much assamite lore have you lot actually read?<br /> They're theocratic fascists who believe they're physically and morally a superior race.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, the whole point is the Schismatics are running away from the theocratic fascists.<br /> <br /> The Vizier Caste is almost an inversion really since they're basically Assamite Toreador.<br /> <br /> I admit to not being a huge huge fan of Revised Assamites but I appreciate what they were trying to do: get away from the one note stereotype.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-15-2022, 09:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T20:52:37-07:00","id":1486576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486561#post1486561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is though, the Camarilla is not going to officially support a policy that allows for a very broad policy of banning of vampires from cities simply because of their clan, wven if the clan targeted is the Assamites or the Lasombra Antitribu or one of the other non-major clans. If the Camarilla allows Princes to ban vampires from some clans, then it's only a matter of time before Princes start trying to ban vampires from other clans and that's just going to cause headaches for the Camarilla. So the Camarilla will always have the official policy of supporting access of clans to cities.<br /> <br /> Now the reality on the ground might be a bit different. Maybe the Prince of a given city is too strong for the Camarilla to want to oppose. Maybe the Prince has ties to the Inner Circle. There could be tons of other reasons. So it's possible for a Prince to broadly ban vampires from a given clan from settling in his city and the Camarilla might not actually do much about it. But, at least officially, the Camarilla will say that what the Prince is doing is unfair or unjust and officially they'll take a position that the Prince should allow vampires from that clan into his city.<br /> <br /> So you could see some Princes trying to refuse to allow Assamites from entering or settling in their cities. And the Camarilla would exert various forms of pressure on those Princes to accept the Assamites, and in some cases the Princes would accede but in others they wouldn't. That would not likely include outright assassination of the Prince (though that might be result of standing against a clan of well known assassins and you could have vampires who don't like the Assamites, or more traditional Assamites, assassinate the Prince in order to make the Banu Haqim who joined the Camarilla look bad).</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I have to say that the domain of a vampire is sacred and it's one of the 6 traditional laws of the Camarilla. If the Camarilla doesnt follow that, the sect does not exist.<br /> <br /> Also, the VAST majority of cities will NOT have members of all the major clans of the Camarilla - let alone minor bloodlines. And in fact, a great many deal of small towns dont have a single vampire living in it at all!<br /> <br /> A city with a few Brujah, a few Nosferatu and a few Toreador (say, just 3 of each, for the impressive number of 9), could perfectly resonably refuse an individual Ventrue to take residence in it, without needing any further explanations. Now, obviously said Ventrue could negotiate and could bring something to the table for that arrangement, but there's nowhere that says that local kindred populations HAVE to accept any sort of foreigners trying to set shop in their towns. They dont.<br /> <br /> Now, obviously a Prince that keeps branding at full lungs that Ventrues or Tremere or Brujah or whomever are scum and that's why he'll never suffer one to enter his domains, is an utter imbecile and I would very much like to unravel the mystery behind how such a stupid moron became Prince in the first place (and I would like to know his primogen of at least equally idiotic elders), but a Prince can simply handwave solicitations of residence from foreigners without needing to give any sort of further explanations.<br /> <br /> So, in theory all are &quot;welcomed&quot;, but in practice the local leaders (Prince and Primogen) can in fact discriminate, if that's truly their thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T21:41:00-07:00","id":1486583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486576#post1486576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I have to say that the domain of a vampire is sacred and it's one of the 6 traditional laws of the Camarilla. If the Camarilla doesnt follow that, the sect does not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then may I ask what sort of power do you think the Inner Council actually possesses. If it can't control the Princes, it doesn't actually have any power whatsoever.<br /> <br /> At least as a body of itself.<br /> <br /> They might be immensely powerful personal Kindred but who are they ordering around if they're not the bosses of the Princedoms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T22:10:15-07:00","id":1486586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486509#post1486509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- there are few Assamites because the schismatics have largely been purged. Also, the Assamites weren't really a big clan in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure about this. The clan's size was barely touched upon even before it got expanded into three castes and then the Web of Knifes. The majority of known pre-Schism contact with them is mostly the WoK, but those are just a fraction of the whole clan, <i>at most</i> a little more than a fourth, but possibly far less.<br /> <br /> The influence of the WoK rose considerably, but their actual numbers relative to the rest of the clan only started to swell by the end of the 90's, as the recruits of the Gulf War got ready in their first attempt at &quot;mass-Embrace&quot;. That can indeed be massive given how it happened. Even adding their second generation of mass Embraces by the time of <i>Lore of the Clans</i>, they comprise just half the Warrior Caste, reaching that little more than a fourth. Before those events the Warriors would be more influential but about as numerous as the Viziers, and the Web just a small faction within them. And even then they're mostly living outside contact and knowledge of most Kindred in the major Sects, so the Web itself may be larger than it appears, and they're secretive about their numbers and meeting places even among the Ashirra, so no one can actually say how numerous they are.<br /> <br /> Reverse-calculating, whatever it is you picture as the apparent Banu Haqim's size by the regular books, their actual size would be at least four times that and possibly several times more. Ultimately it is as hard to grasp as any clan, but there is no reason to be <b>sure</b> they're particularly small.<br /> <br /> Also the Schismatics got their hardest hit on Alamut, but they were also the less likely to be there at any given time. If you go by V20 their Schism was a decade in the making, which makes it even less likely to kill a lot of them. So there was a purge, but it is hard to say to which extent this purge meant murders instead of just early defection, as both fit within the definition of a purge. No doubt the Web and Ur-Shulgi want to just eliminate as many of the Schismatics as possible as the murder-hobos they are, but ultimately there's plenty of space for the ST to assume that they just couldn't do nearly as much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486553#post1486553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, how much assamite lore have you lot actually read?<br /> They're theocratic fascists who believe they're physically and morally a superior race.<br /> Even if we just talk schismatics, we're still mostly in the territory of &quot;superior race&quot; with a lot of schismatics also being zealots for maladapted human religions. IE &quot;I'm not a Nazi, I'm a conservative&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read quite some lore on them, although admittedly not all of it. Yet, a lot of people here have a tendency to focus on the parts of the lore they like more and downplay the parts they don't. I'm no exception to this, but you neither, what I do see on you and some other posters (on both sides of the current discussion) is a tendency to exacerbate it into full on claiming your interpretation is the only actual lore.<br /> <br /> Since they started to be more fleshed out the Banu Haqim has increasingly being described as dominated by moderates in numbers, with the theocratic fascists being a vocal minority whose influence comes from their combination of martial power and willingness to use it. Which is to say they're a moderate society under the dominance of a zealot military dictatorship, nothing new to me or my country. This has only increased since then, in <i>Revised</i> the clan reached the apex of the notion of being mostly moderate religious people with a more secular view on their life and doings. In V20 it is explicitly stated that they're mostly non-religious, on top of many religious members being devout but not zealots, with the obvious exception of the Web of Knifes.<br /> <br /> On a side, but somewhat more serious note, I would ask what you meant by &quot;maladapted human religions&quot;, as I'm not sure I understood your message or the opposite of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-15T23:02:20-07:00","id":1486591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486509#post1486509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>If the Cam really wants more members, it hurts them less to just embrace a few more neonates rather than have foreigners join them</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla wants all vampires to be members of the Camarilla. As long as vampires exist outside of the Camarilla then they don't have a monopoly on the power base they want to. Letting the Assamites join reduces the number of vampires outside of the Camarilla while bringing with them a massive amount of power. A bunch of Neonate Ventrue or Tremere are useless to someone like Tegyrius who rode with Alexander the Great.<br /> <br /> Which is another element that the Tremere Neonates are powerless versus the Assamites who bring REAL power as see with Ur-Shulgi effortlessly breaking the Tremere Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486586#post1486586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since they started to be more fleshed out the Banu Haqim has increasingly being described as dominated by moderates in numbers, with the theocratic fascists being a vocal minority whose influence comes from their combination of martial power and willingness to use it. Which is to say they're a moderate society under the dominance of a zealot military dictatorship, nothing new to me or my country. This has only increased since then, in <i>Revised</i> the clan reached the apex of the notion of being mostly moderate religious people with a more secular view on their life and doings. In V20 it is explicitly stated that they're mostly non-religious, on top of many religious members being devout but not zealots, with the obvious exception of the Web of Knifes.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>My theory on how the Assamites work</b><br /> <br /> Specifically, this all ties together with the Road of Blood/Path of Blood versus religion in general. The Road of Blood is what teaches that Haqim is a vampire who Embraced himself and orders that all other Cainites but the Banu Haqim be destroyed. Even this is an extremist interpretation of things but was the primary &quot;face&quot; the Banu Haqim presented in Europe due to the fact these guys in the Web of Knives showed during the Anarch Revolt when they were hired &quot;en masse&quot; to kill the Elders of Europe.<br /> <br /> Why did they ally with the Anarchs? Well, the Anarchs were very often Higher Generation and happy to nark on their sires and grandsires. Notably, when the Anarchs wanted to learn about Haqim, the Assamites went, &quot;No no no no no.&quot; They made up the Road of Caine instead and it's kind of hilarious that one of my favorite Roads is complete bullshit and watered down Haqim with the name hit find/replace.<br /> <br /> The Banu Haqim's NON-CRAZY psycho side was part of the Ashirra and I take the interpretation of 5th Edition that actually works quite well, which is the fact the Ashirra are officially all Muslims but most of them are just paying lip service to the religion of Allah. The Viziers more or less interacted peacefully with other vampires and the Mages were doing their own weird esoteric things. I also like the idea that the Banu Haqim LET themselves be cursed by the Tremere to make Kindred vitae poisonous to them because they wanted to get rid of their vitae addiction.<br /> <br /> (Because the Baali may have been responsible for that curse in the first place)<br /> <br /> But gradually, the Assamite Antitribu (which were a mixture of hardcore Road of Blood members and those Embraced after) and the Warrior Caste Embraced more than the other castes while indoctrinating a large number at Alamut into the extreme position. In Revised, it was Ur-Shulgi who ordered all Muslims to recant their beliefs then pledge themselves to Haqim above all other gods. This probably because Ur-shulgi finds monotheism silly (even if Haqim was himself religious) and my suspicion that Haqim is actually a Baali. This gets soft retconned by BDJ into being fear of the Web of Knives now.<br /> <br /> 5th Edition has the SHEPHERDS OF UR-SHULGI and Alamut having been destroyed. Ur-Shulgi has goen &quot;somewhere else&quot; and the Shepards are now just a minor Blood Cult. My view is that the Sabbat Gehenna War probably was fought primarily against the Web of Knives and the Sabbat's entire war in the &quot;Middle East&quot; was less against random elders than the Web of Knives that they eventually wore down with sheer numbers.<br /> <br /> That's admittedly the LEAST mystical and esoteric take on the Gehenna War and that's probably why I like it.<br /> <br /> So the HUGE IRONY of all this is the Schismatics have won their war against the Web of Knives primarily because of the Sabbat and have spent the past 20 years sitting pretty in the Ivory Tower.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a side, but somewhat more serious note, I would ask what you meant by &quot;maladapted human religions&quot;, as I'm not sure I understood your message or the opposite of it. </div> </div> </div>I believe MyWifeIsScary is referring to the fact that he believes a lot of religions, particularly Islam, cannot reasonably be adapted to vampire life so any Muslim vampire is fooling itself. I actually agree with him on this but pointed out the same applied to Christianity or any ethical person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-16-2022, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T00:48:47-07:00","id":1486598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486576#post1486576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I have to say that the domain of a vampire is sacred and it's one of the 6 traditional laws of the Camarilla. If the Camarilla doesnt follow that, the sect does not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, the Camarilla was not an organization created by Princes for the benefit of princes, but an organization created by Vampire clans for the benefit of the Vampire clans. Princes are given a lot of leeway and respect, but in a conflict between a Prince and one of the vampire clans that comes to the attention of the Camarilla, the body is generally going to side with the clan. Especially if it's something as basic as, &quot;The Prince refuses to allow any members of Clan X to settle in his city, despite the Camarilla having declared that all vampires from all clans are ostensibly equal.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla can't really condone or support Princes blatantly discriminating against Vampire clans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486576#post1486576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, obviously a Prince that keeps branding at full lungs that Ventrues or Tremere or Brujah or whomever are scum and that's why he'll never suffer one to enter his domains, is an utter imbecile and I would very much like to unravel the mystery behind how such a stupid moron became Prince in the first place (and I would like to know his primogen of at least equally idiotic elders), but a Prince can simply handwave solicitations of residence from foreigners without needing to give any sort of further explanations.<br /> <br /> So, in theory all are &quot;welcomed&quot;, but in practice the local leaders (Prince and Primogen) can in fact discriminate, if that's truly their thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have examples of Princes refusing entrance to clans of vampires such as Ravnos and Malkavians and we can see the response from those clans, where they take matters into their own hands and flood the town or cause Masquerade breaches until the Prince finally relents. And it's safe to say that the Camarilla is not going to be on the Prince's side in such a conflict, especially since it's the Camarilla that will have to go into overtime to deal with those Masquerade breaches or other problems.<br /> <br /> Princes are given respect by the Camarilla, until that Prince's actions starts posing a serious problem to the Camarilla's existence.<br /> <br /> There are lots of options that the Camarilla can use against an unruly Prince who decides to start engaging in blatant discrimination against a clan. It's very unlikely to include straight up assassination, but the Camarilla would absolutely start removing its support for the Prince, putting its support behind someone else, the Prince would start losing allies and prestige, etc.<br /> <br /> At the very least, in an event like that the Camarilla is absolutely not going to just shrug and say, &quot;Okay Prince, Clan Malkavian, you guys just do whatever you want. Have fun kiddos and good luck working that that problem out.&quot; The Camarilla will get involved and it's very likely to come down on the side of the clan that's facing blatant discrimination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T01:27:36-07:00","id":1486602,"title":"","content":"This is entirely at my table but one of the big &quot;reforms' of the Camarilla at the Convention of Thorns was guaranteeing right of free movement actually.<br /> <br /> Before, a Prince could refuse access to any vampire he wanted and often would have only his brood in the small cities.<br /> <br /> Now you HAD to give a vampire access as long as he agreed to abide by the Traditions.<br /> <br /> This resulted in so many cities becoming cosmopolitan.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T05:39:34-07:00","id":1486608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486583#post1486583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then may I ask what sort of power do you think the Inner Council actually possesses. If it can't control the Princes, it doesn't actually have any power whatsoever.<br /> <br /> At least as a body of itself.<br /> <br /> They might be immensely powerful personal Kindred but who are they ordering around if they're not the bosses of the Princedoms?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Holy Roman Emperor of the HRE had a lot of power, but he wasnt the pimp of the german princes just simply automatically doing his bidding.<br /> <br /> The Shogun of Japan had a lot of power over his Daimyos, but that doesnt mean that they were automatically bound to obey him.<br /> <br /> We have trouble understanding such things nowadays because now we have nation-states, so for example, the governor of Bavaria wont rebel against the government over Berlin, nor will the governor of California rebel against Washington.<br /> <br /> But that was exactly what happened in the past. The princes of the HRE for instance, were bound to follow the Emperor, but in truth they were the sovereigns of their domains.<br /> <br /> The closest we have today, just so that you could have a mental picture of how it works, would be the European Union - but still, as it is today, the Union has already centralized far too much power.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla would actually be somewhere between the European Union and the United Nations in terms of influence. So, you may say &quot;oh the United Nations have no power&quot;, but that's not true. The UN dont have direct, centralizing power, but it does however have great influence - and can even directly intervene in some particular and extreme cases. Such is also the case of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> So, to sum it up: you can have an organization without having absolute power centralized in an &quot;Emperor&quot;. We've had many many examples throught history, like the HRE, the Shogunate Japan, the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, the Hellenic League, and today the European Union and UN.<br /> <br /> And it's not that the Inner Circle have no power; they do have power, just not absolute power that needn't answer to no one. The Shogun of Japan or the Emperor of the HRE had a lot a power, just like the European Congress in Bruxels have a lot of power. It doesnt mean that, if the Inner Circle sends a &quot;memo&quot; that some princes dont like that they have no saying in the matter; just imagine the EU, how many times it were defied by the UK, by Poland and Italy.<br /> <br /> It's politics; in the EU for instance, a country like Slovakia, what weight does it have? Almost zero, so such a country most of the time just comply with Bruxels. Now, a Germany, a Poland, even Hungary, those are countries that can openly defy it. And it all turns into negotiations and politics.<br /> <br /> Likewise, the prince of Smallville with the incredible population of 3 cainites wont be openly defying the Inner Council - not alone at least; this could however change if he managed a coallition of princes - but the Princedom of cities like NY, LA, London, Paris, Berlin, Frankfurt etc etc etc have too much weight on them to just simply being bossed around, and decisions for those cases arent reached by top down bossing around, but rather by compromises and agreements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T06:27:53-07:00","id":1486613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486598#post1486598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Again though, the Camarilla was not an organization created by Princes for the benefit of princes, but an organization created by Vampire clans for the benefit of the Vampire clans. Princes are given a lot of leeway and respect, but in a conflict between a Prince and one of the vampire clans that comes to the attention of the Camarilla, the body is generally going to side with the clan. Especially if it's something as basic as, &amp;quot;The Prince refuses to allow any members of Clan X to settle in his city, despite the Camarilla having declared that all vampires from all clans are ostensibly equal.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> The Camarilla can't really condone or support Princes blatantly discriminating against Vampire clans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We have examples of Princes refusing entrance to clans of vampires such as Ravnos and Malkavians and we can see the response from those clans, where they take matters into their own hands and flood the town or cause Masquerade breaches until the Prince finally relents. And it's safe to say that the Camarilla is not going to be on the Prince's side in such a conflict, especially since it's the Camarilla that will have to go into overtime to deal with those Masquerade breaches or other problems.<br /> <br /> Princes are given respect by the Camarilla, until that Prince's actions starts posing a serious problem to the Camarilla's existence.<br /> <br /> There are lots of options that the Camarilla can use against an unruly Prince who decides to start engaging in blatant discrimination against a clan. It's very unlikely to include straight up assassination, but the Camarilla would absolutely start removing its support for the Prince, putting its support behind someone else, the Prince would start losing allies and prestige, etc.<br /> <br /> At the very least, in an event like that the Camarilla is absolutely not going to just shrug and say, &amp;quot;Okay Prince, Clan Malkavian, you guys just do whatever you want. Have fun kiddos and good luck working that that problem out.&amp;quot; The Camarilla will get involved and it's very likely to come down on the side of the clan that's facing blatant discrimination.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said that such a policy is wise or practical on an overall level. You do need however to be careful not to generalize and to understand that things must be considered on a case by case situation. For major cities, simply outright refusing Clan X or Clan Y is unpractical due to the consequences; just imagine the kindred on Paris trying to impose a ban on Toreador settling there; the backlash to this would've been insane.<br /> <br /> However, this is something that the Camarilla cant even enforce in practice. Think about it. If YOU were a vampire looking for a new city to stay for whatever reason, would you move to a place that you know the locals will be openly hostile to your presence, even if they supposedly have to swallow it dry? I recon it would be far better to keep looking for a greener place rather than living with a knife constantly hanging above your head.<br /> <br /> Now, to begin with yet again, that sort of decision is NOT a &quot;Prince&quot;; the Prince most often than not end up being just the collective voice of the local kindred population. Such a decision from &quot;The Prince&quot; actually is a reflection of the Primogen, the ancilla harpies and even neonates to some degree.<br /> <br /> And the reason this doesnt happen quite so often is because the math simply says &quot;NO&quot;. Elders are survivors; and in order to do so, they must calculate their odds in all actions. What's the benefits of doing X? Well, maybe forbidding Toreador in your city may have a small benefit. Does that outweight the costs? If the answer is no - which most certanly it isnt - then you dont do it.<br /> <br /> Like you said, imagine banning malkavs or ravnos. What are the consequences? Oh yes, the consequences are severe. So you dont do it.<br /> <br /> It's as simple as that. It's NOT because the &quot;Princes&quot; (in truth, representatives of the Primogen and local kindred overall) CANT do it, but rather because it is most of the time a stupid decision to be made, that would bring far too much troubles for far too little again (if any).<br /> <br /> It's just the same as irl kings or emperors; in theory, they can do whatever they want; in truth however, there are things they they SHOULDNT do (because it may cause them to end up on the wrong side of an axe).<br /> <br /> That being said, the fact that has never been an elder revolt against the Inner Circle is already a testment of their skill and cunnning. Just look at real life places like shogunate Japan, the HRE, the Polish-Lithuanian CW and many medieval kingdoms and we see that the vast majority of revolts were always of nobles, very very rarely of peasants. The Inner Circle manages to keep a bunch of elders under relative control, that's one hell of an accomplishment.<br /> <br /> And they wouldnt ruin it by forcing the entire Camarilla to throw out one of their most sacred laws - specially since there's no need to, since as I already said, there are cities that will want desperatly to receive the Assamites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T07:28:23-07:00","id":1486617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486602#post1486602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is entirely at my table but one of the big &amp;quot;reforms' of the Camarilla at the Convention of Thorns was guaranteeing right of free movement actually.<br /> <br /> Before, a Prince could refuse access to any vampire he wanted and often would have only his brood in the small cities.<br /> <br /> Now you HAD to give a vampire access as long as he agreed to abide by the Traditions.<br /> <br /> This resulted in so many cities becoming cosmopolitan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess we need to take a look at the text of the Camarilla's Lex:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Traditions</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">First Tradition: The Masquerade<br /> Thou shall not reveal thy true nature to those not of the Blood.<br /> Doing such shall renounce thy claims of Blood.<br /> <br /> Second Tradition: The Domain<br /> Thy domain is thine own concern.<br /> All others owe thee respect while in it.<br /> None may challenge thy word while in thy domain.<br /> <br /> Third Tradition: The Progeny<br /> Thou shall only Sire another with the permission of thine Elder.<br /> If thou createst another without thine Elder's leave, both thou and thy Progeny shall be slain.<br /> <br /> Fourth Tradition: The Accounting<br /> Those thou create are thine own children.<br /> Until thy Progeny shall be Released, thou shall command them in all things.<br /> Their sins are thine to endure.<br /> <br /> Fifth Tradition: The Hospitality<br /> Honor one another's domain.<br /> When thou comest to a foreign city, thou shall present thyself to the one who ruleth there.<br /> Without the word of acceptance, thou art nothing.<br /> <br /> Sixth Tradition: The Destruction<br /> Thou art forbidden to destroy another of thy kind.<br /> The right of destruction belongeth only to thine Elder.<br /> Only the Eldest among thee shall call the Blood Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are the basic laws of the Camarilla, the cornerstone upon which the sect's foundation lays, and the guiding body of laws that guides all of the Camarilla's policies, politics and behavior.<br /> <br /> To blatantly disregard those is to breed instability and possible dissolution to the sect - and that's NOT something that the Inner Circle - the most cunning and apt members of the Camarilla, as well as the best connected ones - would willingly do.<br /> <br /> Of importance for the present discussion is the Second and Fifth Traditions, that respectivelly claim:<br /> <br /> &quot;Second Tradition: The Domain<br /> Thy domain is thine own concern.<br /> All others owe thee respect while in it.<br /> NONE MAY CHALLENGE THY WORD WHILE IN THY DOMAIN.&quot;<br /> <br /> And the Fifth:<br /> <br /> &quot;Fifth Tradition: The Hospitality<br /> Honor one another's domain.<br /> When thou comest to a foreign city, thou shall present thyself to the one who ruleth there.<br /> WITHOUT THE WORD OF ACCEPTANCE, THOU ART NOTHING.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The Traditions form the legal backbone of Camarilla society, although in modern nights, the Prince fulfills the Elder role outlined in the traditions. Most vampiric culture springs from the Traditions \u2013 presentation is outlined in the Tradition of Hospitality, the Blood Hunt in the Tradition of Destruction and the parceling of land in the Tradition of Domain.&quot;<br /> - From the White Wolf Wiki.<br /> <br /> This means that any Camarilla vampire can VISIT any Camarilla city - as long as they fulfill the tradition of presentation - but they can only STAY with the permission of the owner of the place.<br /> <br /> Guys, the Tradition of Domain is the second tradition! Down there bellow the Masquerade itself! It is the single most important tradition besides the masquerade!<br /> <br /> And the letter of the fifth tradition, the tradition of hospitality is enfatic into reinforcing this: &quot;Without the word of acceptance, thou art nothing.&quot;<br /> <br /> The reason why cities became more cosmopolitan is political - not a thuggish imposition of Justicars. It comes from political agreements between Elders (Princes+Primogens) of different locations. And again, it's often better to make some concessions than facing some of the consequences, but again, no Kindred community (represented by their Primogen and/or Prince) are ever FORCED to accept foreigners, under any circumstances.<br /> <br /> This means that ALL acts of &quot;kindred immigration&quot; are ALWAYS political acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T07:37:41-07:00","id":1486619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486586#post1486586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure about this. The clan's size was barely touched upon even before it got expanded into three castes and then the Web of Knifes. The majority of known pre-Schism contact with them is mostly the WoK, but those are just a fraction of the whole clan, <i>at most</i> a little more than a fourth, but possibly far less.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC The WoK was a relatively modern invention right? Otherwise it would've taken over long ago. The WoK does not have a monopoly on the Path of Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The influence of the WoK rose considerably, but their actual numbers relative to the rest of the clan only started to swell by the end of the 90's, as the recruits of the Gulf War got ready in their first attempt at &quot;mass-Embrace&quot;. That can indeed be massive given how it happened. Even adding their second generation of mass Embraces by the time of <i>Lore of the Clans</i>, they comprise just half the Warrior Caste, reaching that little more than a fourth. Before those events the Warriors would be more influential but about as numerous as the Viziers, and the Web just a small faction within them. And even then they're mostly living outside contact and knowledge of most Kindred in the major Sects, so the Web itself may be larger than it appears, and they're secretive about their numbers and meeting places even among the Ashirra, so no one can actually say how numerous they are. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I read somewhere that the warriors have <i>always </i>been the most numerous caste since they clan has always had more soldiers to pull from while scholars and mages who can adapt to vampire living are few, so warriors have been outnumbering the other two casts together even in the best of times.<b> The WoK had plenty of allies among other warriors</b>. The number of warriors has increased significantly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've read quite some lore on them, although admittedly not all of it. Yet, a lot of people here have a tendency to focus on the parts of the lore they like more and downplay the parts they don't. I'm no exception to this, but you neither, what I do see on you and some other posters (on both sides of the current discussion) is a tendency to exacerbate it into full on claiming your interpretation is the only actual lore. </div> </div> </div>I think you really<i> have</i> to do this, especially as different editions contradict one another, with retcons often being for the worse.<br /> <br /> The Assamites are unfortunately one of the worst for this. It comes across as really.. split personality kinda stuff.<br /> <br /> First, they're a monsterous reactionary Islamist clan.<br /> Then we have attempts to seperate them from Islam,<br /> ...and we have attempts to use them to promote the culture of the middle east and Islam, again from a western lense, because orientalism is fun.<br /> ...and now that we've established how cool that is we're happily half-tying them to Arabs and Islam again, while also making them multicultural because the writers want to have their cake and eat it too. &quot;Banu Haqim&quot; amrite?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a side, but somewhat more serious note, I would ask what you meant by &quot;maladapted human religions&quot;, as I'm not sure I understood your message or the opposite of it. </div> </div> </div>Vampires are adopting human religions which do not work for vampires, and twisting them into horrendous parodies of the human religions. You simply can't keep to the Tennets of Islam or Christianity as a Vampire. Thus vampires ignore/change/reverse rules to keep up the practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-16-2022, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T07:56:40-07:00","id":1486621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Camarilla wants all vampires to be members of the Camarilla. As long as vampires exist outside of the Camarilla then they don't have a monopoly on the power base they want to. Letting the Assamites join reduces the number of vampires outside of the Camarilla while bringing with them a massive amount of power. A bunch of Neonate Ventrue or Tremere are useless to someone like Tegyrius who rode with Alexander the Great.<br /> <br /> Which is another element that the Tremere Neonates are powerless versus the Assamites who bring REAL power as see with Ur-Shulgi effortlessly breaking the Tremere Curse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I 100% agree with you on that one. The Camarilla wants all vampires inside, and abbiding by their rules (at least allegedly; of course vampires will always work behind the scenes too). That includes even the more unsavory types like Setittes and Tzimisce<br /> <br /> Edit: the one exception would be the Baali, because those are known infernalists. Oh yes, and also that bloodline that needs to EAT the mortals in order to feed, what's their name again? I largelly ignore them, which is why I dont remember their name, but those are walking masquerade violations, so yeah, those are the two exceptions for the Camarilla, marked as &quot;terminate on sight&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-16-2022, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T08:09:16-07:00","id":1486623,"title":"","content":"If we consider the history of the clan, my thoughts are as follows: <br /> Assamites were the late Gestapo of the declining second city. a militant sect who worshiped the founder. <br /> The Baali curse made them especially bloodthirsty<br /> Their beliefs warped. <br /> The Ashirra formed in large part due to Baali and assamite threats, and tried to play the Assamites off against other foes while also trying to make the assamites more moderate by promoting human religion. <br /> The Tremere curse was highly effective in curbing the Warriors, and combined with the efforts of the Ashirra this allowed for the blossoming of a more liberal Assamite sect. <br /> The WoK, among other groups, form as a reaction. Prepping to purge &quot;outside influences&quot;. <br /> The last century gives the warriors a huge boost <br /> Ur Shulgi wakes up, or he doesn't, either way it's a good time to start the revolution. <br /> <br /> <br /> Bringing it back to the main topic: While Warriors were mostly Loyalist and Viziers mostly Schismatic, canonically the Sorcerers were an even split. One could even reason that they might be more likely to go loyalist: Modern religion isn't good for Dur-An-Ki practitioners, and the rise of a great master like Ur-Shulgi will be a great boon for the Sorcerer caste both politically and knowledge wise. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T09:32:05-07:00","id":1486633,"title":"","content":"I think that the Tremere are going to have serious rivals in the blood sorcery business with the addition of Banu Haqium, Aybss mystics of the Lasombra and the odd Hecata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:15:33-07:00","id":1486652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486623#post1486623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing it back to the main topic: While Warriors were mostly Loyalist and Viziers mostly Schismatic, canonically the Sorcerers were an even split. One could even reason that they might be more likely to go loyalist: Modern religion isn't good for Dur-An-Ki practitioners, and the rise of a great master like Ur-Shulgi will be a great boon for the Sorcerer caste both politically and knowledge wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal view is the Sorcerers would split in large part because Al-Ashrad, Ur-Shulgi's only known child and the leader of the Assamite Sorcerer caste, is a Schismatic.<br /> <br /> Probably because Al-Ashrad knows Ur-Shulgi is a Baali.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:46:09-07:00","id":1486657,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that make Al-Ashrad a Baali, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:52:59-07:00","id":1486658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486633#post1486633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the Tremere are going to have serious rivals in the blood sorcery business with the addition of Banu Haqium, Aybss mystics of the Lasombra and the odd Hecata.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldnt call such a disorganized rabble as &quot;serious competition&quot;. They no longer hold the monopoly that's for sure, but are still number 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:54:20-07:00","id":1486659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486657#post1486657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that make Al-Ashrad a Baali, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if Ur-Shulgi converted to Baali after embracing his progeny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T12:59:33-07:00","id":1486661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, this all ties together with the Road of Blood/Path of Blood versus religion in general. The Road of Blood is what teaches that Haqim is a vampire who Embraced himself and orders that all other Cainites but the Banu Haqim be destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Religion is what gives <i>Via Sanguinis</i> the context it needs, because it doesn't completely defines &quot;honor&quot; by itself. It is an interesting Road in how it puts weight on a concept &quot;to be defined by specific law&quot;, so to speak. With that, two Kindred on the Road can have completely distinct outlooks on what constitutes &quot;honor&quot;.<br /> <br /> But it doesn't command destruction based on clan on any interpretation. Even the Web of Knives has a notion of honor that can be extended to other Kindred (although their zealotry males this almost impossible), and even the most moderate follower of the Road can see some clan mates as dishonorable. As it also commands forethought in lieu of impulsive action, in practice most followers of the original Road aren't zealots like the Web.<br /> <br /> That's also why the Web of Knives <b>does not</b> follow <i>Via Sanguinis</i>. Just as the modern Paths are simplifications of the Roads to fit the Sabbat's agenda in most cases, the <i>Path of Blood</i> is a hyper-focused version of the Road to sharpen the Web's zealotry. It strips the Path from almost every mention to honor, which was the core tenet, and doubles down on destruction and Diablerie, which were secondary. It also substitutes mentions to honor and worth for &quot;enemies&quot; and &quot;Path followers&quot;, which makes a far more evident &quot;we against the world&quot; mentality.<br /> <br /> Also worth of noting, the Road does not forbid teaching about Haqim or whatever else to people outside the clan, or require that your expectations of Honor on others be equal to your own notion of honor. As long as you're able to consider the other honorable, they're good, which is great when you need to be a part of a greater society. The Path actually commands the teaching of the Path, reserving death to those who reject it (which only makes them insufferable evangelists and even more dangerous to clan mates).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">which is the fact the Ashirra are officially all Muslims but most of them are just paying lip service to the religion of Allah.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not required to be of any particular religion. The Ashirra requires <i><b>the sect itself and its Domains</b></i> to heed Islamic Law, which is a very distinct matter (even because the overzealous interpretations of it we frequently see today are just one possibility within it). It is basically their equivalent to the Camarilla's Traditions.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking, not being Faithful is barely a concern within the Quran, and for political reasons the Ashirra does not enforce other texts as a part of its tenets. Islamic law extends more rights to the Faithful than to infidels, but it does not forbids from equating those rights and the Ashirra does that, at least as far as mortals go. What is undoubtedly criminal within this law is to actively work towards deviating the Faithful from the Faith (not even demanding non-Islamic laws is a problem in itself if you don't try to convert Muslims out of it, lobbying for Quran-abiding legal reform is their obligation, not yours).<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, it has always been said that most Ashirra members are irreligious at best after a time, and young members are more common to hold to their previous faiths for a time. It is also the Sect where Blood Cults are rarer because mortal religions adapt better to it when you feel the need, specially when you consider that Christianity is rarer among them and both Islam and Judaism are easier on Kindred (you may be cursed, but you're not Damned on those).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also like the idea that the Banu Haqim LET themselves be cursed by the Tremere to make Kindred vitae poisonous to them because they wanted to get rid of their vitae addiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>While non-canonical, I really like this idea. It makes a lot of sense for everyone within the clan BUT the Web of Knives. That would also justify why the Web so desperately demands the Sorcerers to find relief from it, but they haven't found anything (they actually could, but that would only make the Web even more dangerous, as demonstrated in the <i>Revised</i> metaplot).<br /> <br /> If there's a curse that always made more sense to me for the Sorcerers to be working on, it is the Baali Curse, not the Tremere one, that is, all things considered, not that big of a deal, specially after they developed <b><i>From Marduk's Throat</i></b> (seriously, that ritual is gold. On the long run it is better than Diablerie for it purpose).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This probably because Ur-shulgi finds monotheism silly (even if Haqim was himself religious) and my suspicion that Haqim is actually a Baali. This gets soft retconned by BDJ into being fear of the Web of Knives now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ur-Shulgi finds the devotion to anything but Haqim abhorrent, not only monotheism, and his substitution by the Web is just partial, the Web was always far more in-tune with his ideas. It is also worth of note that other Methuselah who knew Haqim consider him bat-shit crazy for thinking Haqim would approve of anything like what he's doing, but Ur-Shulgi has always been crazy and unhealthily loyal to the person of Haqim instead of any idea he defended.<br /> <br /> Soft-retconning was a means to let on the hands of the ST if Ur-Shulgi would awaken or not, but otherwise it makes little difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the HUGE IRONY of all this is the Schismatics have won their war against the Web of Knives primarily because of the Sabbat and have spent the past 20 years sitting pretty in the Ivory Tower.</div> </div> </div> </div>They won far before this, seriously.<br /> <br /> What happens is that even in <i>Revised</i> it was clear that the Loyalists were actually the minority (if a very big minority) and considered as deluded in their beliefs by the others and detrimental not only to the clan's existence or power, but actually to their purpose. The Schismatics are the bigger faction (although they may have been rendered smaller by the purge at the ST's discretion), have more resources, and are <b>actually leaving Allamut out of loyalty to Haqim's purpose for them</b>.<br /> <br /> So the true irony is that it is less that the Schismatics left the Banu Haqim and more that the Banu Haqim left the &quot;loyalists&quot; to rot in the palace they occupied. Other than that, there was no war, just a bunch of terrorists whose destiny was sealed due to their lack of competence at being functional and the Sabbat just hasted the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486591#post1486591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe MyWifeIsScary is referring to the fact that he believes a lot of religions, particularly Islam, cannot reasonably be adapted to vampire life so any Muslim vampire is fooling itself. I actually agree with him on this but pointed out the same applied to Christianity or any ethical person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Although I disagree.<br /> <br /> Ethics is a complex thing. And unless you consider the almost entirety of Humanity as monsters, we're not as better than a vampire would have to be than it seems at first. We cause a lot of impact on the planet and on other humans even when just attending to our basic needs. We are predators ourselves, just with the ability to elaborate complex belief and logistic systems to put on a facade of not needing death and suffering to survive and thrive. Yet we <b>can</b> be ethical about it. We can acknowledge our impact and do something to lessen it, we can question our needs and strive to better ourselves, we can find ways to detect and reduce the suffering we cause even if eliminating it isn't feasible.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a blight upon the world because that's a game convention and a trope. And it is accepted because most people either find the trope appealing or just can't stand something that does to us what we do to others (including other human beings we just chose to pretend they don't exist as long as we don't specifically know about them). A vampire that is mindful of its own needs, but also the need to lessen the impact of their fulfillment, is just as ethical as a human can be. And just as capable of being a good person despite also being our predator. Even capable of leaving a net positive mark upon society. It won't cease to be a predator and cause some harm, but that's not necessarily the point unless <b>you</b> want to make ot the point.<br /> <br /> On the matter of following particular religions, it is a striking misunderstanding of non-Christian religions. A lot of the things Christians think to be common threads among religions are no such a thing. Islam in particular not only <b>can</b> have inhuman creatures that prey upon Humanity in some form among the Faithful. It <b>does</b>. There are spiritual beings in Islamic Faith that may be harmful to humans and still are every bit as Faithful as one can be, and in fact expressing the Faith is considered a protection because it shows the entity you're a fellow Muslim and protected under the law. Neither Islam nor Judaism have the notion of Damnation, eternal or otherwise, that Christianity has (and that came from reinterpretations on Plato, not from the Middle East). Almost no religion has it, actually.<br /> <br /> The go-to pagan religion for Christians to show that others are just like them is &quot;Norse Polytheism&quot;, because it's easy to show as having the same themes in some form. But you know why? <b>Because we only have Christian texts on Norse Mythology</b>. It was not a written religion, and most of our knowledge of it comes from the Eddas, two books written already two centuries within official complete Christianization of Iceland, based upon fragmentary stories passed down mostly by already Christian storytellers, and put together in a reconstruction effort by Christian authors. The first and most complete, by the way, by a poet, historian and politician whose main goals were the construction of a mythic origin for the Scandinavian royal families and the establishment of a book that would be very didactic on the characteristics of the hardest traditional poetic styles of Iceland.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486602#post1486602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is entirely at my table but one of the big &quot;reforms' of the Camarilla at the Convention of Thorns was guaranteeing right of free movement actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as just movement goes, this is not your table. This is official Camarilla interpretation of the Traditions according to the core books.<br /> <br /> Even if you deny residence to a vampire, you must follow hospitality to anyone who present themselves and give them &quot;reasonable&quot; time to leave, which is at the very least until the next night and usually a few more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486608#post1486608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have trouble understanding such things nowadays because now we have nation-states, so for example, the governor of Bavaria wont rebel against the government over Berlin, nor will the governor of California rebel against Washington.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have no problem understanding it nowadays, just in the last two years we had clear rebellion from California against Trump in the exact manner you describe, and of Pernambuco and Bras\u00edlia against Bolsonaro, among others that happened on both countries. The problem isn't that.<br /> <br /> The problem with this particular tangent is that a lot of people chose their words very badly and most are currently attacking the most extreme interpretations of a position instead of the espoused position, because those extreme positions popped out at some point. The whole tangent started with MWIS stating that <b><u>most</u></b> cities would <b><u>ban</u></b> the Banu Haqin altogether, blatantly ignoring the setting without admitting it at the time. And then CTPhipps stating some posts later that Justicars can bulldoze Princes in a regular basis. Everyone is currently arguing against <u>those</u> positions and assuming then on the others, and that includes you.<br /> <br /> No one but MWIS think the Princes can just ignore Sect-wide policy completely (when this policy doesn't even exists without them, mind you), and no one but Phipps think Justicars will pop in Domains willy-nilly to publicly execute Princes in the name of the Inner Circle, and even them stopped making those claims about now (but you can go back on the first 3 pages of the thread to see the shit-storm forming).<br /> <br /> <b>Banning</b> a clan is different from never accepting people from that clan, because it infers you're throwing subtlety out of the window and making it clear you won't give them a chance, won't pretend they're welcome and maybe won't even grant them full passage rights, all those being things that are either not rights given in the Traditions or are arguably against the Traditions (as the Tradition of Hospitality may be interpreted as you still having to give right of passage and a short stay to those who abide to the law). Subtly not accepting them is another thing, although doing so in bulk (as MWIS directly stated originally) <b>would</b> be a problem the Camarilla would have to address (if it is just some scattered cases no one cares). The Inner Circle moving against any and every Prince as if they were all irrelevant and replaceable employees is too obvious BS to be argued against seriously.<br /> <br /> And for whatever it is worth, Mithras is <b>not</b> an example of anything. He was explicitly not a member of the Camarilla precisely so he could run his fief however he saw fit (including, you know, ban clans outright, including the Tremere, but curiously never the Banu Haqim).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486619#post1486619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC The WoK was a relatively modern invention right? Otherwise it would've taken over long ago. The WoK does not have a monopoly on the Path of Blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Founded 1102 CE, but still had conservative Embrace criteria until the First Gulf War in 1990, so their direct numbers only surged up very recently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486619#post1486619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure I read somewhere that the warriors have <i>always </i>been the most numerous caste since they clan has always had more soldiers to pull from while scholars and mages who can adapt to vampire living are few, so warriors have been outnumbering the other two casts together even in the best of times.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are and I described so, it is just that the difference only goes so far.<br /> <br /> Precisely speaking, the Warriors are the biggest faction and probably outnumber the other two together, but the Viziers are directly stated to be about a third of the whole clan, so that's a hard ceiling on how big the Warriors can be. And that's in V20, with their numbers swelled by the recent Gulf War and Afghanistan and Iraq Wars &quot;mass&quot; Embraces.<br /> <br /> So at most they're about 65% of the clan (assuming barely 1% or less Sorcerers), probably less, and less than absolute majority is an option (if the Sorcerers are more than half the Viziers, then the Warriors are less than 50% total. Not saying that's the case, just that it is a valid interpretation within the canon).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486619#post1486619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> The WoK had plenty of allies among other warriors</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but relative. While they have some support and considerable influence among the other Warriors (and even some among other castes), it's hard to parse the exact extent of it, both in terms of how many are actual supporters and how far even those go. While it should be expected that more than half the Warriors show a general support for the WoK even before their numbers increase, the exact details are up to the ST, including interpreting how they would react to the actual events of the Schism.<br /> <br /> Add to this that the Warriors are <b>also</b> the ones that follow Islam the most, despite the Caliph's disgust over this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486619#post1486619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you really<i> have</i> to do this, especially as different editions contradict one another, with retcons often being for the worse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't because I don't have to know every contradicting version to reach a conclusion I'm comfortable which, nor will this result in a secretly finding a decisive and objectively true version of them. Knowing the broad strokes of it and that the contradictions exist is more than enough to know most of the ways they can be interpreted.<br /> <br /> Who's adamant about interpreting them in a definitive way and shitting on everyone else's ideas about how they could be within the given lore is you, not me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486621#post1486621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, and also that bloodline that needs to EAT the mortals in order to feed, what's their name again? I largelly ignore them, which is why I dont remember their name, but those are walking masquerade violations, so yeah, those are the two exceptions for the Camarilla, marked as &quot;terminate on sight&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nagaraja, and they were changed to have to consume Blood <i>and</i> flesh, but not necessarily human flesh, just fresh, raw flesh, and it can come from a corpse not drained by them too. So while not easy to handle if you decide it must be human, not an insurmountable challenge Masquerade-wise. It can come from preserved corpses (not embalmed, but ritually preserved or simply refrigerated is enough) or from living people that will remain living (tasty surgery leftovers, anyone?).<br /> <br /> Very technically a Baali could give up on infernalism (or not have taken up to it to begin with), but I doubt anyone would take chances with them. Yet, if one is has the guts to arrive at a Camarilla Domain and present themselves honestly, it would at least be funny to see the faces of the Prince as they decide how to deal with such impudence. Probably would be accepted as a temporary guest as the law demands and then murdered in secret and missed by no one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486623#post1486623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing it back to the main topic: While Warriors were mostly Loyalist and Viziers mostly Schismatic, canonically the Sorcerers were an even split. One could even reason that they might be more likely to go loyalist: Modern religion isn't good for Dur-An-Ki practitioners, and the rise of a great master like Ur-Shulgi will be a great boon for the Sorcerer caste both politically and knowledge wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main point for the Camarilla is that mostly Warrior Schismatic didn't went to the Camarilla, to the point that it is directly stated that <i>in the Camarilla</i> the Warriors are the smallest caste, implied to be by a significant margin (and that assumption has been consistent since the Schism became a thing). So whatever happened in the middle, this is the canon result. But the majority in the Cam are Viziers, that's not even in question.<br /> <br /> Curiously in the Sabbat the Warriors did a curious exchange. First the <i>Antitribu</i> went back to Alamut because their goal had always been to get rid of the Curse by slaying Tremere, the Curse is gone and they're loyal to the WoK. Then the Schismatics came because they want war against Alamut and Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486652#post1486652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal view is the Sorcerers would split in large part because Al-Ashrad, Ur-Shulgi's only known child and the leader of the Assamite Sorcerer caste, is a Schismatic.<br /> <br /> Probably because Al-Ashrad knows Ur-Shulgi is a Baali.</div> </div> </div> </div>Al-Ashrad is extremely respected among the Sorcerers (and even the Viziers), the creator of <b><i>From Marduk's Throat</i></b>, and not only <i>a</i> Schismatic, but one of their leaders. Also a Methuselah who personally knew Haqim and that has been with the clan and leading the Caste for thousands of years, while Ur-Shulgi is an old myth virtually no one met before, effectively a newcomer to most of them, like, almost all of them.<br /> <br /> Not sure if he is a Baali, though, but that wouldn't change a thing, Al-Ashrad doesn't need to know Ur-Shulgi is a Baali, he knows Ur-Shulgi is a crazy jerk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T13:58:51-07:00","id":1486670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if you deny residence to a vampire, you must follow hospitality to anyone who present themselves and give them &quot;reasonable&quot; time to leave, which is at the very least until the next night and usually a few more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's this elaboration, I haven't seen it. (To an extent it sounds reasonable, but a few nights can do a lot of damage)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem with this particular tangent is that a lot of people chose their words very badly and most are currently attacking the most extreme interpretations of a position instead of the espoused position, because those extreme positions popped out at some point. The whole tangent started with MWIS stating that <b><u>most</u></b> cities would <b><u>ban</u></b> the Banu Haqin altogether, blatantly ignoring the setting without admitting it at the time. And then CTPhipps stating some posts later that Justicars can bulldoze Princes in a regular basis. Everyone is currently arguing against <u>those</u> positions and assuming then on the others, and that includes you.<br /> <br /> No one but MWIS think the Princes can just ignore Sect-wide policy completely (when this policy doesn't even exists without them, mind you), and no one but Phipps think Justicars will pop in Domains willy-nilly to publicly execute Princes in the name of the Inner Circle, and even them stopped making those claims about now (but you can go back on the first 3 pages of the thread to see the shit-storm forming).<br /> <br /> <b>Banning</b> a clan... </div> </div> </div>Did I say such a thing? Maybe I got hyperbolic, I did humour it at some point but I thought I made it clear that I thought outright banning Assamites was unlikely. The prince is going to need to be held hostage for that (Which the Tremere might do)<br /> <br /> -I think many or most cities will discourage and have individuals target Assamites with a good deal of political tact. Outright declaring &quot;No Assamites&quot; will be a rare thing.<br /> -I am very skeptical towards the idea that Assamites in the inner circle=sect wide mandate to accept Assamites everywhere. The unity just isn't going to be there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Precisely speaking, the Warriors are the biggest faction and probably outnumber the other two together, but the Viziers are directly stated to be about a third of the whole clan, so that's a hard ceiling on how big the Warriors can be. And that's in V20, with their numbers swelled by the recent Gulf War and Afghanistan and Iraq Wars &quot;mass&quot; Embraces.<br /> <br /> So at most they're about 65% of the clan (assuming barely 1% or less Sorcerers), probably less, and less than absolute majority is an option (if the Sorcerers are more than half the Viziers, then the Warriors are less than 50% total. Not saying that's the case, just that it is a valid interpretation within the canon). </div> </div> </div>Pedantic note but &quot;about a third&quot; doesn't necessarily mean 33%, it could just as well mean 29%. Furthermore &quot;Mass&quot; embraces during the wars could just as well be to replace loses rather than a sudden numbers boost. Though it would be a great opportunity for more reactionary elements to take the lead on new recruits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main point for the Camarilla is that mostly Warrior Schismatic didn't went to the Camarilla, to the point that it is directly stated that <i>in the Camarilla</i> the Warriors are the smallest caste, implied to be by a significant margin (and that assumption has been consistent since the Schism became a thing). So whatever happened in the middle, this is the canon result. But the majority in the Cam are Viziers, that's not even in question. </div> </div> </div>Of course<br /> But outsiders are largely ignorant of caste divides and warriors and viziers don't need to do much in order to be confused for the other.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T15:35:58-07:00","id":1486687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's this elaboration, I haven't seen it. (To an extent it sounds reasonable, but a few nights can do a lot of damage)</div> </div> </div> </div>Too much time ago, I'm not going after it now, sorry (for real, I should and I know that).<br /> <br /> Details may be wrong, of course, but then it is a vague thing one way or another. The important thing is just that the Prince has to make at least a token effort, which sometimes is enough of a deterrent for more obnoxious behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did I say such a thing? Maybe I got hyperbolic, I did humour it at some point but I thought I made it clear that I thought outright banning Assamites was unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than half of this discussion is we being to adamant to deconstruct what was actually hyperbole, sometimes by construing new hyperbole.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I think many or most cities will discourage and have individuals target Assamites with a good deal of political tact. Outright declaring &quot;No Assamites&quot; will be a rare thing.<br /> -I am very skeptical towards the idea that Assamites in the inner circle=sect wide mandate to accept Assamites everywhere. The unity just isn't going to be there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone here really thought there would be a sect-wide policy of including them everywhere (and that would be anything between weird and outright creepy). It is also good to mention that Viziers usually have a good deal of political tact (it is hinted that a number of Toreador, even Harpies, are already &quot;infiltrated&quot; Viziers anyways).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pedantic note but &quot;about a third&quot; doesn't necessarily mean 33%, it could just as well mean 29%.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, indeed. Accounting for that I'd say that about 70% would be an acceptable ceiling for Warrior numbers, more than that becomes really weird with the information given. 45% is as good as a floor for anyone wanting to downplay them instead, anything in between is acceptable within the given canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Furthermore &quot;Mass&quot; embraces during the wars could just as well be to replace loses rather than a sudden numbers boost. Though it would be a great opportunity for more reactionary elements to take the lead on new recruits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is specifically explained that it was an experiment on huge numbers of Embraces at the same time that did swelled their numbers significantly, and got repeated in the Afghanistan and Iraq wars with those Gulf War vampires being now among the sires and/or teachers. So that's not a conclusion, but a V20 <i>Lore of the Clans</i> introduction.<br /> <br /> Not going to confirm right now, but IIRC the Clanbook already stated the WoK as a relative minority in direct numbers, despite counting with a significant political influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486670#post1486670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But outsiders are largely ignorant of caste divides and warriors and viziers don't need to do much in order to be confused for the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that was mostly to address why they're relevant for the thread's topic.<br /> <br /> Regardless of how common the Sorcerers were on Alamut, in the Camarilla they're the second most common caste. That implicates a high enough number for them to not be considered a complete snowflake (those are the Warriors). From this each ST take what they will.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T16:51:20-07:00","id":1486698,"title":"","content":"I think Beckett's Jyhad Diary's take on it is fairly good and small samples of books are okay to share:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As the Final Nights approach, each of the Clans<br /> struggle with the signs of Gehenna in their own way,<br /> but the Assamites perhaps the most. Known to the<br /> Camarilla for centuries as a Clan of bloodthirsty assassins,<br /> the Assamites have always been more complex<br /> than most knew, but their diversity has been<br /> hidden away for centuries due to the machinations<br /> of the warrior-led death cult known as the Web of<br /> Knives. </div> </div> </div>The book also states the &quot;majority&quot; of the clan was held hostage by the Web of Knives which is apparently a minority even if a large chunk of the Warriors follows it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That faction, which venerates a vision of<br /> Haqim as a blood god who desires the extermination<br /> of all other Kindred, has ruled the Clan of Silence<br /> for centuries, presenting an image of Clan Assamite<br /> as a family of assassins obsessed with diablerie.<br /> <br /> Of course, that image was itself the product of centuries<br /> spent under a blood-curse inflicted on them by<br /> the Baali during the nights of the Roman Empire, a<br /> blood-curse unwittingly neutralized by the Camarilla<br /> when the Tremere Clan placed all Assamites under<br /> a newer and more potent curse with the Treaty of<br /> Tyre. Denied the chance for regular diablerie, the<br /> Web of Knives turned to contract assassination in<br /> exchange for vitae, leaving the Viziers and the Sorcerers<br /> to their own devices. </div> </div> </div>It's notably the Web of Knives that was 2nd Edition Assamites in all of their crazy Klingons meets Assassins Creed orientalist glory. I admit to being kind of iffy about this because it still says there is a bunch of Muslim zealot genocidal terrorists with a bizarre honor code out there but it recontextualizes them in a way that doesn't wholly tear apart canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This state of affairs continued until a seer predicted<br /> the rise of Ur-Shulgi, a Methuselah of unimaginable<br /> power who sought to lead a culling of<br /> the Assamites. Galvanized into action, Tegyrius, the<br /> leader of the Viziers, and the Amr fashioned a conspiracy<br /> of Viziers, Sorcerers, and moderate Warriors<br /> wishing to defect from the main Clan in the event<br /> of Ur-Shulgi\u2019s rise. </div> </div> </div>This makes Al-Ashrad to be the mind behind it while Tegyrius is more of the spokesmen. It's notable both of these guys are 2000+ year old vampires who don't appear to suffer the Beckoning. The Vermillion Wedding is kind of fascinating because it depends on a massively powerful Methuselah being married to a reasonably powerful Elder. You have to wonder if Victoria Ash thought this through or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic by Other Means: The Tremere Inner<br /> Circle is livid at the prospect of a bloodline as magically<br /> puissant as the Assamite Sorcerers gaining<br /> admittance to the Camarilla and threatening their<br /> occult monopoly. Local chantries do whatever they<br /> can to make Assamite refugees feel unwelcome while<br /> Princes who disdain the Tremere welcome the newcomers<br /> as a magical counterweight. Kindred of any<br /> Clans not gifted at sorcery get caught in the middle. </div> </div> </div>So we really have the canonical answer here that the Pyramid doesn't want the Assamites joining but they can't stop it and plenty of anti-Tremere Princes are willing to open their doors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-16-2022, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T22:22:59-07:00","id":1486716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have no problem understanding it nowadays, just in the last two years we had clear rebellion from California against Trump in the exact manner you describe, and of Pernambuco and Bras\u00edlia against Bolsonaro, among others that happened on both countries. The problem isn't that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol that brough me some good laughs hahahaha<br /> <br /> In neither case there was a &quot;rebellion&quot; - althought I do agree that in the US there have been violent protest which included murders and the arsoning of several cities. In Brazil however the &quot;protests&quot; against Bolsonaro couldnt even fill a bank line. There have been massive spontaneous demonstrations in favor of the president thou; it's easier to have a demonstration against the left thou - the ones in 2014 against the leftist government of Dilma gathered MILLIONS. But they werent violent thou, such as the protests against Trump.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, none of those constituted &quot;rebellions&quot;, not even close hahahaha but thanks for the laughs.<br /> <br /> Also, the politics behind modern countries in no way ressembles the politics of the Camarilla - which was the point I was making to begin with. The US, Brazil and any other modern countries have strict governmental hierarquies; they dont have independent or even semi independent sub-divisions within their territories. Which is why the thing that most closely ressambles the Camarilla in the modern world would be the EU, which isnt a true state, thus the nation states within the EU can defy the authority in Bruxels - as they do time and again.<br /> <br /> The other historic examples are those I already stated: Japanese Shogunate, the HRE, the Polish Lithuanian Common Wealth, even the Northern German Federation (just initially that is), the Byzantine Empire and pretty much any feudal state.<br /> <br /> Countries like Brazil or the US dont even come close, nor any other modern country which are either fully democratic or autocratic and centralized.<br /> <br /> And no, we are NOT used to such a concept - which is why someone would come with the hilarious idea of comparing feudal systems to protests of civilians on democratic states hahahaha<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this particular tangent is that a lot of people chose their words very badly and most are currently attacking the most extreme interpretations of a position instead of the espoused position, because those extreme positions popped out at some point. The whole tangent started with MWIS stating that most cities would ban the Banu Haqin altogether, blatantly ignoring the setting without admitting it at the time. And then CTPhipps stating some posts later that Justicars can bulldoze Princes in a regular basis. Everyone is currently arguing against those positions and assuming then on the others, and <b>that includes you.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>If you had paid attention to what I wrote, you would see that I was difusing the situation and staying in a compromising middle ground, by trying to demonstrate how the Inner Circle's position aint that of a Sun Emperor commanding from high above, but neither that Princes are completely autonomous. The reason why this is actually hard to understand is precisely because it's a complex issue with no clear cut answer; there's no black and white yes or no answer - and that's what I was saying all along. It's all politics, so there's no &quot;the Inner Circle ordered X&quot; or &quot;the Princes demand Y&quot;, because everything turns into politics, and backrooms deals and concesions, compromises and agreements; so it's important to understand what ISNT before getting a picture of what IS. Princes CAN - <i>in theory</i> - do whatever they please. In practice thou, it doesnt work that way. And the Inner Circle again, in theory, cannot interfere on the <i>&quot;princedoms&quot;</i> except when the Camarilla's Lex is being disregarded. In between those two extremes that exist on paper only, comes a ton of politics that puts things on a middle ground, which is why both propositions of Justicars turning Princes into cinders by the dozens just by criticizing Hardestads hair cut as having Princes screaming that X clan are &quot;scum&quot; like a spoiled child, both are ridiculous propositions that would NEVER happen.<br /> <br /> So, I guess that the one who's assuming my position is you, and you're just projecting this on me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one but MWIS think the Princes can just ignore Sect-wide policy completely (when this policy doesn't even exists without them, mind you), and no one but Phipps think Justicars will pop in Domains willy-nilly to publicly execute Princes in the name of the Inner Circle, and even them stopped making those claims about now (but you can go back on the first 3 pages of the thread to see the shit-storm forming).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is just simply not true. AnubisXY claimed clearly that &quot;some Princes could be made an example of&quot;. And there were others making statements that, while not so blatantly extreme, would go in the same vein. Check out previous posts, or I could point those out for you.<br /> <br /> PS: by the way, nothing wrong with anybody that thinks A or B - that's why we're having this discussion to begin with; that's how we can all change our misconceptions after all. I dont agree with CTTPhips-something or AnubisXY or with Mywifeis-something, and we all share our views and try to convince one another, and maybe by the end of it we get a better reformulated idea that improves our games. That's the reason for such forums after all. I just hope I've managed to form a solid case for my own point of view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Banning a clan is different from never accepting people from that clan, because it infers you're throwing subtlety out of the window and making it clear you won't give them a chance, won't pretend they're welcome and maybe won't even grant them full passage rights, all those being things that are either not rights given in the Traditions or are arguably against the Traditions (as the Tradition of Hospitality may be interpreted as you still having to give right of passage and a short stay to those who abide to the law). Subtly not accepting them is another thing, although doing so in bulk (as MWIS directly stated originally) would be a problem the Camarilla would have to address (if it is just some scattered cases no one cares). The Inner Circle moving against any and every Prince as if they were all irrelevant and replaceable employees is too obvious BS to be argued against seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did previously stated that it would be ridiculous for a Prince to scream out loud with full lungs &quot;Those bastard Brujah/Ventrue/Toreador/Nosf (etc etc) are the scum of the Earth, and I'd rather suffer being devoured by my own children or sire than suffering a single one in my city!&quot;. So, perhaps I wasnt clear before, but let me be clear now: such a cartoonish extremism would NEVER happen; NEVER would such an idiotic person become a Prince to begin with.<br /> <br /> The answer, once again, is a complex middle ground in the in-between, that comes after a lot of political come and go. Some Princedoms will get away with keeping X clan out while still keeping a welcome face, while others will have to bulge in to the external pression.<br /> <br /> This means that, sometimes the inner circle manages to have their way, sometimes it doesnt, and the game continues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486661#post1486661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for whatever it is worth, Mithras is not an example of anything. He was explicitly not a member of the Camarilla precisely so he could run his fief however he saw fit (including, you know, ban clans outright, including the Tremere, but curiously never the Banu Haqim).</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont recall having used Mithras as an example. Check my previous posts and you'll see that my example was another entirely. Clearly you are mistaking my words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T22:42:37-07:00","id":1486719,"title":"","content":"But as much as everyone outside the Tremere hate the Tremere how many of them can actually afford to be Anti-Tremere, a clan that wracks in favours like they're hotcakes, and one of the few clans organized enough to call in heavy hitters from outside the city without much difficulty (Assamites could do this, but it wouldn't be good for them at this stage). In most cases, a prince who sides with Assamites over Tremere is just going to be replaced. Millenia of ill-will with the Assamites haven't done much to improve the situation. <br /> <br /> As of 2022, I'd guess that at least 80% of cities either haven't had assamites approach them, or have had significant movement towards supressing them. In about 15%, we have fair two-sided competition / reasonable agreements / the Tremere were never present, and in 5%, we have Assamites gaining a better possition than Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T23:08:36-07:00","id":1486722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486719#post1486719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as much as everyone outside the Tremere hate the Tremere how many of them can actually afford to be Anti-Tremere, a clan that wracks in favours like they're hotcakes, and one of the few clans organized enough to call in heavy hitters from outside the city without much difficulty (Assamites could do this, but it wouldn't be good for them at this stage). In most cases, a prince who sides with Assamites over Tremere is just going to be replaced. Millenia of ill-will with the Assamites haven't done much to improve the situation. <br /> <br /> As of 2022, I'd guess that at least 80% of cities either haven't had assamites approach them, or have had significant movement towards supressing them. In about 15%, we have fair two-sided competition / reasonable agreements / the Tremere were never present, and in 5%, we have Assamites gaining a better possition than Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... The Tremere are NOT the biggest movers inside the Camarilla. The <b>Ventrue</b> are. And the Ventrue have been for a long time waging a fierce competition to reduce Tremere influence inside the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> As for &quot;big hitters&quot;, please, it doesnt work that way. That's again the same absurd proposition of Justicars running amok creating mayhem among Princes. A few hits here and there, sure, all clans do that on a regular basis. But it's the Ventrue that calls most of the shots - dont forget that. And for the Ventrue - who are the most pragmatic of the clans - the Assamites come as a bless, new pawns to help counter Tremere influence.<br /> <br /> No, there will be no mass assassinations perpetrated by &quot;big hitters&quot; among the Tremere. Too risky for too little. Last thing the Tremere needs is to have the Camarilla kicking them out and hunting them. And by the way, the Ventrue are united too you know. And again, they are MORE powerful than the Tremere.<br /> <br /> What will happen is what ALWAYS happens: lots of bickering, backdoors deals, backstabbings and lots of shadow politics and fierce competition.<br /> <br /> Now, the subject of city presence will be a case by case scenario; even a few cities with a Tremere Prince may end up having a few Assamites - rare, but not impossible.<br /> <br /> And, while the Tremere will obviously make this assimilation harder, they cant stop it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-16T23:45:58-07:00","id":1486724,"title":"","content":"The Ventrue aren't waging a fierce competition against the Tremere. They have their reservations, they have some conflicts, but It hasn't been described as &quot;fierce competition&quot;. That, and Ventrue modus operandi has always been about risk aversion and going with &quot;old reliable&quot; rather than &quot;new and ambitious&quot; ; the Ventrue and Tremere share the same bed and in most places it'll take more than the appearance of assamites for the relationship to end. <br /> <br /> I didn't mean &quot;justicar&quot; level. <br /> Above the Regent, there's a lord, then there's a pointifex. Not to mention there are various strong and dangerous Tremere who remain as apprentices. But in any case the Tremere are a clan-first organization and they have the ability to look after another member's holdings while he goes to City B to help Chantry B. Others can do this, but none quite so readily as the Tremere. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:26:37-07:00","id":1486727,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No personal attacks and ridiculing other posters. We should also keep RL politics relevant to examples only here. More and the thread will shut down.<br /> <br /> If you have a problem with other posters, please report them than try to correct their behavior yourself.<br /> <br /> That is all.</span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:30:08-07:00","id":1486729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486724#post1486724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ventrue aren't waging a fierce competition against the Tremere. They have their reservations, they have some conflicts, but It hasn't been described as &amp;quot;fierce competition&amp;quot;. That, and Ventrue modus operandi has always been about risk aversion and going with &amp;quot;old reliable&amp;quot; rather than &amp;quot;new and ambitious&amp;quot; ; the Ventrue and Tremere share the same bed and in most places it'll take more than the appearance of assamites for the relationship to end. <br /> <br /> I didn't mean &amp;quot;justicar&amp;quot; level. <br /> Above the Regent, there's a lord, then there's a pointifex. Not to mention there are various strong and dangerous Tremere who remain as apprentices. But in any case the Tremere are a clan-first organization and they have the ability to look after another member's holdings while he goes to City B to help Chantry B. Others can do this, but none quite so readily as the Tremere. <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Ventrue are master manipulators. Sure they share businesses with the Tremere. But they also compete for influence inside the sect.<br /> <br /> Now, when I said &quot;compete&quot; it seems that you infered &quot;conflict&quot;; that's not the case (no more than normal cainite general untrustworthy backstabbing there is). <br /> <br /> Just think about it: who inside the Camarilla have the power and will to compete with the Ventrue? The Nosferatu are a powerhouse, but they cant interact in the world as other vampires do. The Brujah are perhaps the most disunited of all the clans - at least inside the Camarilla. The Toreador lack the will and the focus to do it - and for the most part are content with being under the thumb of the Ventrue. The Gangrel werent real contenders even when they were officially in. And there's one more clan that... Goes without mentioning.<br /> <br /> That leaves only the Tremere as the Ventrue main &quot;frenemies&quot;.<br /> <br /> You do know that a lot of the anti Tremere propaganda inside the Camarilla comes from the Ventrue, right? They actively seek to undermine the Tremere position without alienating the clan.<br /> <br /> You may think of it as the relation US-China up to 2010... Yes yes, we are <i>friends</i>, of course we are, we are all good pals...<br /> <br /> I think you may be a little biased towards the position of the Tremere inside the Camarilla. Once again, this is a highly complicated issue with no clear cut answer. Now, obviously absolutely a massive amount of ZERO Ventrues will ever say &quot;no, we are gonna accept Assamites in our city because we dont trust the Tremere, we want to reduce their influence in the sect so that we can increase our own, and we want to break Tremere's monopoly on blood magic&quot;. Absolutely no Ventrue EVER will say any such nonsense. What they'll do is say that &quot;in the spirit of fraternity upon which we are all bound, and as a gesture of goodwill towards both our guests and the Camarilla's collective decision, we have decided to harbor a few Assamites in our prosperous city!&quot;. And the local Tremere residents will smile and cheer on behalf of the &quot;fraternity&quot;, all the while boiling on the inside, and planning what sorts of malevolent rumors they may concoct to spread upon the right ears.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Nosfs are right up there backing the Ventrue on that one, because they too see the benefits of reducing Tremere influence, and will be attentive to the Tremere's machinations.<br /> <br /> The way you frame it seems to imply that the Tremere basically have the Camarilla by the balls, which simply isnt true.<br /> <br /> The Assamites will throw their lots with the elders of the Camarilla, and wont stay idle either. The best the Tremere can do is try to call some favors, use their influence and manipulate local social landscapes. The idea of them engaging into what would basically be an open but covert war to purge the Assamites is ludicrous. All it would take to spell their ruin would be one Nosf with a big mouth. So, the math says no.<br /> <br /> And, like I said, this is a golden opportunity for the Ventrue, too good to let it pass. And the Ventrue are the real bosses - not the Tremere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T00:40:57-07:00","id":1486732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486719#post1486719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But as much as everyone outside the Tremere hate the Tremere how many of them can actually afford to be Anti-Tremere, a clan that wracks in favours like they're hotcakes, and one of the few clans organized enough to call in heavy hitters from outside the city without much difficulty (Assamites could do this, but it wouldn't be good for them at this stage). In most cases, a prince who sides with Assamites over Tremere is just going to be replaced. Millenia of ill-will with the Assamites haven't done much to improve the situation.<br /> <br /> As of 2022, I'd guess that at least 80% of cities either haven't had assamites approach them, or have had significant movement towards supressing them. In about 15%, we have fair two-sided competition / reasonable agreements / the Tremere were never present, and in 5%, we have Assamites gaining a better possition than Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree based on how secure the Tremere would be on their power on those 80% of cities. They want the secrets of Dur-An-Ki, and while they may not be powerful enough for it to be a good idea to pressure the Banu Haqim out, they're still enough for the competition to be limited as they're still the best on business. In many of those cities they would be better taking the initiative in offering Sorcerers a hand in being accepted, and through this guarantee that those Sorcerers will be a limited competition or no competition at all. Of course, some of those could still block the Sorcerers because of local sentiments, politics, whatever, but the more powerful the Tremere are in a city, the more they can force a situation on the Sorcerers that is beneficial for the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The cities where the Tremere would face a more balanced competition, for whatever reason, are exactly the ones where they would feel the need to completely block the Sorcerers altogether, as those are the cities where they stand to lose and can't guarantee conditions of advantage to themselves. In some they may fail and have to split the business, in some they may either keep the Sorcerers at bay or achieve the upper hand through a lot of effort, and in some they may be driven away. As those are already cities where the Tremere have some problems I think it's fair to assume their own reputation weights more than the general fears about the Banu Haqim on most of those, give or take particular cases.<br /> <br /> On cities where the Tremere are weak they obviously have no means to resist the coming of the Sorcerers. But at the same time, the reason for the city to have weak or no Tremere on the first place may <b>also</b> play against the Sorcerers. Why does the Prince doesn't want Camarilla's best wizards around? The answer may have no bearing or favor the Sorcerers, but if their problem is with the magic itself, then the Sorcerers may be up to a similar situation.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not even sure if there are enough sorcerers for 50% of Camarilla's cities, even that is up to the ST. Most Banu Haqim are still Viziers and I doubt the Tremere would be successful in forbidding entrance to a caste that specializes in making both Ventrue and Toreador very happy and feeling cultured and stuff. <b>If</b> it is just the Tremere, that'll be an uphill battle that they certainly can win, but probably isn't worth the cost on most cities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T01:04:46-07:00","id":1486737,"title":"","content":"Interjecting into a subject that I rarely do, my opinion of the Tremere is the fact the Tremere have firmly ensorceled (hehe) themselves into the role of being <b>Evil Chancellors</b>. In V:TM 1st Edition, my favorite edition, the presentation of the Tremere is that they are people who have managed to find themselves a niche in the Camarilla that is very secure but also not the traditional source of power for most of them.<br /> <br /> My take on the Tremere in the Camarilla is that the Tremere hitched their wagon to the Ventrue and are their strongest supporters for the most part. In a very real way the Ivory Tower is a Trinity of the Ventrue, Tremere, and the Toreador that all get something different out of it. They also want different things.<br /> <br /> 1. The Ventrue wish to rule. They wish to have public title and power that gives them the ability to command respect from those around them.<br /> <br /> 2. The Toreador wish to socialize. Their currency is rumor, prestige, and the high society that they basically HAD TO INVENT in order to get Kindred to hang around them. The Camarilla exists in large part because the Toreador really hate having no one to play off of.<br /> <br /> 3. The Tremere, by contrast, want to have security. The Tremere really don't give a shit about having the trappings of power, they're more interested in gaining literal wizardry and command over the universe. For that, though, they need protection and financing as well as security from the rest of the world's society. As such, Tremere prop up the system so they can spend decades reading as well as experimenting. They traffic in magic and favor trading, certainly, but really their desire for respect as well as power is almost limited to their own Pyramid.<br /> <br /> A Tremere would rather have 4 points of Clan Prestige than 4 points of Status. 4 Points of Thaumaturgy than 8 points of Dominate and Auspex.<br /> <br /> My later take on Revised and Dark Ages is the Tremere supported the Camarilla because it was their chance to basically move from being something like the Baali or other &quot;renegade&quot; bloodline to something respectable.<br /> <br /> They're heavily invested in the Camarilla because the Camarilla was their original bulwark against everyone else ranging from Gargoyles to Assamites to Tzimisce to the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> A Tremere power broker would prefer to control a Prince from behind the scenes like Nicolai and Lodin than sit in the Big ChairTM itself. They'd rather be Littlefinger or Tywin than Robert or Stannis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T02:56:25-07:00","id":1486747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486737#post1486737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interjecting into a subject that I rarely do, my opinion of the Tremere is the fact the Tremere have firmly ensorceled (hehe) themselves into the role of being <b>Evil Chancellors</b>. In V:TM 1st Edition, my favorite edition, the presentation of the Tremere is that they are people who have managed to find themselves a niche in the Camarilla that is very secure but also not the traditional source of power for most of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO, the Tremere are essentially a large corperation. They want profit, they want to live comfortably, they want to be respected, they want to influence politics to give them more favourable conditions, but they only go so far: Actually administering everyone else has no merit to them, directly getting into politics is just an annoying distraction and puts an undue level of scrutiny onto their business side. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My take on the Tremere in the Camarilla is that the Tremere hitched their wagon to the Ventrue and are their strongest supporters for the most part. In a very real way the Ivory Tower is a Trinity of the Ventrue, Tremere, and the Toreador that all get something different out of it. They also want different things.. </div> </div> </div>This is not a bad take of things but I'd be weary of the idea that the Cam serves these three clans more than the other four. These three have more obvious benefits, but the others have them too<br /> -The Gangrel ironically need to push for stability and rule-of-law in order to keep their domain/prestation claims, which they would have a hard time enforcing otherwise. <br /> -the Brujah need to moderate themselves. The secular nature of the cam keeps them from going wild.<br /> -The Nosferatu need to keep themselves as an &quot;us&quot; clan rather than a &quot;them&quot; clan. <br /> - Malkavians: &quot;All of the above&quot;<br /> [quote]<br /> My later take on Revised and Dark Ages is the Tremere supported the Camarilla because it was their chance to basically move from being something like the Baali or other &quot;renegade&quot; bloodline to something respectable. [/quote[<br /> I think it was inevitable. They're too useful, too organized. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're heavily invested in the Camarilla because the Camarilla was their original bulwark against everyone else ranging from Gargoyles to Assamites to Tzimisce to the Order of Hermes. </div> </div> </div>Speaking of &quot;renegade bloodlines&quot;, that's what the non-camarilla clans are in many respects. The FoS and Giovanni play reasonably well with others but the Tzmisce,Lasombra, Assamites and Ravnos are problem children. This isn't a Tremere idea, this is something recognized everyone, including the problem children. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T06:23:03-07:00","id":1486764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486657#post1486657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that make Al-Ashrad a Baali, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's weird. The cut text from Cb:Assamite Revised that said ur-Shulgi was Baali is here: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Unpublished_text_from_Clanbook:_Assamite_Revised\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Un...samite_Revised</a><br /> <br /> It suggests ur-Shulgi was Baali, but Embraced by Haqim, and was later either re-Embraced as Assamite or had the Baali essence torn from him to make him a proper Assamite again.<br /> <br /> So he both is and isn't Baali, and his childe might be either Baali or Assamite (al-Ashrad doesn't have the trademark Assamite dark skin which is suspicious...).<br /> <br /> (This has turned into a tangent on one of my favourite parts of canon, so I apologise. Stop reading if you're not interested in Baali lore and lots of conjecture...)<br /> <br /> Essentially, the full story is this: Haqim took a shepherd boy with a soul destined to become corrupted (i.e., he likely had an inverted avatar, making him a Widderslainte), threw him into the Well of Sacrifice at the site of the First Tribe's city (Chorazin, probably), making him into a Baali in the same way Saulot created the bloodline in the first place.<br /> <br /> The boy arose as a leader around which all the Baali rallied. This made them a unified force, so they were easier to take down. Haqim arrives at the end of the war and basically turns the tide.<br /> <br /> After the Baali were defeated, Haqim tore the 'demon' from him (you could interpret this in multiple ways; since Embraced mages lose their Avatars, it seems unlikely it was that, though). <br /> <br /> Then Haqim told everyone he was forced to Embrace the 'innocent' boy to save him on the battlefield, hiding his true origin and his own role in the history of the Baali. Though this could be literal -- meaning perhaps he re-Embraced him into clan Assamite, and therefore used some form of the Baali rite of apostasy.<br /> <br /> But Sarah Schneier, the IC author of the email outlining this info, emphatically says, &quot;It is not Baali, and it is not possessed, and we do not think it is not working with or for anything infernal, but it is a case where the whole is greater than the sum of its parts, and it is not one of Haqim's Children any more, not really. It is something more, and it is something less.&quot; Which muddies things a bit (I assume the double negative is an error, meaning he isn't working with the infernal), but still seems to back up the theory that he isn't Baali anymore (or at least, isn't totally Baali).<br /> <br /> Notably, the story of the shepherd boy parallels that of the slave boy who is the first Methuselah to claim the title of Shaitan, as described in several older sourcebooks detailing the origins of the Baali (and later repeated in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook). <br /> <br /> Both ur-Shulgi and the slave boy are linked to a time in which 'the skies rained fire and wept blood' (slave boy) or 'the stones spoke and the skies cried a blood rain' (ur-Shulgi). Shaitan/the slave boy is said to have rallied the Baali together, using the title given to their mythical Antediluvian founder, and this title was later used by Nergal and Azaneal to similar ends. This matches ur-Shulgi's origin story closely.<br /> <br /> This may reconcile two of the contradictory origin stories of the Baali, where Shaitan was said to have founded the bloodline in their first appearance (the DA Companion) but later on, the bloodline was founded by three separate vampires (in Cb:Baali), all sired by Saulot (or Cappadocian, or Tzimisce, or all three of them at separate times using the same well...).<br /> <br /> It's a clever way to make all the stories mesh, while adding some suitable apocalyptic menace. And it makes the Baali a creeping threat to all the clans -- they've wormed their way into the history of every clan in one way or another, which also ties into the original history of them, where they recruited apostates from all the 13 clans to found the bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:11:22-07:00","id":1486779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486747#post1486747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of &quot;renegade bloodlines&quot;, that's what the non-camarilla clans are in many respects. The FoS and Giovanni play reasonably well with others but the Tzmisce,Lasombra, Assamites and Ravnos are problem children. This isn't a Tremere idea, this is something recognized everyone, including the problem children.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, the retcons of the Ravnos and Assamites are, &quot;They are in fact massively powerful local Clans in incredibly ancient regions that have absolutely no shits to give about the Camarilla because the only ones of their kind who interact with them are their outliers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T11:30:55-07:00","id":1486782,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong to hope that Ur-Shurgi makes no more appearances in future supplements? I don\u2019t find him all that interesting as a character in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T13:13:20-07:00","id":1486792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486764#post1486764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's weird. The cut text from Cb:Assamite Revised that said ur-Shulgi was Baali is here: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Unpublished_text_from_Clanbook:_Assamite_Revised\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Un...samite_Revised</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It must be noted that this story never made it into canon. It is <i>Word of God</i> for whatever value that has for you, but has no weight on the official lore until and if it is put into official material.<br /> <br /> But that said, I like it, and it fits nicely. It makes for a dark secret that isn't necessarily a damning secret on Haqim (he wasn't perfect and did shit, but he wasn't just corrupted, it was a desperate gamble to solve a dire problem). It explains Al-Ashrad's condition without making him into Baali himself. And in the end it makes for a better story for Ur-Shulgi without really changing him much in any way, he's still just a crazy jerk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486782#post1486782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong to hope that Ur-Shurgi makes no more appearances in future supplements? I don\u2019t find him all that interesting as a character in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>He isn't an interesting character, he just got a better backstory. In my chronicles he just got nuked in the place of the Vienna Chantry and that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T14:57:02-07:00","id":1486800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486782#post1486782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong to hope that Ur-Shurgi makes no more appearances in future supplements? I don\u2019t find him all that interesting as a character in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Hand book wrote Ur-Shulgi out of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486792#post1486792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He isn't an interesting character, he just got a better backstory. In my chronicles he just got nuked in the place of the Vienna Chantry and that's it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had the reason for the Schismatics joining the Camarilla include access to the power they had over the US military.<br /> <br /> The &quot;real&quot; Alamut wasn't in Iran but Iraq (when both were part of Persia) and got bombed under direction of the undead.<br /> <br /> This buried Ur-Shulgi and destroyed the majority of the Web of Knives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-17-2022, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:14:19-07:00","id":1486871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486779#post1486779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, the retcons of the Ravnos and Assamites are, &quot;They are in fact massively powerful local Clans in incredibly ancient regions that have absolutely no shits to give about the Camarilla because the only ones of their kind who interact with them are their outliers.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Which basically translates as &quot;we are writters from the United States, so we understand the West, thus we can imagine all the cultural movements of those fictious supernatural creatures in the western world, thus the vast majority of the cultural diversity will exist in the western world, but since there's more to the world than just that, we'll just give those ultra generic groups for those very large number of people and ahh... India gets Ravnos... Middle East gets Assamites, East Asia we wont even try, and lets call it a day&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486782#post1486782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong to hope that Ur-Shurgi makes no more appearances in future supplements? I don\u2019t find him all that interesting as a character in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Super, super fine. But, it would be good for him to show up to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-18-2022, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T06:26:51-07:00","id":1486873,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that Eastern Europe gets Tzmisce and southern Europe/America gets Lasombra because <i>Fuck Them</i>, Amrite? . Western Europe and North America just get the high-functioning &quot;normal&quot; clans, because they're normal, right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T07:03:46-07:00","id":1486878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486873#post1486873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't forget that Eastern Europe gets Tzmisce and southern Europe/America gets Lasombra because <i>Fuck Them</i>, Amrite? . Western Europe and North America just get the high-functioning &amp;quot;normal&amp;quot; clans, because they're normal, right.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's the difference between a Pole, a Romenian and a Bulgarian anyway, amirite? It's all Tzimisce and that's that!<br /> <br /> Oh, and for the sake of our sanity, let's not even try to do Russia... It's the USSR, we know nothing of the guys because it's such a closed nation so... Let us just call ALL of Russia as &quot;Baba Yaga&quot; and it's ready to print.<br /> <br /> And it's the same for the all the other splats too. European mages are hermetics, chorists, verbena, representing all the major creeds of Europe (christians, kabbalists, pagans). Also, the order of Reason, victorian culture have Etherites, modern west have the VA... And a... Oh yes, there's this annoying &quot;rest of the world&quot; thing... So, India, that massive country with hundreds of languages and thousands of different syncretic religions... Euthanatoi. China... Buddhists right? Akashics. And while we are at it, lets put all the cool &quot;kung fu shit&quot; with them. Middle East err... We already did the &quot;Islam thing&quot; with the Assamites, so lets try something a bit more &quot;1001 nights&quot;. Ahl I Batin (but they'll just be a footnote and we wont really use them). And the rest that we know even less of eh... Dreamspeaker.<br /> <br /> Right. All done now.<br /> <br /> To be fair thou, those games were done in the 90's when the internet wasnt what it is today (and at the very beggining it simply wasnt), and it's incredibly hard to try to truly grasp cultures totally different from your own, but yes, those games were made by western people for western people, so obviously they absolutely fall short for anything outside of North America - West Europe. I wouldnt expect any different, and a game that were designed in China I would find it very usual if they had made a good conception of the western world either - it would probably have all sort of &quot;poetic licenses&quot; about how they view us (probably as degenerates with no honor and no sense of tradition or respect).<br /> <br /> But this should be well understood by the writters, they should be well self aware of this intern criticism and work with it instead of against it, so simply saying &quot;oh no, you know what, the Ravnos actually are super powerful in India and just simply dont care&quot; it's extremely silly. Just own to the fact that you dont really know all too much about those cultures - which is no crime at all - and make it a little more vague. Or even ask for players help and imput - maybe ask an hindu to write about India, a chinese to write about China (instead of the terrible &quot;Kuei Jin&quot; thing) and so - if truly want to write about it at all to begin with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T15:55:59-07:00","id":1486920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486878#post1486878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldnt expect any different, and a game that were designed in China I would find it very usual if they had made a good conception of the western world either - it would probably have all sort of &quot;poetic licenses&quot; about how they view us (probably as degenerates with no honor and no sense of tradition or respect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is kind of funny because that's pretty much the opinion that the Wan Kuei have about Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T16:41:40-07:00","id":1486922,"title":"","content":"The Assamite and Ravnos corrections are basically an attempt to &quot;fix&quot; what was an orientalist depiction of them and sort of running head first into a whole other set of problems because of the same basic assumptions.<br /> <br /> 1] Assamite Revised is about turning the Assamites into basically their own mini-Camarilla. The Vizier being the Toreador, the Warriors being the Original RecipeTM Assamites, and the Sorcerers being the Tremere. This is better than them being a one-dimensional bunch of terrorists and based on the Alamut novel that inspired Assassins Creed.<br /> <br /> 2] HOWEVER, the problem is that basically is attempting to patch over the hole by missing the problem is that the entirety of the Middle East and its cultures being the Assamites is, itself, an inherently stupid idea.<br /> <br /> 3] This is basically the same issue with the Ravnos as instead of being &quot;thieving trickster illusionist&quot; Clan, they have since become &quot;India clan.&quot; Which means that it's even more stereotypical in attempting to cultivate the entire oldest culture in the world and its many-many branches.<br /> <br /> 4] Ebony Kingdoms gets this right for the most part with the idea that if you have ALL of the Clans there, then there's the more appropriate diversity you'd expect for it. That's because Ventrue aren't &quot;Western European Kindred Clan&quot;, theyr'e nobility clan, which can be anywhere.<br /> <br /> My .02.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:31:04-07:00","id":1486940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486871#post1486871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which basically translates as</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> The increase in size actually means &quot;we have this lore in the setting and now that we look back at it, it was really stupid and racist. But we can't just get rid of it, and we can't really dedicate a whole lot of books to the minutiae of a place we don't know (last time KotE happened). Also, a lot of people grew to like those things, <i>including players from those places</i>. We'll just try to make this mess less messy as best as we can.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can have an opinion on their success, but I completely disagree with the completely cynic take on the matter. Also, they eventually did a lot on the matter of increasing complexity elsewhere through the available means, which is declaring that Europe doesn't have an actual monopoly on the other clans and they exist elsewhere doing their own things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486922#post1486922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Assamite and Ravnos corrections are basically an attempt to &quot;fix&quot; what was an orientalist depiction of them and sort of running head first into a whole other set of problems because of the same basic assumptions.<br /> <br /> 1] Assamite Revised is about turning the Assamites into basically their own mini-Camarilla. The Vizier being the Toreador, the Warriors being the Original RecipeTM Assamites, and the Sorcerers being the Tremere. This is better than them being a one-dimensional bunch of terrorists and based on the Alamut novel that inspired Assassins Creed.<br /> <br /> 2] HOWEVER, the problem is that basically is attempting to patch over the hole by missing the problem is that the entirety of the Middle East and its cultures being the Assamites is, itself, an inherently stupid idea.<br /> <br /> 3] This is basically the same issue with the Ravnos as instead of being &quot;thieving trickster illusionist&quot; Clan, they have since become &quot;India clan.&quot; Which means that it's even more stereotypical in attempting to cultivate the entire oldest culture in the world and its many-many branches.<br /> <br /> 4] Ebony Kingdoms gets this right for the most part with the idea that if you have ALL of the Clans there, then there's the more appropriate diversity you'd expect for it. That's because Ventrue aren't &quot;Western European Kindred Clan&quot;, theyr'e nobility clan, which can be anywhere.<br /> <br /> My .02.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also partially repaired the problems further by introducing this same idea to other places: all the clans exist and they have their own organizations. Then we got the Ashirra and India became home to a huge society where the Ravnos were just the Ravnos (which is still better than being &quot;the filthy thieving Gipsies that call themselves Ravnos and I call Blood Hunt&quot;).<br /> <br /> V20 further distinguished being a Banu Haqim from just being Arab Vampire, while still working within the constraints of the lore. It isn't a perfect job, but it isn't an easy job to begin with. It could have been easy 31 years ago, before a single book was published with the name <i>Assamites</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T20:38:55-07:00","id":1486945,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to note the Banu Haqim have been heavily liberalized (for lack of a better term) and made more normal as part of the Camarilla, the Ravnos has been reintroduced with New York by Night, and the Kuei-Jin have been erased from existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:04:31-07:00","id":1486952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486922#post1486922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2] HOWEVER, the problem is that basically is attempting to patch over the hole by missing the problem is that the entirety of the Middle East and its cultures being the Assamites is, itself, an inherently stupid idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol, stupid doesnt even begins to describe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486922#post1486922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3] This is basically the same issue with the Ravnos as instead of being &amp;quot;thieving trickster illusionist&amp;quot; Clan, they have since become &amp;quot;India clan.&amp;quot; Which means that it's even more stereotypical in attempting to cultivate the entire oldest culture in the world and its many-many branches.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean? Are you somehow trying to imply that India have a culture?<br /> <br /> Nah, nonsense, it's all Ravnos clan. No need for all that boring minutia about &quot;culture&quot;, who wants that when you can have cool and exotic &quot;Indian vampires&quot;, amirite?<br /> <br /> Look, if that's not enough, just add a few even weirder and even more exotic bloodlines into the mix like the Nagaraja and the problem basically solves itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486922#post1486922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4] Ebony Kingdoms gets this right for the most part with the idea that if you have ALL of the Clans there, then there's the more appropriate diversity you'd expect for it. That's because Ventrue aren't &amp;quot;Western European Kindred Clan&amp;quot;, theyr'e nobility clan, which can be anywhere.<br /> <br /> My .02.</div> </div> </div> </div>YES! THANK YOU!<br /> <br /> That's EXACTLY what I have always thought! Why not just throwing in all the same old same old 13 clans EVERYWHERE - and maybe just throw some different names for the same guys in some places. So, the &quot;Caliphs&quot; or &quot;Sultans&quot; could still be Ventrue - even if in the middle east they have another arabic name for themselves. Muslim poets could be Toreador - again, with or without a different name. And the same goes for everywhere else; and that also means that all of a sudden, instead of the Assamites being middle eastern terrorists, they are &quot;multicultural assassins&quot;. Imagine how cool wouldnt be to have Assamites ninjas in Japan (if there were no Kuei Jin), or Assamites Janissaries or Assamites Templars... Just picture how much cooler if ALL the 13 clans had a much larger interaction between themselves rather than the Ravnos being the &quot;lost sheep&quot; from India wandering in Europe.<br /> <br /> But, what could we expect since the Ravnos literally were originally written to cover the &quot;fear of gypsies getting at your house at night to drink your blood&quot;, and that the old WW wrote the supplement &quot;Gypisies&quot; depicting an entire human group as the worse steriotype of themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:20:45-07:00","id":1486956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486940#post1486940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (which is still better than being &amp;quot;the filthy thieving Gipsies that call themselves Ravnos and I call Blood Hunt&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember as a teen in the 90's reading about that stuff, and it was the 90's so all the modern &quot;sensitivities&quot; werent as high as today, and I was never much of a progressive even back then, but if I would read all that stuff and think &quot;Jesus christ, so Assamites are basically murderous islamic terrorists and Ravnos are deceptful gipsies? Jeez... I hope those guys dont make a clan of jewish vampires...&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I enjoyed the game but, suffice it is to say that me and my pals basically ignored that those two existed at all, and the Followers of Set, althought existing, would never show their faces ever in any game... Lets just... Stick to the Camarilla and the Sabbath... Because... Trying to use those 2 were sort of... You know... It just didnt feel right.<br /> <br /> I mean, I really dont know what the hell was wrong with the writters for doing that. The &quot;Gipsies&quot; supplement in particular was one of the most bizarre things I would ever see in a RPG, it was a total &quot;wtf&quot; moment","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T21:31:01-07:00","id":1486958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486945#post1486945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">, and the Kuei-Jin have been erased from existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Praised be Caine for this. That was another very, very, very stupid idea.<br /> <br /> Like I said, nobody has the duty to know everything about completely foreign cultures - I myself couldnt do much better (when, I wouldnt throw in some insane steriotypes, but anyway), but it's better not to try at all than what we got.<br /> <br /> And you know, the worst part of it is that they werent trying to be racist, the writters were genuinely trying to paint gipsies with a good light and also make them special, but it absolutely backfired horribly and painted them as the clan of the untrusthworth thieves that are absolutely despised and universally hated, when all they wanted to do was to say that the gipsies were special, and that they were aware of the hidden world and had a cool of stuff going on for them... It's sad actually how it all went down thou.<br /> <br /> Edit: well, in the case of the Assamites however it were indeed a bit of a racist steriotype thou","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T22:22:41-07:00","id":1486961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486952#post1486952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, nonsense, it's all Ravnos clan. No need for all that boring minutia about &quot;culture&quot;, who wants that when you can have cool and exotic &quot;Indian vampires&quot;, amirite?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I liked the Idea, the first Ravnos was created by the Gods especially to combat the Kue-Jin<br /> But I loved and still love Kindred of the East as a whole so, I guess I'm an anomaly ^^'<br /> <br /> As Cainites, India was a treasure trove<br /> - The Ravnos<br /> - The Danava (who claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava; and the Antediluvian is sleeping there, they are its guardian. As a side note, the Salubri say that Saulot achieved a transcendent spiritual state in the Indian city of Golconda, which falls within territory controlled by the Danava, If you want to remove Xue and Zao-Lat from the eqation, the very notion of Golconda originated from the Danava basically)<br /> - Kartarirya, the Many-Armed, the first childe of the Tzimisce Antediluvian and his brood who was - at least by the CB - embraced before the flood and considers all of India to be its personal hunting grounds and as a Tzimsice, very territorial... and who tried impersonating Kartikeya, the god of war, only to discover the Brahmans wielded their True Faith as a weapon and saw through such artifice. Surprisingly, in its search to find worshipers among the growing Vedic pantheon, Kartarirya came to understand and appreciate their religion. The multi-limbed divinities represented multiple states of beings, interpretations, and personalities. While the divinities were certainly terrifying to behold, the Indians accepted the complex and often conflicted gods and precepts as natural. Enamored with the concept of multifaceted existence and perception, Kartarirya geared its transcendence toward that effort. Instead of seeking worship, Kartarirya sought to remold itself into a creature that could exist in multiple states of awareness, simultaneously<br /> Even the Nagaraja was a nice addition<br /> Just a few examples of awesome coltural, spiritual, or basically any cool stories<br /> Alas, WoD sometimes can't handle their own good ideas...<br /> ...and we ends up soemthing like the WoD:Gypsies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:45:29-07:00","id":1486997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486958#post1486958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praised be Caine for this. That was another very, very, very stupid idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet we already have <b>Asian players</b> complaining about this removal. It was bad, but could be worked around. They mostly played with the normal clans, but a number of them thought having the KotE material added to the game and was generally interesting even if needing some work.<br /> <br /> And I understand them, because news is that they're going to do the same to the Metis in Werewolf, that is a stupid ableist stereotype, yet as a disabled person myself I think the game is only made worse by the removal, and it leaves a bitter taste of erasure in the mouth.<br /> <br /> <b>Stop saying that every attempt at inclusion is stupid</b>. You and MWIS aren't being any less &quot;Wight Knights&quot; than you blame White Wolf on being, actually you're worse. The kind that just uses this as an excuse to say that nothing should be done. And with the insufferable habit of assuming that none of the people affected are in the conversation, ever.<br /> <br /> <b>We are.</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T06:54:09-07:00","id":1486999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486997#post1486997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You and MWIS aren't being any less &quot;Wight Knights&quot; than you blame White Wolf on being, actually you're worse. The kind that just uses this as an excuse to say that nothing should be done. And with the insufferable habit of assuming that none of the people affected are in the conversation, ever.<br /> <br /> <b>We are.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>This is a personal attack. Take a warning.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T08:46:43-07:00","id":1487017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486997#post1486997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet we already have <b>Asian players</b> complaining about this removal. It was bad, but could be worked around. They mostly played with the normal clans, but a number of them thought having the KotE material added to the game and was generally interesting even if needing some work.<br /> <br /> And I understand them, because news is that they're going to do the same to the Metis in Werewolf, that is a stupid ableist stereotype, yet as a disabled person myself I think the game is only made worse by the removal, and it leaves a bitter taste of erasure in the mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wasnt saying inclusion is bad. You misunderstand my words. What Im saying is that what White Wolf did back in the day was... Terrible. And again, I dont blame them - well, I sort of half blame them thou, the least they could do is to having properly researched it, but since it was pre internet, I give it a pass.<br /> <br /> My problem with KotE was not that they were Asian, but rather that they were in effect a different splat, but that only ever happened in Asia (and when we say &quot;Asia&quot; here, it's the typical western stereotype, which excludes India, Middle East, Central Asia and Russia, so there's also that)<br /> <br /> Why the dead only rise again in &quot;Asia&quot;? That's just even more orientalism, so their ideas of diversity are horribly executed<br /> <br /> I would have no problem with the &quot;Kuei Jin&quot; being another regular splat, and having them all over the world. I mean, that probably would be great for Mexico for example, having dead aztecs coming back and HATING what they see. I mean, it wouldnt be my cup of tea, we already have Wraith which I believe is far superior, but I wouldnt mind it either.<br /> <br /> What they did instead in their efforts to include was segragate; they basically said that (southeast) asians are different, they are not like us. When what they should do is have the same clans, preferably with different names, and with their own cultural norms.<br /> <br /> What they did for the eastern Fera for instance, while still not perfect was a much better approach. Yes, they did have a single tribe of &quot;kung fu werewolves&quot;, but they quickly realized this and fixed it in the proper way; eastern Fera are different because their culture is different, not because asians are different.<br /> <br /> It would be far better to have confucian Ventrue and taoist Tremere than saying that chinese people are magic and have basically a spiritual barrier segregating East and West. This was not much different from gipsies being magic either.<br /> <br /> About the Metis, I didnt know that this was being planned. It seems a massive change. I dont know how I feel about it. I never personally liked the concept, not because of the disabilities but because of the aspect of being infertile, thus unable to spread the gift of Gaia, and unjustly hated. At the other hand, I understand how they serve a purpose of tragedy to the story, more so than to themselves but rather to the Fera, who end up being forbidden to love one another - a heavy personal blow. So, I dont know what to think. Maybe reformulating it would've been better than erasing the concept, I dont know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486997#post1486997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Stop saying that every attempt at inclusion is stupid</b>. You and MWIS aren't being any less &quot;Wight Knights&quot; than you blame White Wolf on being, actually you're worse. The kind that just uses this as an excuse to say that nothing should be done. And with the insufferable habit of assuming that none of the people affected are in the conversation, ever.<br /> <br /> <b>We are.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Im not saying every attempt of inclusion is stupid, Im saying that stupid attempts of inclusion are stupid - particularly when the end result is having segregation instead of inclusion. I mean, if White Wolf have said that brazilians are a &quot;magic people&quot; who are different from the rest because of the powers Soccer and Samba and that because of that we have the &quot;Carnavallis&quot; exclusive supernatural splat, I would be rightfully pissed. It would be better NOT to write a single line about Brazil than making such a garbage - and I wouldnt mind not being included (particularly if &quot;inclusion&quot; means stereotype and segregation). Now, I know this game was made by americans, and just how the brazilian culture influences who you and I both are, I know that an american sees the world and understands it by their cultural lenses, just as a japanese, chinese, iranian etc, and I dont expect a Somali to be an absolutely expert in all aspects of the peruvian culture any more than I would expect an american to know all about Brazil - just as I know a few bits of american culture, but I wouldnt dare trying to depict it with perfection, and despite my personal love for the hinduist religion, I dare not trying to depict the highly complex culture of India.<br /> <br /> And I dont blame them for getting it wrong - but I do however blame them for the terrible generalizations. And no, no need to include brazilians at all if that means depicting us as a bunch of criminals that spend all our time playing soccer and communing with the &quot;powers of carnival&quot;. That type of inclusion I pass - and if you think that's an exaggeration, lets just remember that the assamites were the worse kind of stereotype of arabs as terrorists. So, thanks but no thanks.<br /> <br /> No need to take it personally thou. Both me and Mywifeis, we are not going against inclusion, quite the opposite. Which is exactly why we are criticizing West Europe and North America getting the &quot;normal&quot; clans while the rest of the world gets the problem children. It's exactly because we would like to see this &quot;rest of the world&quot; treated with the same respect - not because we would want it to be completely erased.<br /> <br /> Edit: just to close it up, I was not accusing White Wolf of being White Knights nor of having prejudices against the rest of the world. I was saying I recognize the limitations of my fellow human beings, but saying that their ideas simply were terrible, and their ideas to fix those issues arent much less terrible than the original. That's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-19-2022, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T09:20:30-07:00","id":1487019,"title":"","content":"As an Italian, I can say that I can't see Giovanni as offensive. Of course, they are incestuous, with tendencies towards necrophilia and the mafia, but they also have flaws.<br /> But I can't really take offense perhaps because I see them as &quot;Americanate&quot; (American stuff).<br /> However, I believe that for an Italian-American who &quot;must&quot; find a way to integrate into the American melting polt and, at the same time, has its origins as an identity factor that must defend everything, it can be much more offensive.<br /> But, on the other hand, there are ways and ways to play and make certain stereotypes cool and I think that all in all the Giovanni are a good example.<br /> <br /> It is true that bad stereotyping is harmful but I believe, despite sharing many points of your post, Kakost, that no representation is even worse. A misrepresentation can move criticisms and create movements of opinion that the total lack of representation cannot give.<br /> You can start with Brazilian vampires who love football and samba but you can get to deepen and find links with the very interesting history of your country (if I understand correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T09:38:03-07:00","id":1487021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487019#post1487019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an Italian, I can say that I can't see Giovanni as offensive. Of course, they are incestuous, with tendencies towards necrophilia and the mafia, but they also have flaws.<br /> But I can't really take offense perhaps because I see them as &amp;quot;Americanate&amp;quot; (American stuff).<br /> However, I believe that for an Italian-American who &amp;quot;must&amp;quot; find a way to integrate into the American melting polt and, at the same time, has its origins as an identity factor that must defend everything, it can be much more offensive.<br /> But, on the other hand, there are ways and ways to play and make certain stereotypes cool and I think that all in all the Giovanni are a good example.<br /> <br /> It is true that bad stereotyping is harmful but I believe, despite sharing many points of your post, Kakost, that no representation is even worse. A misrepresentation can move criticisms and create movements of opinion that the total lack of representation cannot give.<br /> You can start with Brazilian vampires who love football and samba but you can get to deepen and find links with the very interesting history of your country (if I understand correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, I had completely forgotten about the Giovanni &quot;mafia-incestuous-necrophiliac-italian-vampires&quot; lol.<br /> <br /> I see your point. Well, it could be, I hadnt really thought about that from that angle. Maybe you're right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T09:43:32-07:00","id":1487022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1486997#post1486997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Stop saying that every attempt at inclusion is stupid</b>. You and MWIS aren't being any less &quot;Wight Knights&quot; than you blame White Wolf on being, actually you're worse. The kind that just uses this as an excuse to say that nothing should be done. And with the insufferable habit of assuming that none of the people affected are in the conversation, ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there was this interesting little thing I read today about women in the workplace: Though the author wrote about how Women outperform men in management, they're far more likely to get imposter syndrome than men are. One of the funny things about imposter syndrome is that if you try to reasure the &quot;imposter&quot; that they're doing well and they're awesome and they shouldn't feel like imposters... well that'll just make things worse won't it? All the &quot;let's put women in the workplace&quot; kinda messaging can really make people feel like they were a diversity hire rather than someone picked for their skills.<br /> <br /> Why do we need to categorize everyone and put them in little groups so we can US vs THEM? The first seven clans started off satirizing types of people and they could work anywhere, the next six clans were crude parodies of ethnic groups, explicitly tied to specific human cultures. In addition to this we have little throwaway details like &quot;Indian Ventrue are wizards because they're so much better&quot; With that there's the implications are that indians are more spiritual because they have magic and less likeable since they lose presence. There isn't really much thought put into how indian vampire society would change now that the guys that keep everyone together are no longer people=pwersons.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first seven clans were a parody of class values, something that applies across cultures. the other six are ethnic and cultural attacks. We went from &quot;the west is great and foreigners are terrible&quot; to &quot;The west is dead and the east/south are superior because they still have culture&quot;<br /> <b>Neither is ok</b>.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla should be a global organization, not a European one. The Core 7 clans, minus the Tremere, excell because you can easily adjust them to local cultures, because they are culture-less (The Tremere have a clear european origin, but they do have an inclusive attitude that really enables a great amount of world-wide expansion)<br /> <br /> I think every step should be taken to cut mortal cultures out of clans. FoS have the whole masks of set thing, good. The Giovanni? They've got incestuos necromancer families all around the world. Good. The Assamites should really have cells all around the world: many mountains, not just one. Perhaps many sects. The Ravnos? Make them international, just like the Gangrel, a clan influenced by their locality rather than defined by it. The Tzmisce? Stop throwing Transylvania into the mud, it's a beautiful place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-19-2022, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T11:49:48-07:00","id":1487034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487017#post1487017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why the dead only rise again in &quot;Asia&quot;?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that one was explained<br /> The Yama Kings conducted several rituals when created Yomi, tearing pieces from the Yin and Yang world, defiling and twisting dragon lines and dragon nests (caerns and ley lines) that isolated the Middle Kingdom in that regard and ultimately backfired and prevented them to claim souls from the &quot;west&quot; in to their Hells in Yomi. And to be a Kuei-Jin escaping from Yomi is part of the process<br /> The Dead not rise only in &quot;Asia&quot;, the Hun and the P'o is basically the Psyche and Shadow/Beast (and even the Ba and Khaibit of the Mummies) and the Kuei-Jin are technically Raisens, with added curses from the August Personage in Jade and the Ministers of Heaven and Yi the Archer. The whole thing is spiritual, thats why the Yama Kings actually supported the Great Leap Outward to spread their and the Middle Kingdom's infulence. I suspect belife is plays a big part too, since Kuei-jin do rise on the West, they are called k\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n<br /> Common knowledge is that only inhabitants of the Middle Kingdom can take the Second Breath, but this is disproven by the existence of k\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n (Kuei-jin that have taken the Second Breath outside the Middle Kingdom and somehow managed to transcend their chih-mei phase out of sheer force of will. And could happen basically anywhere tho eastern communities the most common) and the Yulan-jin (who are known to be able to possess the corpses of people of non-asian descent).<br /> In the West with similar process eg. the two part of the soul makes a deal basically/co-exist and inhabit its own body (or posess one) also happnes, except you don't have to escape from Hell and don't have that many curses... they are called Risen<br /> <br /> And if you want to go an extra mile, the Settite firmly belive Sutekh returned from Duat (Hell - Duat is pretty hellish place if you dont have rituals and cheat codes from the Book of the Dead) after battled Apep and risen as a creature of neither alive nor dead. The Light sensitivity is Ra's wrath... basically making him a &quot;Kuei-Jin of Egypt&quot; and strangley enough the level 9 Serpentis power &quot;remind Ra the time when Set was his Champion and for a day, your settite is immune for sunlight... so who knows? Could have some merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-19-2022, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T15:37:02-07:00","id":1487064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487034#post1487034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually that one was explained<br /> The Yama Kings conducted several rituals when created Yomi, tearing pieces from the Yin and Yang world, defiling and twisting dragon lines and dragon nests (caerns and ley lines) that isolated the Middle Kingdom in that regard and ultimately backfired and prevented them to claim souls from the &am