 </div> </div> </div>Yes, so you get some lore to reinforce this idea that the gipsies - oops, I mean, east asians - are different.<br /> <br /> It doesnt really change what I said.<br /> <br /> Now, you may strech things if you want to, but Risen are NOT Kuei Jin, nor are the Setites either. It doesnt matter what kind of silly myths the setites have about their &quot;god&quot;, the Followers of Set are cainites, they drink blood, they make ghouls, they sire progeny by sucking a mortal dry and feeding their own vitae to the mortal, and they even learn the disciplines of other clans - and can teach their own disciplines to other clans. The Kuei Jin do none of that.<br /> <br /> And likewise, neither are the Risen Kuei Jin - they dont drink blood, they are immune to the sun, they feed on Pathos.<br /> <br /> You may draw some parallels, but all those 3 are effectively vastly different types of critters.<br /> <br /> So, the fact that an entire group of people are treated differently - you know, like they did with the gipsies in the pre historic WoD writting - still remains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T16:27:51-07:00","id":1487069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487022#post1487022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there was this interesting little thing I read today about women in the workplace: Though the author wrote about how Women outperform men in management, they're far more likely to get imposter syndrome than men are. One of the funny things about imposter syndrome is that if you try to reasure the &amp;quot;imposter&amp;quot; that they're doing well and they're awesome and they shouldn't feel like imposters... well that'll just make things worse won't it? All the &amp;quot;let's put women in the workplace&amp;quot; kinda messaging can really make people feel like they were a diversity hire rather than someone picked for their skills.<br /> <br /> Why do we need to categorize everyone and put them in little groups so we can US vs THEM? The first seven clans started off satirizing types of people and they could work anywhere, the next six clans were crude parodies of ethnic groups, explicitly tied to specific human cultures. In addition to this we have little throwaway details like &amp;quot;Indian Ventrue are wizards because they're so much better&amp;quot; With that there's the implications are that indians are more spiritual because they have magic and less likeable since they lose presence. There isn't really much thought put into how indian vampire society would change now that the guys that keep everyone together are no longer people=pwersons.<br /> <br /> <br /> The first seven clans were a parody of class values, something that applies across cultures. the other six are ethnic and cultural attacks. We went from &amp;quot;the west is great and foreigners are terrible&amp;quot; to &amp;quot;The west is dead and the east/south are superior because they still have culture&amp;quot;<br /> <b>Neither is ok</b>.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla should be a global organization, not a European one. The Core 7 clans, minus the Tremere, excell because you can easily adjust them to local cultures, because they are culture-less (The Tremere have a clear european origin, but they do have an inclusive attitude that really enables a great amount of world-wide expansion)<br /> <br /> I think every step should be taken to cut mortal cultures out of clans. FoS have the whole masks of set thing, good. The Giovanni? They've got incestuos necromancer families all around the world. Good. The Assamites should really have cells all around the world: many mountains, not just one. Perhaps many sects. The Ravnos? Make them international, just like the Gangrel, a clan influenced by their locality rather than defined by it. The Tzmisce? Stop throwing Transylvania into the mud, it's a beautiful place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, Assamites would make great Ninjas, Janissaries and Templars. Japanese tzismisce, making &quot;living objects&quot; and horrenduous masked faces, or Indian Tzismisce &quot;Rakshasas&quot; would also be incredible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T18:26:28-07:00","id":1487082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487017#post1487017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if White Wolf have said that brazilians are a &quot;magic people&quot; who are different from the rest because of the powers Soccer and Samba and that because of that we have the &quot;Carnavallis&quot; exclusive supernatural splat, I would be rightfully pissed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, don't you enter a Capoeira Fighting Trance when listening to Samba like everyone else? Maybe you should ask for a new blessed foot ball from the bishop (note: as the British, I too refuse to call true football (and its related ball) by the name of a piece of clothe just because the US don't like to call armored rugby by its proper name).<br /> <br /> MWIS wasn't just talking about the beginning of the game, he talks like that about every book that does <b><u>anything</u></b> with <b><u>anything</u></b> that was originally a stupid racist stereotype, or at least that's my firm impression. And as I said before, <b>actual Asians</b> don't necessarily want to solve KotE by excluding them, and the same applies to other minorities.<br /> <br /> No matter how bad it was at first, just trying to ignore or erase the past won't really give closure to any offended party. Learning about them or, better, asking them what they want, helps. Won't ever be easy or perfect, but it is what can be done, and frequently the actual people affected already managed to adapt those things into their games, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Any claim</b> made in their behalf of what should or shouldn't be done is White Nighting in some way, even one that doesn't proposes any constructive way out, just destruction.<br /> <br /> Oh, also that:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487019#post1487019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is true that bad stereotyping is harmful but I believe, despite sharing many points of your post, Kakost, that no representation is even worse. A misrepresentation can move criticisms and create movements of opinion that the total lack of representation cannot give.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of our current collective awareness about several social problems came from stereotypes being spread to then be questioned. If there is no representation, then the plight of the group goes unheard. And I personally know of some gaming groups that had to face some realities and misconceptions about disabilities just because the Metis in WtA &quot;forced&quot; them to. Common? Not. Is it a good depiction? Not by a mile. Did more good than not by just being there?<br /> <br /> Yes. It did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487019#post1487019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can start with Brazilian vampires who love football and samba but you can get to deepen and find links with the very interesting history of your country (if I understand correctly).</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the ideas people have about Brazil are actually just about Rio de Janeiro city (there's also the state of Rio de Janeiro) and the rainforest. It isn't completely dissimilar to how so many people think of Italy as if it was a bunch of wine-producing villages around the Colosseum speaking Sicilian with a Calabrian accent. Or, to Americans, as if the entire country was either Miami or the Arizona desert.<br /> <br /> Football (or, as only the US and Japan call it in the entire world, Soccer) is exceedingly popular, although that has been changing little by little with other sports becoming more popular, but indeed most people play it or watch it all across the country (I don't do either, yet even I know most rules by heart). Samba is largely overplayed, though, and not even a fraction of all the music genres around the country. Its heyday is long gone by now.<br /> <br /> But overall the problem is the difference between we having something and people thinking that's all there is to know about the country.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487022#post1487022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first seven clans were a parody of class values, something that applies across cultures. the other six are ethnic and cultural attacks. We went from &quot;the west is great and foreigners are terrible&quot; to &quot;The west is dead and the east/south are superior because they still have culture&quot;<br /> <b>Neither is ok</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet when they try to better, you keep bashing as if nothing changed. On top of that, you keep not even considering the opinion of any other people, you <i>assume</i> the people affected need this or that and bulldoze everything. Or, again, that's my firm impression of many of your posts on those matters.<br /> <br /> There are people from all over the world that play those games and can be reached for their opinions. Did you ever talked to one of them or you just assumes everyone else in the forum has zero contact outside &quot;the West&quot;? I'm Brazilian, Heavy Arms is Jew, we have regulars in this forum from Polland, Germany, Italy and Korea just taking some I personally know about. There are people around here that <b><i>really</i></b> know what it feels like to be a minority or minority-like in pop culture, or what a depiction does to them in their own culture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T21:46:03-07:00","id":1487107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487082#post1487082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, don't you enter a Capoeira Fighting Trance when listening to Samba like everyone else? Maybe you should ask for a new blessed foot ball from the bishop (note: as the British, I too refuse to call true football (and its related ball) by the name of a piece of clothe just because the US don't like to call armored rugby by its proper name).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, no. In fact I hate samba; love Metallica thou. My daughter, 2 years old now, would only sleep listening to Metallica or Iron Maiden from her 3 months old up to her 1st year, Enter Sandman was literally her lullaby, and now her dancing it is the cuttiest thing ever.<br /> <br /> I hate football (but like you I also hate calling it &quot;soccer&quot;), and I dont mind Capoeira, my 5 years old son practices it, althought Im a black belt in Karate.<br /> <br /> Oh, and I also absolutely hate with all my strenght Carnival, that's the worse part of the year for me.<br /> <br /> Im an atheist, my wife however is umbandista (for the non brazilians, this is a politeistic religion of african origin, similar to Voodo or Santeria, and with heavy syncretism with catholicism). I love mythologies, so I've taken a deep interest in the mythology of the Yorubas which my wife adheres ever since I met her, but Im not a follower, being a firm atheist and totally skeptical materialist.<br /> <br /> That in fact makes me a second generation atheist, both of my fathers are atheists, and my father was a stauch commie - no jokes here, he were about to receive paramilitary training in order to fight in the guerilla with the sole purpose of instauring the dictatorship of the proletariath. And Im being dead serious here. Luckly for him (and for me too, 'cuz I wouldnt exist otherwise), the terrorist organization that was recruiting him were dismantled and arrested before he could join - which probably saved his life, and my own future existance too.<br /> <br /> Much to the displeasure of my father thou, althought he succesfully managed to raise me as an atheist, he did not managed to make me a good &quot;comrade&quot;. Im an Anarcho-Capitalist, so you could say that yes, Im a rebel, because reactionary is the new revolutionary. And althought I would share one of my father's favorite phrase &quot;religion is the opium of the masses&quot;, I grew to be much more tolerant and to think by myself, and nowadays while I still think that belief in God or the supernatural doesnt make any sense - and unlike most people I never &quot;deconverted&quot;, faith is something that never made sense to me because I never had it, today I have deep sympathies towards the religions of people and no longer hold the arrogant view that it is just a &quot;burgeoise distraction&quot; for the ignorant.<br /> <br /> You see, this is why I hate placing people into boxes of groups; we are more than just mere group identity, we are each one of us unique on our own right, and the tiniest minority will always be the individual. Im certanly much more complex than just Black/White, Gay/Straight, Rich/Poor or any other classification that exists only for our overlords to divide and conquer us peasants, as Im sure you or any other person in the world are. I mean, if I were to simply call you &quot;brazilian&quot; and pretend that this is all I need to know about you, that would be shameful towards your entire life history.<br /> <br /> In my own example, Im an atheist in the largest catholic country in the world, I hate football - in the country of football, and I love Metallica and hate carnival in the country of samba and carnival.<br /> <br /> When you place labels on entire groups of people, you reduce them to a mindless hive mind of faceless crowds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487082#post1487082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">MWIS wasn't just talking about the beginning of the game, he talks like that about every book that does <b><u>anything</u></b> with <b><u>anything</u></b> that was originally a stupid racist stereotype, or at least that's my firm impression. And as I said before, <b>actual Asians</b> don't necessarily want to solve KotE by excluding them, and the same applies to other minorities.<br /> <br /> No matter how bad it was at first, just trying to ignore or erase the past won't really give closure to any offended party. Learning about them or, better, asking them what they want, helps. Won't ever be easy or perfect, but it is what can be done, and frequently the actual people affected already managed to adapt those things into their games, too.<br /> <br /> <b>Any claim</b> made in their behalf of what should or shouldn't be done is White Nighting in some way, even one that doesn't proposes any constructive way out, just destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im not white knighting anything. Let me put this here, which I totally agree:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487022#post1487022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do we need to categorize everyone and put them in little groups so we can <b>US vs THEM</b>? The first seven clans started off satirizing types of people and they could work anywhere, the next six clans were crude parodies of ethnic groups, explicitly tied to specific human cultures.<br /> ...<br /> The first seven clans were a parody of class values, something that applies across cultures. the other six are ethnic and cultural attacks. We went from &quot;the west is great and foreigners are terrible&quot; to &quot;The west is dead and the east/south are superior because they still have culture&quot;<br /> <b>Neither is ok.</b><br /> <br /> The Camarilla should be a global organization, not a European one. The Core 7 clans, minus the Tremere, excell because you can easily adjust them to local cultures, because they are culture-less (The Tremere have a clear european origin, but they do have an inclusive attitude that really enables a great amount of world-wide expansion)</div> </div> </div> </div>So, he is absolutely right, the first 7 clans - which ironically are the functional ones (yes, even the malkavians) were well constructed because they werent tied to any culture. There wasnt a &quot;Prussian clan&quot;, and despite the Spanish/Italian/French-alike names such as &quot;Toreador&quot; or &quot;Brujah&quot; - that by the way, make next to zero sense, &quot;Brujah&quot; for instance is spanish for &quot;witch&quot;, so a clan thousands of years old has as their name a word in a language that would form thousands of years later... Hmmm... Okay.<br /> <br /> It's not about &quot;white knighting&quot;, it's about how poor of a decision it was from going from the very human parodies that the first 7 were, to just throw in bland cultural groups for the next 6.<br /> <br /> To be clear: the results would've been no better than if the Assamites were texan cowboys, the Ravnos French mimics, the Giovanni prussian warmongers or the Setites tea drinking brits that love the empire. So, it's not about misrepresentation of minorities, but rather about what a poor design choice it is to tie supernatural &quot;families&quot; with cultural groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487082#post1487082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also that:<br /> <br /> Most of our current collective awareness about several social problems came from stereotypes being spread to then be questioned. If there is no representation, then the plight of the group goes unheard. And I personally know of some gaming groups that had to face some realities and misconceptions about disabilities just because the Metis in WtA &amp;quot;forced&amp;quot; them to. Common? Not. Is it a good depiction? Not by a mile. Did more good than not by just being there?<br /> <br /> Yes. It did.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well. I can concede on that point, and this doesnt bother me. I dont personally deal with Metis because WtA aint my cup of tea, but ok.<br /> <br /> Still, I would prefer that the idiotic racist stereotype were due to some silly depiction of an Indian Ventrue, rather than the boring &quot;clan of India&quot;. And that's because a Ventrue is a parody of a &quot;Blue Blood&quot;, be it a Maraja in India, a bureocrat in China or an european noble; that in my opinion is a much better design than simply the &quot;indian clan&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or, in other terms, I would prefer a lazy, criminal, untrustworthy brazilian Ventrue, representing all possible worse stereotypes, that just wanna dance samba and watch football all day long than a &quot;brazilian clan&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-19T23:22:02-07:00","id":1487112,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">We can either stop the attacks and accusing other posters of racism and move back to discussing the Tremere and rivalry for Blood Magic or it will be shut down.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:27:38-07:00","id":1487187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487107#post1487107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, if I were to simply call you &quot;brazilian&quot; and pretend that this is all I need to know about you, that would be shameful towards your entire life history.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that equating <i>any</i> classification to <u>simplification</u> is a dangerous and unhelpful fallacy.<br /> <br /> I'm Autistic. This by no means resumes everything I am. You don't know everything you need to know about me, my abilities and inabilities, my work, my personality, or any other aspect of my life just by knowing I'm Autistic.<br /> <br /> Yet, I'm Autistic, and it <b><u>does</u></b> affect my life. The entirety of it. While it doesn't resume any aspect of my life, it affects each one of them. It affects my marriage, my work, the way I talk and write and make friends, it affects how I play games. It is a <b>fact</b> of my life, not just a meaningless label.<br /> <br /> When people try to be nice by saying that I don't seem to be Autistic, that I'm high functioning, or otherwise pretending this is not a thing to be considered it doesn't help. <b>it hurts. <u>a lot</u></b>. Because while they're trying to &quot;see me beyond the label&quot;, what they're really doing is to negate a whole and important aspect of my life, my experiences, my suffering and joys, my needs and difficulties.<br /> <br /> And that is a common thread among minorities, I've talked to so much people from such groups, some I belong to, some I don't. We are not a label, but that goes without saying, it should be obvious. But we <b>need</b> to have those aspects of ourselves and their implications recognized and accepted by what they are.<br /> <br /> Just as that, I'm a Brazilian. It doesn't make me an average Brazilian, actually as many nerds around here I have similar tastes to you (and my father was actually a member of MR8, although acting only as student organizer, which was a pacific branch). But it does mean I can't help but have my life affected by being Brazilian. I deal with football's popularity even if I don't like it, I speak Portuguese, I know MPB and many of the stories behind certain songs. I live under Bolsonaro and our current political landscape regardless of my opinion on it, I live under Brazilian law, politics, culture, language, history, geography, strife, prejudices, the good, the bad, the ugly and the things I don't particularly care about in my daily life.<br /> <br /> Being a Brazilian isn't a label that defines me. But it <b>is a fact about me</b>. That affects my life and has consequence. That needs to be taken into account. Pretending it is not there to not label me won't help anything about it, just make this whole part of me invisible and unspeakable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487107#post1487107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about &quot;white knighting&quot;, it's about how poor of a decision it was from going from the very human parodies that the first 7 were, to just throw in bland cultural groups for the next 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're not grasping in my argument is the difference between committing a mistake and addressing it after the fact.<br /> <br /> All those poor design decisions are, indeed, poor design decisions. There are many of them all around the place. Some are relatively minor, some are huge.<br /> <br /> <b>But now they're there</b>. The best scenario would be for them to not have happened in the first place. But they did. What now?<br /> <br /> This is the problem, and the reason there are Asian players pissed at them for erasing KotE and calling them racists for pretending a racist stereotype didn't existed.<br /> <br /> Once that game element existed, and had time to take root (something <i><b>Gypsies</b></i> hadn't), this changes the context completely and this distinct context deeply changes the consequences of what you do next. <u>Erasing a mistake is not the same as not having committed it in the first place</u>, and does not have the same consequences.<br /> <br /> So, when I say that someone is White Knighting in this (double checked, no more typos on the word, and I'm not effectively calling anyone a White Knight), it is about what you propose as a solution <b>now</b>. The mistake from 30 years ago happened 30 years ago. What do we do <b>now?</b> Pretending the mistake never happened isn't necessarily a fix, it is just a proposal for solution like any other, and <b>must consider the actual opinions and actual effects on actual people like any other</b>.<br /> <br /> It may backfire. It may offend more instead of address the original offense. It may make things worse rather than better. Damned if they do, damned if they don't and all that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T09:08:04-07:00","id":1487202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487187#post1487187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[b]I'll Summarize</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to reduce my posts and not be so pedantic, althought for me that's difficult, so I'll also try summarize your post.<br /> <br /> First, I understand how it may hurt to have the feeling that others deal with your autism in an unconsidered manner, and maybe even to seem to disregard it completely. I mean, I understand, but obviously I dont know. I cant possibly know how you feel, but I can understand.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing that I can tell you, is not to let it hurt so much, by trying to also understand the other people - and that's hard. It's hard because each one of us, every single human, is an universe by ourselves. You for example, are just a figment of my inagination. NOTHING exists outside of me, outside of my Ego, and when I die, the entire universe will cease to be.<br /> <br /> So, each one of us, we can only experience ourselves; we can never experience the other. We can run mental simulations to try to understand, but those are approximations of reality, not reality. When we exercise empathy, that's what we do - we simulate the pain of the other as if it were being inflicted in our own Ego.<br /> <br /> So, that's what the other people do to you when they say that your autism is barely noticiable, or that you're highly functional. Now, I know that, for you, it seems as if your hardship is somehow diminished by them saying that. But you need not think that way. When that happens, remember that those people are trying to exercise their empathy, thus they are actively running simulations of what they think that you feel in order to feel themselves. But those are simulations, not the real deal, but not that they are <b>trying as best they can</b>, and take comfort in that.<br /> <br /> I myself for example, I wouldnt know what to say to you. I mean, it's one thing to type a bunch of text on the internet, and it's another to look you in the eyes and try to transmit confort and compassion. And honestly, I guess I've already made a great impression in this forums to show Im not exactly a persons type of guy. And yet, I would want you to know that I do sympathize with your condition. Now, if I may and please take no offense, try to reverse places. Imagine for a moment you were not an autist, and you were trying to confort a person that is, what would you say?<br /> <br /> Now, I do have a different experience because I suffer with chronicle grave depression my entire life, and sometimes life is just devoid of any purpose, mean or joy. And people come to say &quot;you're such a handsome guy, so intelligent, you have so much to live&quot;... And yes, I hate to hear that on my lows, but with time I came to understand that this is not an attack on me, but just simply imperfect humans just as myself, trying to show empathy towards a person suffering with something they cant possibly understand, and they do it in the only way they know how, and as best as they can.<br /> <br /> I hope this can help you draw new meanings in your life brother (or sister, I dont know).<br /> <br /> Now, my views are obviously biased by my worldview, I 100% admit that. Like I said, Im an ancap (if there were any doubts at all right, since subtlety aint my strongest point), I have my personal convictions and that absolutely colours my personal opinions, and Im by no means more immune to selective blindness or cognitive dissonance than any other person. That being said - and again, this may be due to my own incapability to see beyond my &quot;bubble&quot; - I do not like group identity, because I find it to be merely divisive rather than unifying. Sure, I absolutely agree that we do share many traits with our &quot;group&quot;, so obviously I'll probably find more common ground with another brazilian than with a german or korean. However, we are defined by a multitude of different &quot;groups&quot; that shape each one of us over our lives. For example, everybody here belongs to the &quot;group&quot; of WoD players, and to the bigger group of RPG players. You have the group of &quot;autists&quot;, Im in the group of the chronic depressives, and those two (most of the time) do not connect - and yet, here we are, finding common ground and a connecting point in the &quot;Vampire the Masquerade&quot; group, were you and I both, two human beings with vastly different lives and histories, find a place were we connect.<br /> <br /> And look how funny this is: you dont know if Im white, black, gay, straight; had I not tell you, you wouldnt know if Im an atheist, or catholic, or muslim or jew or buddhist. And neither do I know those informations about you.<br /> <br /> Maybe we would hate each other in person, who knows? But despite that, we are having this enthusiastic conversation.<br /> <br /> That's were I stand. I prefer to see each individual as their own unique thing, and look for what unite us, what we have in common, rather than what sets us apart.<br /> <br /> But yes, I do understand that there are particular points of contention for the individuals. In your case for instance, I understand that autism doesnt define you, but it IS an important aspect of your life and who you are, and that cant just be set apart. I understand that for a muslim, for example, althought being a muslim aint the entirety of who they are, is significant if everybody else keeps calling an honest and decent good hearted person of a terrorist due to prejudice, or how any other minorities feel. I know prejudice exists and the world aint rainbows, I just prefer to look for what unite us instead.<br /> <br /> As for what could the writters do, just &quot;internationalize&quot; everything. Make Assamite ninjas, Ventrue daimyos and ronin Brujah samurais.<br /> <br /> And let them do some entirely different stupid mistakes, but at least ones that would have an interesting dynamic.<br /> <br /> For example, I like what Wraith did. There is Stygia - which is our world, the world that we understand, the western world. And out of that, there are the more vague dark kingdoms. But ultimately, they are all wraiths and specters just as the ones in the west, only adapted by their own cultures, and with their own particular dumberies (like for example EVERY single one of the southeastern wraiths that arent Han Chinese being sent to the forges, Im sure the japanese, koreans, vietnamise etc must love that)<br /> <br /> Edit: bah so much for trying not to be pedantic. Sorry for my long texts, I just simply cannot be objective","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-20-2022, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T11:13:35-07:00","id":1487212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487082#post1487082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet when they try to better, you keep bashing as if nothing changed. </div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, I've given credit where it's due<br /> The Good: <br /> FoS- Easily one of the best written clans/sects in V20 (Violently excluding the DAV20). There's room to improve, but it's very solid on the whole. <br /> Giovanni-Family diversity is a great move, they could do well to go further with it. 9/10, only wish they'd just fucking join the camarilla and be a -normal- clan. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Middle<br /> Lasombra- Hey, slightly less emphasis on race this time. More religions than just catholics. Great. More could've been done. <br /> <br /> I love Assamites. However, as much as it makes sense for them, as an extremely militant sect, to localize around one location, it doesn't make political sense for them to have one localization. IE they should have had more schisms and more mountains. <br /> I love the Schism, it lets us have our cake and eat it too in a way that seems wholly sensible: We can have blood-fanatic loyalists with their own sect and erudite moderates causing drama in the Camarilla. <br /> -I hate that writers are making too much light of how easy it would be for the schismatics to integrate into the Camarilla, which should naturally be a massive and messy political undertaking. The game is all about struggle after all. a lot of writing is just too one-sidedly positive towards the schismatics. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Ugly:<br /> Ravnos. On one hand, the Vedic/Buddhist influence on the clan's philosophy is awesome: &quot;Reality is illusion&quot; is perfect for them, the focus on fate fits the clan like a glove. And I can see some rational for Ravnos being more appreciated in india due to being used as mercenaries against monsters. <br /> But it's one thing to have an Indian influence and another thing to be &quot;The Indian clan&quot;. Especially when that clan is the clan of conmen and thieves. That, and, y'know, I like the Ravnos, and really their clan concept should work absolutely everywhere. Making the clan &quot;The Indian clan&quot; automatically makes other Ravnos second-rate. <br /> <br /> Tzmisce: There's a good attempt to make more cosmopolitan neonates. But the elders are racial caricatures. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On top of that, you keep not even considering the opinion of any other people, you <i>assume</i> the people affected need this or that and bulldoze everything. Or, again, that's my firm impression of many of your posts on those matters. </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understand how much of a fucking monumental task it would be to give every culture/subculture their own cool bloodline and represent everyone in a way that's reasonable and fair. Lets say you give South America 7 unique clans to compete with the Camarillas OG 7? Are they well written and reasonable? If not, that's a problem. Are you sowing US vs THEM divisions and sowing nationalism? Are they superior to the Cam's 7? that's a problem. Are they worse than the Cam's 7? That's a problem. Are they equal to the Cam's 7? Wouldn't you be whitewashing history to do that? Now imagine doing this to all the major continents, hell do we need a bloodline for small populations like the Ainu or the Uyghurs or the Fins or the Jews or the Lesbians? They probably need the representation more, right? Once you do all this, we can happily all get pigeonholled into that one clan that &quot;represents&quot; us, right? <br /> <br /> If you want to go represent more, Who the fuck decides what's worth representing and what's not: you? It's a black hole, a good way to make your list of clans and bloodlines look like a phonebook. Can a publisher afford to give everyone the rightful amount of attention to detail they deserve when covering the planet with bloodlines? How much would you need to multiply the book budget? <br /> <br /> Gah! The Audacity! <br /> <br /> Giving the players everything they want is the fastest way to ruin a game. People want challenge, not to have everything handed to them. Rather than divide everyone up into little sections, it's simply better to lump them all in with the Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavians,Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue, perhaps the Ravnos, Followers of Set and Giovanni. They can change the names localy how they please. Everyone is equal. <i>Everyone</i> Is represented. Nobody is special. Keep it simple. The best way to represent everyone is to represent nobody. <b>The Ventrue are relatable villains across every culture</b>. </span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T14:56:31-07:00","id":1487256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, I've given credit where it's due<br /> The Good: <br /> FoS- Easily one of the best written clans/sects in V20 (Violently excluding the DAV20). There's room to improve, but it's very solid on the whole. <br /> Giovanni-Family diversity is a great move, they could do well to go further with it. 9/10, only wish they'd just fucking join the camarilla and be a -normal- clan. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Middle<br /> Lasombra- Hey, slightly less emphasis on race this time. More religions than just catholics. Great. More could've been done. <br /> <br /> I love Assamites. However, as much as it makes sense for them, as an extremely militant sect, to localize around one location, it doesn't make political sense for them to have one localization. IE they should have had more schisms and more mountains. <br /> I love the Schism, it lets us have our cake and eat it too in a way that seems wholly sensible: We can have blood-fanatic loyalists with their own sect and erudite moderates causing drama in the Camarilla. <br /> -I hate that writers are making too much light of how easy it would be for the schismatics to integrate into the Camarilla, which should naturally be a massive and messy political undertaking. The game is all about struggle after all. a lot of writing is just too one-sidedly positive towards the schismatics. <br /> <br /> <br /> The Ugly:<br /> Ravnos. On one hand, the Vedic/Buddhist influence on the clan's philosophy is awesome: &quot;Reality is illusion&quot; is perfect for them, the focus on fate fits the clan like a glove. And I can see some rational for Ravnos being more appreciated in india due to being used as mercenaries against monsters. <br /> But it's one thing to have an Indian influence and another thing to be &quot;The Indian clan&quot;. Especially when that clan is the clan of conmen and thieves. That, and, y'know, I like the Ravnos, and really their clan concept should work absolutely everywhere. Making the clan &quot;The Indian clan&quot; automatically makes other Ravnos second-rate. <br /> <br /> Tzmisce: There's a good attempt to make more cosmopolitan neonates. But the elders are racial caricatures. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> I don't think you understand how much of a fucking monumental task it would be to give every culture/subculture their own cool bloodline and represent everyone in a way that's reasonable and fair. Lets say you give South America 7 unique clans to compete with the Camarillas OG 7? Are they well written and reasonable? If not, that's a problem. Are you sowing US vs THEM divisions and sowing nationalism? Are they superior to the Cam's 7? that's a problem. Are they worse than the Cam's 7? That's a problem. Are they equal to the Cam's 7? Wouldn't you be whitewashing history to do that? Now imagine doing this to all the major continents, hell do we need a bloodline for small populations like the Ainu or the Uyghurs or the Fins or the Jews or the Lesbians? They probably need the representation more, right? Once you do all this, we can happily all get pigeonholled into that one clan that &quot;represents&quot; us, right? <br /> <br /> If you want to go represent more, Who the fuck decides what's worth representing and what's not: you? It's a black hole, a good way to make your list of clans and bloodlines look like a phonebook. Can a publisher afford to give everyone the rightful amount of attention to detail they deserve when covering the planet with bloodlines? How much would you need to multiply the book budget? <br /> <br /> Gah! The Audacity! <br /> <br /> Giving the players everything they want is the fastest way to ruin a game. People want challenge, not to have everything handed to them. Rather than divide everyone up into little sections, it's simply better to lump them all in with the Brujah, Gangrel, Malkavians,Nosferatu, Toreador and Ventrue, perhaps the Ravnos, Followers of Set and Giovanni. They can change the names localy how they please. Everyone is equal. <i>Everyone</i> Is represented. Nobody is special. Keep it simple. The best way to represent everyone is to represent nobody. <b>The Ventrue are relatable villains across every culture</b>. </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally always hated the bloodlines businesses to begin with. To me there would be the clans and that's it<br /> <br /> And hey, my beloved Ventrue arent villains! They are just... Complex <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: what I would truly love to see would be some global politics of Camarilla vs Sabbath + Anarchs on a Global scale you know... High politics. Ventrue Princes from Portugal plotting with Ventrue Daimyos from Japan to fight against the Spaniards Lasombra Bishops and japanese Lasombra Shinobies, or an American Tremere Regent travelling to the persian gulf to meet a Tremere Mullah, stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-20-2022, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:06:27-07:00","id":1487258,"title":"","content":"Anyway, anyhow... As written, the Tremere still hold the largest share of the market for Blood Magic; they are still the better connected guys in the Camarilla, aside from the Ventrue, they are well established within it and they have the organizatiom and the culture for it.<br /> <br /> Do the Assamites represent some competition? Yes, some. They do not however have the numbers nor are they firmly entrenched in the social structures of the Camarilla as the Tremere are. So yes, the Tremere now have some competition but no, nothing that could threaten their position in any measurable way. I do agree with MWIS thou that I also dislike the idea of having the Camarilla so acceptant to the Assamites, I think it should bring a lot more strife and struggle (not saying it wouldnt happen, just that it wouldnt be so easy), but alas, there's nothing I can do about it (except using my personal head cannon)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T00:58:15-07:00","id":1487323,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a>, first something I forgot to say earlier: you said &quot;my fathers&quot; when I think you meant &quot;my parents&quot;. That's something I think is worth to say publicly to correct any eventual mistake, PM me if you want this edited out. If anyone wants to know, &quot;parents&quot; in Portuguese is just said as the plural of &quot;Father&quot;, so my father is <i>meu pai</i>, my parents is <i>meus pais</i><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487202#post1487202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you need not think that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I have to, I work with disability and autism advocacy and orientation. Don't sweat it, I didn't said that because I can't personally cope with it, but because it literally <b>is</b> my job to help people understand us. Thanks for the kind words, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487202#post1487202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, each one of us, we can only experience ourselves; we can never experience the other. We can run mental simulations to try to understand, but those are approximations of reality, not reality. When we exercise empathy, that's what we do - we simulate the pain of the other as if it were being inflicted in our own Ego.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why people work with advocacy for vulnerable groups, because empathy by itself lacks knowledge and context, and society frequently fail in providing those for how to deal with its minorities (or foreign cultures).<br /> <br /> You can't know how I feel. But you can understand because I can tell you. If I don't, then you can't do either, because your internal simulation lacks data, it has only your own assumptions and perceptions. That's the point with those labels: they're information about people, <b>crucial</b> information, even if far from all the information.<br /> <br /> So my point when I say that people trying to &quot;see beyond the label&quot; hurt me isn't that I blame them, but that their uninformed actions have consequences opposed to their intentions, and in this particular case the heart of the problem is precisely the assumption that the &quot;label&quot; is the problem, when it isn't. <b>It isn't a label, it is information</b>.<br /> <br /> The argument of &quot;group identity is us vs them&quot; is fallacious in this context, and yet used frequently because of people that use it out of context, frequently in bad faith. When we're talking about minorities, conditions, cultures and several other things, the purpose of the identification is to aggregate relevant information. Not all Autistics are the same, yet most of us share a number of perceptions, experiences and hardships that are related, directly or not, to our shared trait of autism. Our individuality shapes how each of us live through those shared aspects, but does not change that we share them. By identifying ourselves as a group we can help each other and help others to understand us.<br /> <br /> Especially because otherwise, going full on on the &quot;beyond the label&quot; mentality, you would have to understand each Autistic person from scratch, without any common reference, committing the same mistakes each time as you don't transfer data from one to the other. A single mistake isn't a problem, you can expect that I have a given common Autistic trait and be wrong, after making things clear everything is ok. But if you simply does not assume any trait whatsoever and have to learn everything from scratch, you won't commit just a few, it will be a problem, and it will repeat itself over and over with others you meet. That group identity will go a long way into helping you to anticipate things, and you're still able to adapt to personal distinctions. It is only a label if you make it a label.<br /> <br /> Just take those principles and apply to the others. Gays, blacks, Jews, Japanese, those people aren't just labels, but the identities in question inform a lot of things they have in common. Sometimes crucial information that can make a huge difference in their lives if you know or not. They're not made the same by identifying as a group and they're not necessarily taking an &quot;us vs them&quot; position, it is just about relevant facts. Sure, there <b>are</b> people that will assume such a position, but it doesn't invalidate the whole identity and the very important function it has in organizing people to deal with the very real problems they face.<br /> <br /> When you blame the &quot;label&quot;, you risk making yourself the person that is assuming an &quot;us vs them&quot; mentality by proxy. Which is the intention of those who use this argument in bad faith.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487202#post1487202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope this can help you draw new meanings in your life brother (or sister, I dont know).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sister. It is literally at the bottom of my signature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487202#post1487202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what could the writters do, just &quot;internationalize&quot; everything. Make Assamite ninjas, Ventrue daimyos and ronin Brujah samurais.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are doing that. Have been doing that for a time, now.<br /> <br /> Yet, again, the devil is in the details and the specifics aren't that simple, but do matter.<br /> <br /> First big problem: how much should they respect the lore, how much should they retcon it? Not from the standpoint if the lore is more important than the affected people, of course it isn't, but at which point retconning it would cause more harm than good? People don't like retcons all that much, it breaks immersion, and this isn't less true for them. They may have their own solutions that will be thrown away with the retcon as it will throw away details about so many people's games. The cause of the retcon, explicit or implicit, may cause relevant reactions. The sudden change, making the culture that was a core concept become an afterthought, may offend and even reinforce prejudice more than help.<br /> <br /> It seems simple, but isn't, and their feedback is the most important factor every time it can be acquired, directly or not. You may not be able to reach to an actual person of the group, but you can do worse than read current research, articles written by natives on as many relevant subjects as possible, statistical data, etc. Nothing is perfect, but the more you seek information from sources that go beyond the basics, the more you build towards doing better than you did before.<br /> <br /> Just so you know, currently the Banu Haqim is being made far more diverse and less focused on being Middle Eastern, but they still have a history of presence (not of being the <b>only </b>presence) in the Middle East as a means to explain their lore. Alamut is the clan's ancestral fortress in the same sense that Vienna is where the Tremere main Chantry is located. There's also a whole other problem with the name where they tried to change it because the original one was a racist trope, but then the one they got came out a bit of a bad reverse translation. <i>Assamite</i> means nothing, just resembles <i>Assassin</i>, which is a bad joke (like, not a modern bad joke, a 12th century bad joke). <i>Banu Haqim</i> means &quot;Children of Haqim&quot; <u>in theory</u>, based upon a few Arabic tribal names, but it is kind of giberish. But until someone who actually speaks Arabic gives me a better option or explains why it shouldn't be used (Arabic has a very particular structure for how words change in context that I can't say for sure what's the error, just that it is there), I'll stick to <i>Banu Haqim</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487202#post1487202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">bah so much for trying not to be pedantic. Sorry for my long texts, I just simply cannot be objective</div> </div> </div> </div>I can assure you that I feel your pain...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, I've given credit where it's due</div> </div> </div> </div>Frequently that's not my impression, but then it may simply be a clash in communication styles. I do feel you also misinterpret me all too frequently, so we just talk past each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FoS- Easily one of the best written clans/sects in V20 (Violently excluding the DAV20). There's room to improve, but it's very solid on the whole.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm currently under the impression that DAV20 is kind of the overall black sheep of the V20 line. Is that correct?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giovanni-Family diversity is a great move, they could do well to go further with it. 9/10, only wish they'd just fucking join the camarilla and be a -normal- clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hecata is almost a good move, although it makes their &quot;independence&quot; even more weird.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Assamites. However, as much as it makes sense for them, as an extremely militant sect, to localize around one location, it doesn't make political sense for them to have one localization. IE they should have had more schisms and more mountains.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it that the problem was lore, avoiding a heavy retcon as much as possible. An in this sense, with a militant sect around a militant Ante, it does make some sense to focus in the place this Ante called home, specially after the whole headquarters shenanigan was rolling around for so long.<br /> <br /> Not the best thing, but I can't really say that splitting them was a feasible solution in comparison with the Schism (that made the whole &quot;mountain&quot; thing irrelevant).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I hate that writers are making too much light of how easy it would be for the schismatics to integrate into the Camarilla, which should naturally be a massive and messy political undertaking. The game is all about struggle after all. a lot of writing is just too one-sidedly positive towards the schismatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but I kind of get it.<br /> <br /> First, I feel like it is less a lack of struggle and more the game not dwelling in this struggle so the ST has more freedom to parse how they want things to be. Actually talking about it and showing how things can be different at different places would be better, but could also just be excessive text when space is at a premium.<br /> <br /> But more relevant, it would take too much of a toll on playability. There are already many clans and bloodlines that are hard to use in game because a lot of reaction from the others is already codified in the game. The worst aren't even Lasombra and Tzimisce, but actually Salubri, Ravnos and FoS. Your character is expected to be heavily persecuted by default for no reason, and that is extremely limiting for both players and STs.<br /> <br /> It would also further complicate the whole point, making the the Banu Haqim less &quot;the Arab Clan&quot;, but still making them &quot;the clan everyone expects to be Arab terrorists&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, as far as explanations go, I think it has enough for me. It is a very different context of interaction than the one where people expect them to act as murderers, in most cities it would probably be less felt like a mass migration and more like just a few members coming looking for a place to stay and accepting Camarilla law and the Prince's authority, and most of the newcomers are Viziers that always felt more at home between the Ventrue and Toreador than in Alamut, so they're the right people to ease other's anxieties.<br /> <br /> We do have struggle in the Sabbat, though, because of the <i>Antitribu</i> defection back to Alamut. In fact I think the Warriors don't make a lot of sense there since they're schismatics that should want to attack Alamut, but not the Camarilla (as they have nothing against it or their clam mates that went there). It is really strange, but as a faction within the Sabbat trying to change the sect's focus, or best as allies of opportunity that didn't actually entered the sect, they do make some sense. The Sabbat already would have the <i>Antitribu</i> Embraced within the sect with no reason to go to Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487212#post1487212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think you understand how much of a fucking monumental task it would be to give every culture/subculture their own cool bloodline and represent everyone in a way that's reasonable and fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm quite aware of that and don't think they should have done that in the first place. In fact, I think even the 7 clans are an excess and prefer the 5 more general clans of Requiem, plus Covenants to cover some trope interactions like magic.<br /> <br /> But I do disagree that making representations is always bad just because we can't represent everything. Each representation itself breaks the illusion that minorities don't exist and ease the path for other authors to make representations for other minorities. We do not have to make everything fit in this game, but that doesn't mean we can't put some different in this game.<br /> <br /> Namely, now that they're here, we absolutely can and should have good representations for the peoples and cultures already presented through the clans and bloodlines in the lore. Hinting that there are other variations in one way or another in different places and cultures not yet covered, so the list isn't exhaustive. The Banu Haqim are, again, a good example: they need to not be just the &quot;Arab Vampires&quot;, but we do need to cover what vampires are, then, in the Middle East. In the same way, we have to cover India and so on, because those are cultures the game already touched, for good or ill, and now have to own its mistakes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487256#post1487256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally always hated the bloodlines businesses to begin with. To me there would be the clans and that's it</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't happen anyway, for several reasons.<br /> <br /> After making the broad main character options, a game will naturally demand the creation of niche specialized options that cover some quirky and interesting themes. Of course as a player you can cover it up with the broad options if they're well designed and you put a little effort, but people will have ideas, will want new themes, and some simply won't have the kind of mind that takes for the effort, so making the specialized option is a great help for them.<br /> <br /> On top of that, the game needs to keep publishing books, plain and simple. It doesn't mean that every Bloodline or Discipline exists just to justify the book, at least not necessarily (some probably do), but since you'll cover a given topic in the book anyway, making up the Bloodline and/or Discipline as a way to put forward your theme and ideas is a given, even if you don't strictly need 'em. Just why not? The existence of unique Bloodlines in general, as a trope, was a given in itself, too.<br /> <br /> But I do agree that they aren't the best design for the concept. Mechanically speaking they're whole clans, and the too rigid Discipline structure and lack of other power mechanics made it almost mandatory to create new gimmicky Disciplines for many of them, simply because the authors didn't saw an alternative.<br /> <br /> Requiem did something a bit better, with Bloodlines effectively deriving from the parent clan as a simple template instead of a whole new splat, and their specific quirks usually resting in access to simpler advantages or a Devotion instead of a whole new Discipline. Yet I can't say I'm completely happy with it, just more than with Masquerade's take.<br /> <br /> Then again, though, I just got used to it. With the passing of time I learned to just accept the game as it is, and that actually improved my games. Bloodlines and Disciplines aren't bad for the game. They're far from the best mechanics it could have, but once I stopped trying to demand perfection from the setting I learned they can actually add a lot of fun with little effort, and options the players enjoy to have. All in all, I made my peace with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487258#post1487258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, anyhow... As written, the Tremere still hold the largest share of the market for Blood Magic; they are still the better connected guys in the Camarilla, aside from the Ventrue, they are well established within it and they have the organizatiom and the culture for it.<br /> <br /> Do the Assamites represent some competition? Yes, some. They do not however have the numbers nor are they firmly entrenched in the social structures of the Camarilla as the Tremere are. So yes, the Tremere now have some competition but no, nothing that could threaten their position in any measurable way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Tremere would keep at the top, I think goes without saying. It is the one point I think everyone agreed in this whole thread.<br /> <br /> But now that I think about it, here's the thing: the Sorcerers wouldn't even try to take on the Tremere's place, because that's not really their thing. <b>Their thing is to work with the other castes</b>. What the Banu Haqim Sorcerers do have as a group is the fact that they belong to the same clan as the Viziers (and eventual Warrior), so they can leverage this close relationship. It is as if every Tremere were Brother-In-Blood with a Toreador. That makes for a very distinct dynamic no other clan have, for good or ill and for both castes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T06:01:52-07:00","id":1487375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On top of that, the game needs to keep publishing books, plain and simple </div> </div> </div>And here's where we get to the root of the problem. That's my problem with comics for example. Due to the fact they have to publish a new one twice every month is exactly the reason why we go from &quot;common super heroes&quot; to having aliens, and magic, and time travel, and Cthullu-esc things and all sorts of bizarre and ridiculous things, and also how we end up for example with superman blowing black holes or dragging planets with chains or any other such ridiculous things.<br /> <br /> That also happens in WoD too, what I call &quot;high power writting fatigue&quot;, with ridiculous things such as the Ravnos ante devastation in India.<br /> <br /> Indeed, I much rather prefered the game when there wasnt even disciplines above level 5. I dont think the game improves at all by knowing that Saulot let himself be eaten to take over Tremere's body. I much prefered when the antes were just stories for putting neonates in their coffins for their day dreams. I still remember when I was a teen playing VTM, when everything was misterious, unknown, and because of that we actually feared the elders, because they didnt just have &quot;Presence 7, Fortitute 6, Dominate 6&quot;, they were more like ghost and monster stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T07:15:42-07:00","id":1487378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487323#post1487323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">first something I forgot to say earlier: you said &quot;my fathers&quot; when I think you meant &quot;my parents</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah! Im always making those stupid mistakes, total lack of attention... Sometimes I read what I've I just wrote, and it has so many mistakes that I dont even many try to fix... But thank you for pointing that out, I really need to pay more attention.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487323#post1487323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually I have to, I work with disability and autism advocacy and orientation. Don't sweat it, I didn't said that because I can't personally cope with it, but because it literally is my job to help people understand us. Thanks for the kind words, anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's an awesome job sister, congratulations. It sounds like a really interesting field that you have chosen there, and particularly in your case where you can add your own personal experience. Really incredible, congratulations. Lol sorry for being... I dont even know what Im being right now, but Im truly in genuine awe. Sorry, I dont wanna pry too much in your personal life, but it sounds like a very gratifying job, so once again, congratulations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487323#post1487323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sister. It is literally at the bottom of my signature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry dear, my apologies. I mean the She-Hulk Avatar was an indication, but I wasnt sure, so you never know. But yeah, it's literally at your signature. Allright sister <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1486212-do-you-think-the-tremere-will-ever-have-competition-in-the-camarilla?p=1487323#post1487323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resuming all the rest</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I see your point. I do not disagree on it, and I do understand what your saying. Like I said, my point is heavily biased by my worldviews. I see our overlords employing divisive tactics and really using us vs them tactics in what I can only describe as divide and conquer tactics, and it bothers me. But at the same time, I understand the struggles of different groups, and I do not seek to downplay that - but rather to show that the fight isnt you against me, as our overlords would have us believe, but rather US against THEM. Well, since Im an ancap, that's mostly self explanatory, and I dont wanna get into politics here, just trying to clarify what I mean, while I also understand where you stand.<br /> <br /> As for the lore of the WoD... It really is a mess, I cannot say that there are easy solutions, and nothing will ever satisfy both greeks and trojans. Hard retcons are indeed complicated. So it goes as always, small improvements and people going with their head cannons, unfortunately there isnt much that can be done to &quot;fix&quot; those issues. Regardless of any of the details that Im not particularly fond off, I still enjoy the game - otherwise I wouldnt be here - so like you said, we learn to accept that. And what we dont, we change in our games and it's all fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}